1791774598217661	claude-buildshapes	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1ee	{"description":"Bob read about historical longhouses: dug into the ground, long hearth fires down the middle, steep roof, raised platforms along the walls. New style next to Timber hall and Stave temple: sunken floor with drip ditch and earth banks (terrain, restorable), hearths with ridge smoke vents, side platforms, aisle posts instead of low tie beams, door near one end of a long wall.","kind":"goal","labels":["buildshapes"],"title":"Hallwright: Norse longhouse style (Bob's ask 2026-10-11)"}	blake3:MFpO_L1CrtAcexU5AroAb8F5kmHodw_kYcsRYffAJ2Q
