1791857553743975	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3in	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec section 3.12 / open decision 1. Raven post is a roost piece that flies messages and one light item stack (<= 10 kg) player-to-player and base-to-base at ~150 m per game minute, with hazards (hawks over Mountains, storms), named ravens with bynames, and a scouting mode (Hugin's cousins). Delivery (mods/Delivery) already has a horn-called food courier that brings items TO the player.\n# Options\n- Build: separate Raven post mod (Delivery stays the food courier).\n- Fold into Delivery: a second courier type in Delivery (shares flight/arrival/pin code; one mod to install).\n- Drop.\n# Considerations\nFolding reuses Delivery's courier body tricks and map-pin code (see delivery-design memory) but grows Delivery's scope. A separate mod keeps Delivery small. Jarldom wants outpost daily reports, expedition news and requests by raven either way.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Bob's answer recorded as a comment; bn-2jw updated (children created, or closed as cut).\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nUnblocks or cuts the last item in the build order.\n","kind":"task","labels":["decision","ravenpost","next-saga"],"parent":"bn-r0a","size":"xs","title":"Decide: Raven post (#79) - build it, fold it into Delivery as a second courier, or drop it?"}	blake3:a0lZZQwpbCMXun8xbPOXCq9PZyypD4k3CF4jdy9Ip48
1791857553744050	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.link	bn-2jw	{"link_type":"blocks","target":"bn-3in"}	blake3:9k4winu13PK5gCm_0AcWyLHf89qB4wikz_h3DQnbZDY
1791857553816045	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1jv	{"description":"# Context & Background\nOpen decision 2. The colony's carts (World/Carts.cs, carters on ore routes, cart trade tier) are Jarldom behaviour on the vanilla Cart, so there is no item or crafting to spin out under the spin-out rule.\n# Recommendation (spec)\nKeep in Jarldom; integrate with Horses (harness, R3) and PassengerCart (mods/PassengerCart, needs a PassengerCart.Api) through their APIs.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Bob agrees or redirects; comment recorded; the Horses harness bone adjusted if needed.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nKeeps the spin-out rule consistent.\n","kind":"task","labels":["decision","jarldom","horses","next-saga"],"parent":"bn-r0a","size":"xs","title":"Decide: carts (#57) stay Jarldom behaviour on the game's cart; integrate with Horses and PassengerCart via their APIs?"}	blake3:k9IpKJe6M7b6gJSKKxUHTKr1_HfrHWpvq7Nn3c8jtJM
1791857553888612	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-zfl	{"description":"# Context & Background\nOpen decision 3 (spec section 3.13). After the spin-out, Loom registers the Jarldom* clothing prefabs. If a player runs Jarldom WITHOUT Loom: (a) Jarldom keeps registering them itself (two code paths, temporary), or (b) Jarldom requires Loom for clothes and hides the weaver.\n# Recommendation (spec)\n(a) for one release with a deprecation note, then (b).\n# Considerations\nUnder (b), a player who updates Jarldom without installing Loom would see clothing items vanish from saves if nothing registers the prefabs - (a) avoids that loss during the transition; (b) must still be loss-safe (e.g. keep a minimal registration-only stub, or a loud warning).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Decision recorded; the Loom fallback bone updated to match.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nProtects players' saves (the \"prefab names forever\" rule).\n","kind":"task","labels":["decision","loom","jarldom","next-saga"],"parent":"bn-r0a","size":"xs","title":"Decide: Loom without Loom installed - (a) Jarldom keeps a fallback for one release, or (b) require Loom for clothes?"}	blake3:isZef68Z0Ir02YxSrkJBTBXZEwzL5LkyU-xQXwUtwUA
1791857553961805	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2mm	{"description":"# Context & Background\nOpen decision 4. J4's calendar (#27) needs a default year length; it is configurable. With 4 festivals that is one festival every 10 days. Note Bob's Creative world runs a short day (~12 s per game hour per memory notes), which makes 40 days pass quickly in testing but is not representative.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Default length agreed and recorded; J4 calendar bone updated.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFestival pacing and anniversaries (#22) depend on it.\n","kind":"task","labels":["decision","jarldom","j4","next-saga"],"parent":"bn-r0a","size":"xs","title":"Decide: colony year length - 40 in-game days (four 10-day seasons) by default: too long, too short?"}	blake3:l7fhn9IkWZ0FsQu9J7QsPV4HqkgvgdFpk5RPIIzZPD0
1791857554034510	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1bn	{"description":"# Context & Background\nOpen decision 5. Larder spoilage (raw food spoils over days; preserved never does) is a toggle; the spec proposes OFF by default because spoilage punishes existing players' stores the moment the mod is installed.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Bob agrees or picks ON; recorded; Larder L3 bone updated.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nSets the tone of the Larder mod (opt-in survival pressure).\n","kind":"task","labels":["decision","larder","next-saga"],"parent":"bn-r0a","size":"xs","title":"Decide: Larder spoilage off by default?"}	blake3:l4SVS0kPxah0X-mBfbuNOmLxo7PatSWaWRNlVtvGqzw
1791857554106627	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1xw	{"description":"# Context & Background\nGround rule: no hard dependencies; Jarldom finds each mod's `<Mod>.Api` by reflection. Today mods/Jarldom/Compat/Compat.cs does this ad hoc for Omens and Shieldwall (and reads AICompanion/BuildOrders/FeedFromChests/SkalTavern bits). ~15 more consumers are coming.\n# Goals\nA small reusable helper in Jarldom Compat (e.g. `ApiRef`): resolve a type by full name across AppDomain assemblies (cache result, retry once after all plugins load), read `int Version`, bind static methods to typed delegates once, and degrade to a no-op/default when absent or when Version < required.\n# Implementation Approach\n- Compat/ApiRef.cs: `ApiRef.Get(\"Omens.Api\", minVersion)` -> object with `Bind<TDelegate>(\"IsAurora\")`; never throws; logs once per missing method.\n- Pure parts (version comparison, name resolution order) in Core so tests/Jarldom.Tests can cover them.\n- Document the publishing side: a template `Api.cs` (public static class Api { public const int Version = N; ... }) and the rule \"bump Version when adding methods; never change signatures; host-only methods say so\".\n- Write the convention into the repo AGENTS.md or a short docs note so other agents follow it.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Helper with unit tests for version gating and missing-method behaviour.\n- [ ] Template/convention documented.\n- [ ] Jarldom with no other mods installed loads with zero errors and zero warnings spam.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nEvery integration bone (Omens aurora, Wayfinder beacon/primstav, GraveGoods rarity, Bathhouse, Byre, Hounds, Horses, Shipyard, Runecarver, Tafl, Wounds, Loom, Seasons, BountyBoard) depends on this.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","foundations","integration","next-saga"],"parent":"bn-26k","size":"m","title":"Api convention + Jarldom reflection helper (ApiRef): find <Mod>.Api by name, check Version, cache delegates","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:vRv1XcyXjHFCvOoJS3-Ak5C-rmuXYPu4VXvEdFgb6Ko
1791857554181653	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2sj	{"description":"# Context & Background\nOmens.Api (GetFate/AddFate, host-only) and Shieldwall.Api (IsSiegeAt/CallOff/StoneAt) are consumed in World/Faith.cs, World/Tribute.cs, Compat/Compat.cs. Moving them proves the helper on real calls before new integrations rely on it.\n# Implementation Approach\nReplace the ad hoc lookups with ApiRef; add `public const int Version` to Omens/Api.cs and Shieldwall/Api.cs if missing (release those mods if changed).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Fuling tribute call-off and Omens fate still work live (or via `jarldom tribute` / `omens` tool commands).\n- [ ] Released (Jarldom, plus Omens/Shieldwall if touched).\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nValidates the foundation with zero new risk.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","foundations","integration","next-saga"],"parent":"bn-26k","size":"s","title":"Move Jarldom's existing Omens and Shieldwall Api calls onto ApiRef (no behaviour change)"}	blake3:IHHsg_ZW5HY9P9vekv5rZbF4rBEGG4_ncZLIidFZ13I
1791857554259725	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2vn	{"description":"# Context & Background\nGround rule: new items keep their prefab names forever; renaming deletes them from players' saves. The Loom spin-out deliberately keeps Jarldom* names in another mod, and a dozen new mods will add items, so an accidental rename is likely over time.\n# Implementation Approach\nFor each mod that registers prefabs, keep a checked-in golden list (e.g. tests/<Mod>.Tests/prefabs.txt) and a test that the registered names (from a pure Data table, or a modcheck dump) are a superset of it. New names are appended; removals fail the test. Start with Jarldom; standalone mods copy the pattern in their first milestone.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Jarldom golden list + test in place; the pattern noted in the Api convention doc.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nProtects players' saves across the whole saga, especially the Loom move.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","foundations","next-saga","save-safety"],"parent":"bn-26k","size":"s","title":"Guard item prefab names forever: golden list test of every shipped prefab name per mod"}	blake3:aW84rfTXQI5U1skWoa_Yq36aH3t_HLUnfnqv6ObKS3Y
1791857554281480	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.link	bn-3je	{"link_type":"blocks","target":"bn-26k"}	blake3:f_je-vill0mOIWY8tlHe-baICnoPWQT12i-qVropIEc
1791857560520138	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.unlink	bn-3je	{"target":"bn-26k"}	blake3:44Xl9xRENIzz1Didj6ZHb6vKvti35wjXGPlsFH97zxE
1791857560544424	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.link	bn-2sj	{"link_type":"blocks","target":"bn-1xw"}	blake3:ibdJ2LJ02WrjzF5kMYMzH0av9J-N-7y2O5jN9DZFVic
1791857844161652	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-epg	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.5 #32. Each villager may hold 1 open request, generated from their traits, backstory, bonds and the event log. Kinds: bring a specific trophy, bring an item from a named biome, visit and mark a place, kill a named or starred creature (Omens' great stag counts), bring a relic. Requests only name things that EXIST and that you CAN REACH at your progress. Expire after 10 days without penalty. Requests also feed J3 #24 (a Dimmed soul \"asks for a deed\" chosen to be doable).\n# Goals\nA deterministic, unit-tested generator in Core that, given a villager, colony progress and a world snapshot (known biomes, defeated bosses, nearby location kinds), returns a doable request or none.\n# Reasoning/Justification\nKeeping generation pure (no Unity) lets tests prove the \"only reachable things\" rule across all progress levels - the main way requests could feel unfair. The world layer only supplies facts.\n# Implementation Approach\n- Core/Requests.cs: `Request { Kind, Target, Biome, At, Day, Reward }`, `Generate(VillagerState, Progress, WorldFacts, rng)`; weights from traits (e.g. \"brave\" -> kill, \"pious\" -> relic, backstory home biome -> biome item) and bonds/log (a fallen friend's killer species).\n- Progress = unlocked biomes (from global keys / defeated bosses), so a Meadows-stage colony never asks for Mistlands items.\n- Store the open request on VillagerState (soul ZDO, not the moving body) - bump Plugin.DataVersion.\n- Expiry: day >= Day + 10 -> silently dropped, no mood penalty.\n- Reward table: opinion, worth for the asker, sometimes their heirloom or a byname for the player (byname tally from J2 #15).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tests: for every progress stage, every generated request names an existing, reachable target (fuzz over seeds).\n- [ ] Tests: expiry at 10 days, no penalty; at most 1 open request per villager.\n- [ ] DataVersion raised for the VillagerState change.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nThe core of \"reasons to roam\": the colony sends the player into the world with personal, fair goals.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j5","p2"],"parent":"bn-1d4","size":"m","title":"#32 Requests: pure request generator (traits/backstory/bonds/log -> 1 open request, reachable-only, 10-day expiry)"}	blake3:rkFPWMYM-Ugx09bkeQnmV90zskT3Vh-mtix6HMZfb7Q
1791857844236169	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3kt	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.5 #32. Completion must be detected in the world and rewards applied once.\n# Goals\nEvery request kind can be completed in play and pays its reward exactly once.\n# Reasoning/Justification\nHand-in through the villager panel reuses the existing give flow (arm ring giving in Ui/VillagerPanel.cs); kills and visits are observed via existing hooks so no new heavy patches.\n# Implementation Approach\n- WorldFacts provider: biomes known, bosses killed (global keys), location kinds within range (ZoneSystem.m_locationInstances, as Tools.cs `find location` does).\n- Hand-in: villager panel \"Give\" with the requested item in inventory (trophy, biome item, relic).\n- Visit+mark: player within 20 m of target -> done, and a map pin is placed.\n- Kill: Character death hook (as Combat/Events do) matching prefab + stars / named creature; Omens' great stag via Omens.Api (through ApiRef; absent -> that kind is never generated).\n- Rewards: opinion (Society), worth for the asker, chance of heirloom item or player byname; a saga/log line.\n- Owner-side only (actions routed to the pillars owner via Jarldom_Act RPC).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each of the 5 kinds completed live once; reward applied once (no double pay after F6).\n- [ ] Without Omens installed, no great-stag requests and no errors.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nTurns requests into real adventures with consequences in the colony.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j5","p2","omens","integration"],"parent":"bn-1d4","size":"m","title":"#32 Requests: world side - detect completion (hand-in, biome item, visit+mark, kill named/starred incl. Omens great stag, relic) and pay rewards"}	blake3:ZohqY3WaDh2Vbl-SDjtusTx4qdHm6PXSGXVkMfn5hic
1791857844310919	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3c1	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.5 #32 + ground rule \"a ClaudeTools command for every system\".\n# Goals\nPlayers see who wants what, where, and for how long; testers can force/list/complete requests.\n# Implementation Approach\n- Ui/VillagerPanel.cs: open request line with days left and reward hint. Ui/ColonyWindow.cs: a Requests list (hall tab).\n- Optional pin for \"visit\" targets once heard.\n- Tools/Tools.cs: `jarldom request [list|make <name> [kind]|done <name>|clear]`, added to the cheats list.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Request visible in panel and colony window with days left.\n- [ ] Tool command lists, forces and completes requests.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nMakes the system legible and testable.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j5","p2"],"parent":"bn-1d4","size":"s","title":"#32 Requests: villager panel + colony window lines, map pins for targets, `jarldom request` tool command"}	blake3:L7jU3zqNX_SJ7iXvLI0Olo5kW2ZbFlyREgGNOBPo2hQ
1791857844384837	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1mx	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.5 #33. BountyBoard is Quad's mod (~/repos/valheim-mods/mods/BountyBoard: Board.cs, Bounties.cs with Bounty.Parse/State.Parse, Tracker.cs). It has no public Api class today.\n# Goals\nA stable way for Jarldom to post a contract and learn when it is finished.\n# Reasoning/Justification\nReflecting into another mod's internals is brittle; per the ground rules the clean path is a tiny `BountyBoard.Api` (Version + Post/IsDone/Complete). Since it's Quad's repo, this is an upstream PR (Bob contributes PRs upstream) - ask Bob before opening one.\n# Implementation Approach\n- Read Bounties.cs/Tracker.cs to see how bounties are created, stored and completed.\n- Draft Api: `int Version`, `string Post(string title, string text, string tag)`, `bool IsDone(string id)`, `void Complete(string id)`.\n- Propose upstream (PR to Quad) after Bob's OK; until merged, the integration stays inert.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Api design written up in a comment on this bone; Bob approves; PR opened or the plan changed.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nLets requests appear in an existing board players already use.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j5","p2","bountyboard","integration"],"parent":"bn-1d4","size":"s","title":"#33 BountyBoard: find or add a BountyBoard API (Quad's upstream mod) for posting/completing external contracts"}	blake3:vvKzbmK7EFM8sHjI6uVTL3IHOU_NDAbQmhfdw7f9m4Q
1791857844458721	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2s4	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.5 #33: with BountyBoard installed, open requests also post as contracts on its board, and finishing one completes both.\n# Implementation Approach\n- Compat: ApiRef.Get(\"BountyBoard.Api\"); on request creation Post(...) and store the contract id on the request; on request done Complete(id); poll IsDone on the owner every ~10 s for contracts finished on the board side; on expiry, remove/close the contract.\n- Absent mod -> no-op.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] With BountyBoard: a request appears on the board; completing it on either side closes both, reward paid once.\n- [ ] Without BountyBoard: no errors.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nIntegration without hard dependency.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j5","p2","bountyboard","integration"],"parent":"bn-1d4","size":"s","title":"#33 BountyBoard: open requests post as contracts; finishing either completes both"}	blake3:WfV7dh6y1yorhNVmS4OTq3iinATmBanrRS43NdUjul4
1791857844530796	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2ss	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.5 #34: in the hall, villagers tell legends pointing to real, UNVISITED locations (crypts, camps, wrecks, towers, standing stones) within 600 m of the pillars, from the game's own list of placed locations. Text is vague (\"a ship went down off the black rocks to the north\"). Hear the same legend 3 times -> map pin. Never anything beyond 600 m or in a biome you haven't unlocked.\n# Implementation Approach\n- Core/Legends.cs: map location prefab names (Crypt*, SunkenCrypt*, WoodHouse*, ShipWreck*, StoneTower*, StoneHenge*, Runestone*, etc.) to kinds; template table in Data/Tables.cs per kind; 8-way direction from pillars; distance words (\"a short walk\", \"half a day\").\n- Filter: dist <= 600, biome unlocked, not visited (visited = explored and player came within ~30 m; store by position key, not ZDOID).\n- Count hearings per legend id in ColonyRecord; at 3 -> pin. DataVersion bump.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tests: no legend beyond 600 m or in a locked biome; 3rd hearing yields a pin; text never states exact coordinates.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nTurns hall evenings into treasure hunts tied to the real world.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j5","p2","toggle"],"parent":"bn-1d4","size":"s","title":"#34 True legends (toggle): pure legend text builder - location kind -> vague line, direction/landmark words, 600 m cap, unlocked-biome filter, 3 hearings -> pin"}	blake3:VD6Vk1Xiu20lN3g7geXOHjzJQ9ie2kxoy0BG_ThjVCk
1791857844604137	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1bi	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.5 #34, world side. Pairs with J2 #19 skald's verse (hall at dusk) and J6 #51 runestone legends.\n# Implementation Approach\n- A villager in the hall with the player present tells a legend as a speech line (existing say lines, Villager/Brain.cs say) every few minutes; mark heard per colony.\n- Read ZoneSystem.instance.m_locationInstances (as World/Captives.cs FindClosestLocation does).\n- Minimap pin on 3rd hearing (reuse pin add/remove by key - existing pintest code).\n- ServerSettings.cs: `TrueLegends` (default on); `jarldom legend [list|tell|reset]` tool.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A legend leads to a real crypt (spec Accept).\n- [ ] Toggle off -> no legends told.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nExploration motivated by the colony's stories.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j5","p2","toggle"],"parent":"bn-1d4","size":"s","title":"#34 True legends (toggle): telling in the hall (skald/elders), map pin on 3rd hearing, server setting"}	blake3:uMYuxl6MEV-k3za3VdJqaU_kTgGooPanX8gqly3HQtI
1791857844678266	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3is	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.5 #35: the Food need's tier target rises with rank (Camp: Meadows food is fine ... Hold: wants Mistlands-tier dishes now and then). Needs live in Core/Rules.cs (Need.Food etc.), ranks in Core/Rules.cs Ranks.\n# Implementation Approach\n- Data/Tables.cs: food -> biome tier table (by vanilla food prefab names); Rules: `FoodTarget(rank)`; meals below target satisfy less; \"now and then\" = target met by a share of meals over a window (e.g. 1 in 4 at Hold), not every meal.\n- Ui/VillagerPanel.cs: \"Wants Plains-tier dishes (lox pie, bread...)\".\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tests: target per rank; satisfaction curve.\n- [ ] Panel names the missing tier.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nKeeps the colony pushing the player to progress, gently.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j5","p2"],"parent":"bn-1d4","size":"s","title":"#35 Expectations rise: Food need tier target rises with rank; panel says what they're missing"}	blake3:i_nVboMy9pdMSkVouqEjJl1uPTPj7dRaPvrijhxDLR4
1791857844753248	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3mc	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.5 #36: each temple's grade above B needs one relic from its own kind of place: Njord serpent scale; Thor a stone from a mountain storm (NEW drop at peaks during thunderstorms); Hel a crypt keystone (NEW drop in sunken crypts); Freyja a golden wildflower (rare Meadows find); Tyr a war trophy from a Fuling champion; Skadi a frost-cave crystal; Odin a raven feather from a Mistlands ruin. Relics can't be sold (m_value = 0).\n# Reasoning/Justification\nReuse vanilla items where they fit (SerpentScale, a starred Fuling trophy, Crystal) only if they aren't too common; otherwise new Jarldom items. New prefab names are FOREVER - choose carefully (JarldomRelicStormStone etc.) and add them to the golden list (bn-2vn).\n# Implementation Approach\n- Items.cs: new relic items cloned from suitable vanilla models, m_value = 0, description says which god.\n- Drops: Thor - spawn a pickable near the player at Mountain peaks (height threshold) during thunderstorm env; Hel - add to sunken crypt chest/drop tables (patch DropTable at location spawn, owner only); Freyja - rare pickable spawn in Meadows; Odin - in Mistlands ruins chests; Tyr - starred Fuling (GoblinBrute?) trophy marked as war trophy; Skadi - frost caves.\n- `jarldom relics [give <god>]` tool.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] All 7 relics obtainable in play (verify each source once with tools).\n- [ ] Relics show value 0 and can't be sold to traders.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nTies temple progress to exploration of specific places.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j5","p2"],"parent":"bn-1d4","size":"m","title":"#36 Relics: seven temple relic items + new drops (storm stone at peaks in thunder, crypt keystone, golden wildflower, raven feather...)"}	blake3:WrdZHVHyZLxCSXcVxaPQ523OzsYa1BC5pGQmeP5ouSk
1791857844827725	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-l0g	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.5 #36. Temples are RoomType.Temple (World/Faith.cs, Core/RoomRules.cs grades via Tables.Grade).\n# Implementation Approach\n- Altar piece interaction (the gods' altars in Colony/Pieces.cs): use a relic item -> stored on the altar (ItemStand-like or ZDO key on the altar, a still object).\n- RoomRules: temple grade = min(grade, B) unless its altar holds the god's relic; room panel explains \"Needs a crypt keystone for grade A\".\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A temple can't reach grade A without its relic (spec Accept); placing it lifts the cap.\n- [ ] Tests for the cap rule.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nGives temples a long-term goal.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j5","p2"],"parent":"bn-1d4","size":"s","title":"#36 Relics: place on the altar; temple grade capped at B without its relic"}	blake3:Xo1ZpBvhqyY1Kz2ADoBvMf3McD2h7tHYWyGEDyuvKPM
1791857844900189	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-28v	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.5 #37: per-zone use counters inside the radius (felled trees, game killed, harvests). Above a threshold, local yields drop by up to -30%, recovering over 10 days without use. Pressure, not punishment: a soft cap only. Fields (#69-71) can later supply real soil numbers.\n# Implementation Approach\n- Core/Worn.cs: counters per 64 m zone (ZoneSystem zone coords) with decay; `YieldMult(count) in [0.7, 1]`; linear recovery to full over 10 days of no use.\n- Stored compactly in ColonyRecord (only touched zones; DataVersion bump) - keep it small (record is ~5 KB).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tests: never below 0.7; full recovery after 10 idle days; threshold behaviour.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nEncourages outposts and expeditions instead of stripping one area.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j5","p2"],"parent":"bn-1d4","size":"s","title":"#37 The land wears thin: pure per-zone use counters, yield multiplier down to -30%, 10-day recovery"}	blake3:GCni1pKcr1_Iw2vJGtDvetWkhLG3WlSXihVdLzjZyEQ
1791857844974053	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-4vq	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.5 #37 world side.\n# Implementation Approach\n- Count: villager work (Villager/Work.cs woodcutting/hunting/farming) and player actions inside the radius (TreeBase/TreeLog destroy, Character death of prey, Pickable/plant harvest).\n- Apply multiplier to drops for villager gathering (and player drops inside the radius, owner side).\n- Colony map overlay: tinted zones by wear (Ui/ColonyWindow.cs map tab / minimap overlay like the hammer overlay).\n- `jarldom worn [show|set <n>|clear]`.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Heavy felling in one zone visibly lowers yields there; 10 idle days restore them.\n- [ ] Overlay shows worked land.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nSoft pressure that makes the map matter.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j5","p2"],"parent":"bn-1d4","size":"m","title":"#37 The land wears thin: hook tree felling, hunting, harvests; apply local yield multiplier; 'worked land' map overlay"}	blake3:GLPcrYjZf75oW8w0IRqKFDvCD_Uqj0R0LIwK1ejchjo
1791857845047979	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3c9	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.5 #38: a fourth part of renown, Saga. Deeds for each first: biome entered, dungeon type cleared, landmark found, furthest distance from the pillars (in steps), circling an island. Per colony, from all its players. Renown today = WealthPart + ComfortPart + Deeds (Colony/Colony.cs:43; Core/Rules.cs Renown).\n# Implementation Approach\n- Core/Rules.cs Renown.Saga(firsts): points per first-of-kind; distance in 100 m steps (diminishing).\n- ColonyRecord: set of first keys (biome:Swamp, dungeon:SunkenCrypt, landmark:<pos key>, island:<id>), max distance. DataVersion bump.\n- Renown = Wealth + Comfort + Deeds + Saga; rebalance rank thresholds if needed (tests).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tests: each first counts once per colony; Saga included in renown.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nRewards exploration directly in the colony's standing.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j5","p2"],"parent":"bn-1d4","size":"s","title":"#38 Odin the Wanderer: Saga renown part - pure scoring of firsts (biome, dungeon type, landmark, furthest steps, island circled)"}	blake3:qmP2lCSxJI6XDPS1Nxp47hAmkur82TuydyrBbF_qLoM
1791857845122881	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3mh	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.5 #38, world side. Any player belonging to the colony (owner/co-jarls) counts.\n# Implementation Approach\n- Per-player periodic check (every few s, local) -> send firsts to the pillars owner via Jarldom_Act RPC: biome under player; dungeon cleared = boss/all enemies dead in a dungeon instance or exiting after visiting the deepest room (pick a simple, documented rule); landmark = within 30 m of a named location; furthest distance from pillars; island circled = cumulative heading around an island's centre while on a ship (reuse J6 island detection if present; else coastline angle sweep >= 330 deg).\n- Ui/ColonyWindow.cs + JarlView: renown breakdown shows Saga.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Renown shows a Saga part that rises when you enter a new biome (spec Accept).\n- [ ] Dungeon and island firsts verified once live.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nMakes the player's journeys part of the colony's renown.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j5","p2"],"parent":"bn-1d4","size":"m","title":"#38 Odin the Wanderer: detect firsts in the world (biome entered, dungeon cleared, landmark, distance, island circled) + renown UI"}	blake3:PrVrK_vbH9s74JIqrEWaT4dOVN_x1ihwJJNshvqA_FM
1791857845196323	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-14a	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.5 #39 (P3).\n# Implementation Approach\n- Piece: clone of the vanilla map table (piece_cartographytable) as JarldomMapTable (name forever).\n- Interact -> opens the minimap large view with temporary pins/overlay layer from colony data: ore claims (World/Claims.cs), outposts (World/Outposts.cs), cart/trade routes, pinned legends (#34), open request targets (#32), recent danger (raids/deaths from the log). Remove the temporary pins on close (pin by key; don't touch player pins).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Table shows each layer; closing leaves player pins untouched.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nOne place to see the colony's reach.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j5","p3"],"parent":"bn-1d4","size":"m","title":"#39 Colony map table (P3): hall map table piece with a colony layer (claims, outposts, routes, legends, request targets, danger)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:MzOuX736DKKGE64NJ1EUfnCkIOiGzr3sAmYp4ex0Soc
1791857845270421	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-i6b	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.5 #40 (P3).\n# Implementation Approach\n- Sample the explored map texture (Minimap explored array) over the 500 m disc around the pillars on the owner, once per in-game day; share fraction (from any colony player) in the record.\n- Moodlet \"Restless\" (Data/Tables.cs moodlets) for villagers with a curious trait while < 70%; clears when >= 70%.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tests for the threshold; live: exploring past 70% clears the moodlet.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nSmall nudge to explore near home.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j5","p3"],"parent":"bn-1d4","size":"s","title":"#40 Edge of the map (P3): Restless moodlet for curious traits while < 70% of 500 m around the pillars is explored","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:K6VoiGXrNW9nEzdHq0vqCPxl2dyjy0kpCKpinRP6K04
1791857845346752	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1ni	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.5 Accept lines. Test in Bob's Creative world with ClaudeTools (see claudetools-live-game / test-tools-blast-radius memories: box-filter tools, check `siege status` and `jarldom tribute` before time jumps).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] With 6 villagers, at least 4 kinds of request appear over 5 days, all doable.\n- [ ] A legend leads to a real crypt.\n- [ ] A temple can't reach grade A without its relic.\n- [ ] Renown shows a Saga part that rises when you enter a new biome.\n- [ ] README playtest checklist updated; version bump, CHANGELOG, dist + manifest (release every change).\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nCloses J5.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j5","p2","live-test"],"parent":"bn-1d4","size":"s","title":"J5 live acceptance test in Creative + release"}	blake3:ROWpaK-n00kn037SvMsz5d16Pndd99S6j4LQHlrn4uc
1791857845422957	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2yt	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.6 #53 (P1 within J6). Builds on follow-the-jarl (Villager/Follow.cs: Follow.Start/End, FollowTask, FollowThroughPortals, away mode when the colony is unloaded). Existing bone bn-2tu (live-test follow: portals, ships, deaths far away, multiplayer) must be done first so the base is solid.\n# Goals\nChoose a named crew with roles and take them along as one group.\n# Implementation Approach\n- Ui/ColonyWindow.cs: Expedition tab - pick 2-6 villagers, assign roles; validation (one navigator for ship trips, etc.).\n- Expedition record (crew vids, roles, leader player, start day) in ColonyRecord - small; DataVersion bump.\n- Start = Follow.Start for each; by ship: crew board and sit on the player's ship (ships part of bn-2tu).\n- Each crew member carries supplies from stockpiles by role (OutfitTask pattern in Villager/Outfit.cs): cook food, carrier camp kit (wood, stone, a chest's worth), guards gear.\n- `jarldom expedition [start <names> | roles | end]`.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A 4-person crew with roles follows across land and by karve.\n- [ ] Ending the expedition sends them home.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nThe P1 heart of J6: taking the colony with you.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j6","p1"],"parent":"bn-bvx","size":"m","title":"#53 Expeditions: pick a crew (2-6) with roles (navigator, cook, guards, scout, carrier) from the colony window; they follow by land or ship","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:Ee7oA7WlQZQ0KRFIds9pCUgODjbC4FKDEAS-cHg-qtU
1791857845500128	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-p3m	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.6 #53: press a key to make camp; they set up a bedroll camp (fire, chest, workbench from the supplies they carry).\n# Implementation Approach\n- Keybind (BepInEx config, default unbound conflicts checked) -> RPC to owner.\n- Place real vanilla pieces (fire_pit, piece_chest_wood, piece_workbench, bedrolls) at a flat spot near the player via the builder pattern (BuildOrders ghosts or direct placement as the builder does), PAYING from carried supplies (no free pieces; pay in full before placing - pitfall).\n- Camp is a lightweight \"camp\" record (position, pieces) - can later upgrade to outpost.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Make camp places fire, chest, workbench, bedrolls; materials leave crew bags.\n- [ ] Without supplies: a clear message, nothing placed.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nField bases without player micromanagement.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j6","p1"],"parent":"bn-bvx","size":"m","title":"#53 Expeditions: 'make camp' key - crew builds a bedroll camp (fire, chest, workbench) from carried supplies","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:VaLdeAj1Kpxl7xrez7Pi_323cvx4z-Mf1uUpBSrPGTg
1791857845578721	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-32k	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.6 #53. Existing tasks to reuse: ScoutTask (map reveal RPC), cooking, guard behaviour (Villager/Combat.cs), gatherers (Villager/Work.cs).\n# Implementation Approach\n- While camped: role -> task selector scoped to the camp radius (~40 m) instead of the colony radius; carriers deposit in the camp chest; cook feeds crew and player (food to player like a hall meal); guards patrol and fight.\n- Villagers outside the colony are far from the colony's loaded area: handle owner/freeze issue (engine freezes chasers with owner 0 outside the player's active area - keep them near the player).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each role visibly works at camp; scout reveals map strips; guards engage hostiles.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nMakes the crew useful, not just escorts.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j6","p1"],"parent":"bn-bvx","size":"m","title":"#53 Expeditions: camp work by role - cook feeds, scout reveals map, guards keep watch, carriers gather","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:2DUW8XcWWqUN8RzTnXsz0xXL_zpqY7jHy2ZWp6waEIU
1791857845655021	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-37e	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.6 #53. World/Outposts.cs (Announce/Link/Candidates/Credit) founds outposts linked to a parent colony; live-tested (Ravnsholt 515 m south).\n# Implementation Approach\n- Colony window/camp interaction \"Make this an outpost\" enabled when distance from parent pillars >= 300 m; raise pillars at camp (cost per existing founding), Outposts.Link; crew members may stay as its first villagers.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Upgrade works at >= 300 m and is refused closer, with the reason shown.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nExpeditions become colonisation.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j6","p1"],"parent":"bn-bvx","size":"s","title":"#53 Expeditions: upgrade camp to outpost on the spot when >= 300 m away (existing outpost code)","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:4QK5g4zbetIDW-CqE6SRnqyB5_oTB9bM-z8_ej1URTE
1791857845733671	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-32w	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.6 #52: sometimes (~1 in 5 arrivals, rank >= Hamlet) a soul is set down in the wilds: Hugin says so, smoke rises at a real location 400-1500 m away in a biome you've unlocked, with a pin once seen. The soul holds out (in a ruin, on an island, up a tree) for 3 days. Reach them -> they follow you home: arrival skill +15 and an \"Owes their life\" bond with you. Missed -> the Valkyrie collects them, no penalty.\n# Implementation Approach\n- Core: ScatterChance(rank), site choice from candidate locations (filter distance 400-1500, biome unlocked), expiry 3 days; tests.\n- Record: pending scattered soul (vid, pos, day) in ColonyRecord; DataVersion bump.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tests for chance gating, distance and biome filters, expiry.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nTurns arrivals into rescue missions.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j6","p2"],"parent":"bn-bvx","size":"s","title":"#52 The scattered reborn: pure rules - 1 in 5 arrivals at rank >= Hamlet, site 400-1500 m in an unlocked biome, 3-day hold-out"}	blake3:8zKItdpVeOdxJLJhmHoJCAPKVittDCA8qabiNXcuZGk
1791857845814780	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1wt	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.6 #52 world side. Migration and the Valkyrie fly-in live in World/Migration.cs.\n# Implementation Approach\n- Migration: on a scattered roll, spawn the soul at the site (only when the zone is loaded, ZNetScene.IsAreaReady); otherwise keep it abstract until a player is near.\n- Smoke: vanilla smoke vfx column at the site visible from far; pin added when a player sees it (distance/line check).\n- Soul idles defensively (ruin/tree/island spot); on player within 10 m -> Follow.Start; arriving home -> arrival skill +15, bond \"Owes their life\" with that player (Society).\n- After 3 days unrescued: Valkyrie collect (reuse fly-in), log line, no penalty.\n- `jarldom scatter [now|where|expire]`.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Rescue a scattered soul (spec Accept); bond and skill bonus applied.\n- [ ] Missed soul collected by the Valkyrie with no penalty.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nStory-rich arrivals.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j6","p2"],"parent":"bn-bvx","size":"m","title":"#52 The scattered reborn: world - Hugin message, smoke column, pin when seen, soul holds out, rescue -> follow home + bond; missed -> Valkyrie"}	blake3:n-Cs98zP6L-JnDTnmqvf913wUi8qfKCjFo0EtoOJpVY
1791857845896199	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1ig	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.6 #46: a new profession that builds the colony's boats from stockpiles at a marked boatyard zone (the game's raft, karve and longship through BuildOrders ghosts). The builder already raises BuildOrders blueprints (emergency_hut live-tested).\n# Implementation Approach\n- Profession \"Shipwright\" (Data/Tables.cs professions), zone \"Boatyard\" (Ui/Designate.cs zones) at the shore.\n- Colony window: order a ship type; place a ghost via BuildOrders at the boatyard; shipwright hauls materials from stockpiles and builds (pay in full before the ship spawns - pitfall).\n- Ships spawned in water/at the slip edge; one order at a time.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The shipwright builds a karve from stockpiles (spec Accept).\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nShips for trade tiers, islands and expeditions without player grinding.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j6","p2"],"parent":"bn-bvx","size":"m","title":"#46 Shipwright: profession + boatyard zone; builds raft/karve/longship from stockpiles via BuildOrders ghosts"}	blake3:PXhKchhRig4tczudf8BFjGDGCP7AapslshZu7kM-Tp8
1791857845978391	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-bhs	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.6 #46: repairs moored ships.\n# Implementation Approach\n- Find WearNTear ships within the colony shore radius below full health; shipwright walks to the shore opposite (Trade.Shore pattern) and repairs over time using wood from stockpiles.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A damaged moored karve returns to full health; wood consumed.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nUpkeep for the colony fleet.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j6","p2"],"parent":"bn-bvx","size":"s","title":"#46 Shipwright: repair moored ships near the boatyard/dock"}	blake3:m9BAAPI5njdU8X9mq7-Oeuxu-0jcM-jBXIoy7Gt9X94
1791857846058859	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-ypr	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.6 #46 and 3.8: with the Shipyard mod, the shipwright works its staged builds (keel -> ribs -> strakes -> deck -> mast, each stage paid in full) and can build the knarr. Needs Shipyard.Api (Shipyard N3 milestone, other bone).\n# Implementation Approach\n- ApiRef.Get(\"Shipyard.Api\"): find slipways in the boatyard, query next stage cost, pay stage from stockpiles, advance stage.\n- Absent -> vanilla path.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] With Shipyard, the shipwright completes a knarr stage by stage; without, nothing breaks.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nKnarrs run island supply and ore by sea.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j6","p2","shipyard","integration"],"parent":"bn-bvx","size":"s","title":"#46 Shipwright x Shipyard: use Shipyard's staged slipway builds and the knarr when the Shipyard mod is installed"}	blake3:AplLz8u7NXEg42g9sX1ydOHNty4CNR5g1diBGB-ngCg
1791857846134699	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3k4	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.6 #45: outposts on islands (no land link to the main colony).\n# Implementation Approach\n- On outpost link: sample a coarse land/water grid along candidate routes (heightmap vs water level) or flood-fill land cells between the two pillars at 16 m resolution, bounded box; cache result on the outpost link key.\n- Pure flood-fill in Core with tests.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tests on synthetic grids; live: the island outpost reports \"island\", Ravnsholt (land) does not.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nBasis for island rules and Saga island firsts.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j6","p2"],"parent":"bn-bvx","size":"s","title":"#45 Island jarldoms: detect island outposts (no land path to the main colony) - pure + world check"}	blake3:RYxhLd0-ZYS5bOLdhlHGuWVcSLvZSJdTDPDnJQo2N0U
1791857846215983	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3qf	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.6 #45. Carters move ore (World/Carts.cs), trade tiers by vehicle in Core/Rules.cs Trading (foot/cart/karve/longship).\n# Implementation Approach\n- Raid strength x0.5 at island outposts (raid scaling hook).\n- Supply/ore routes to islands require a ship-tier run (karve or better, knarr via Shipyard); no cart/foot routes. Trip abstract like traders.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Island outpost raids halved; ore arrives only by ship runs; UI explains why a cart route is unavailable.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nGives the sea a real logistic role (\"no ore through portals\").\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j6","p2"],"parent":"bn-bvx","size":"m","title":"#45 Island jarldoms: raids -50%, supplied by ship trade runs, ore moves by ship only"}	blake3:0CmsFYz6DBULCqWyak8f9Sr6-_UX_CNPlW8bP-ZP19w
1791857846298745	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-246	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.6 #44: more milk, wool and hides; needs a guard. Uses Byre's animals (other bone); otherwise boars. Summer half of the colony year needs J4's calendar (#27); before J4, use a fixed 20-of-40-day window.\n# Implementation Approach\n- Outpost type flag \"shieling\" (World/Outposts.cs) valid in Mountains or Meadows >= 300 m from the pillars.\n- Herder (existing Herder + Pasture zone) moves assigned tame animals there at summer start and back at end; yields bonus while there; without a guard posted, wolves/raids can take animals.\n- Without Byre: tame boars, yields = extra leather/meat.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A shieling is founded; herd moves up and back with the season; bonus yields; guard requirement shown.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nAuthentic transhumance; uses the mountains.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j6","p2"],"parent":"bn-bvx","size":"m","title":"#44 Shielings: shieling outpost type (Mountains or remote Meadows, >= 300 m); herders take animals up for the summer half-year"}	blake3:49CQ6xHHesuGO26fJsFU2C1WqA27fnfFneqeeMH7uRQ
1791857846375114	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-28u	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.6 #44 / 3.2. Needs Byre.Api (Byre S3, other bone).\n# Implementation Approach\n- ApiRef.Get(\"Byre.Api\"): list animals and kinds, produce milk/wool at the shieling; fallback to boars when absent.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] With Byre, shieling yields milk and wool; without, boar path only.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nIntegration without dependency.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j6","p2","byre","integration"],"parent":"bn-bvx","size":"s","title":"#44 Shielings x Byre: use Byre sheep/goats/cattle (milk, wool, hides) via Byre.Api when installed"}	blake3:TZfA1i-THzDaRQJiVjSb3eWx8lvwx9wovomogxVoxOw
1791857846454948	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-225	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.6 #47: the Thing proposes one at a time (rank >= Village), from a catalogue tied to real terrain: Lighthouse (coastal headland; ships home at night always find the beacon, +trade), Great bridge (over a river gorge, for carts and roads), Peak temple (highest peak within 1.5 km; doubles that god's blessing), Mistlands hall (fortified foothold; Dvergr relations +), Sea wall (harbour; island and ship bonuses).\n# Implementation Approach\n- Core/GreatWorks.cs: catalogue (id, bonus, blueprint name), site scoring over sampled heights/water (pure functions on a height grid; tests).\n- World: sample terrain (heightmap) around the colony; colony scouts \"suggest\" sites (top 1-3 candidates with pins).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tests for each site finder on synthetic grids; live: candidate sites look right on Bob's map.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nLong-term colony projects that reshape the landscape.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j6","p2"],"parent":"bn-bvx","size":"m","title":"#47 Great Works: pure catalogue + terrain site finders (headland, river gorge, highest peak within 1.5 km, Mistlands foothold, harbour)"}	blake3:6jMVVHSU8iVtKcnCWxXYqAo96z3CxboHIWl-7qBHUn8
1791857846534283	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2pn	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.6 #47. The Thing is an event (Ui/ThingPanel.cs, petitions in ColonyRecord.Petitions). Builders already raise BuildOrders blueprints; carters do supply trips.\n# Implementation Approach\n- Petition \"Great Work: Lighthouse at <place>\" when rank >= Village and none active.\n- Blueprints: author 5 BuildOrders/Hallwright blueprints (mods/BuildShapes is Hallwright) shipped with Jarldom.\n- Builders sent to the site; supply runs from stockpiles (abstract like carters) feed the blueprint; pay in full per piece.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A proposed Great Work is accepted at the Thing and builders complete it from supplies.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nCollective goals that use the whole colony.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j6","p2"],"parent":"bn-bvx","size":"m","title":"#47 Great Works: Thing proposal (rank >= Village, one at a time), Hallwright/BuildOrders blueprint at the chosen site, builders + supply runs"}	blake3:BE7T6NfRg6sHk6pvYymk1sdcsipzMc-kuEcxR1raFjE
1791857846609096	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-6di	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.6 #47. Lighthouse effect relies on J2 #13 beacon (other bone): ships home at night always find the beacon. Peak temple doubles a god's blessing (World/Faith.cs Blessed). Sea wall: island/ship bonuses (#45).\n# Implementation Approach\n- Completion detection (blueprint 100%); record in ColonyRecord; apply bonus hooks; saga line; persistent map pin with the work's name.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Complete one Great Work and see its bonus applied (spec Accept).\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nLasting rewards and landmarks.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j6","p2"],"parent":"bn-bvx","size":"s","title":"#47 Great Works: completion - permanent bonus, saga entry, named map landmark (Lighthouse ties to the J2 beacon)"}	blake3:snKD_kOdASefh2eoIGrMdoVfRCnAz4wTrkGgWcia1bY
1791857846687501	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-357	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.6 #51: reading one of the game's lore runestones teaches it to the colony; the skald retells it at night as the colony's OWN tale (in-world framing, no new canon). Collected in the chronicle (Core/Stories.cs chronicle).\n# Implementation Approach\n- Patch RuneStone.Interact (postfix) for a colony player -> RPC to owner with the text key; record learned keys (small).\n- Skald evening slot (shared with J2 #19 verse and #34 legends) retells with a framing line (\"As our grandmothers told it...\").\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Read a runestone; that night the skald retells it; it appears in the chronicle.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nWeaves the world's lore into the colony's culture.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j6","p2"],"parent":"bn-bvx","size":"s","title":"#51 Legends from runestones: reading a lore runestone teaches the colony; the skald retells it as the colony's own tale"}	blake3:zRR9I1FlcTYx2VtTK-jAe22unOlxudGwtRrFU4P5XRA
1791857846763022	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-285	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.6 #54: help a Dvergr outpost (kill what attacks it, bring what it asks for) to raise its standing. Jarldom already hires Dvergr mercenaries (Faith/Tribute area).\n# Implementation Approach\n- Track Dvergr outposts (Mistlands locations with Dverger) by position key; standing in ColonyRecord.\n- Help events: kill hostiles within 30 m of the outpost while Dvergr are present; \"asks\" = a simple wanted item shown on hover/interaction near the outpost.\n- Tiers: wary / neutral / friendly.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Standing rises by defending and by delivering asks; shown in the colony window.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nA diplomatic thread for the late game.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j6","p2"],"parent":"bn-bvx","size":"m","title":"#54 Dvergr trade relations: standing per Dvergr outpost, raised by defending it and fulfilling its asks"}	blake3:i1PfZgFqDLy3M4SGENq8KkDvGMeuwWgcVZ0IZeua9Rs
1791857846842149	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-4k4	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.6 #54. Trade runs exist (Core/Rules.cs Trading; World trade code).\n# Implementation Approach\n- New trade destination \"Dvergr <outpost>\" unlocked at friendly; sells Mistlands goods (from a table), buys colony crafts.\n- README: keep details spoiler-light (Bob's rule).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A trade run to a friendly Dvergr outpost returns Mistlands goods.\n- [ ] README section is spoiler-light.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nLate-game economy link.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j6","p2"],"parent":"bn-bvx","size":"s","title":"#54 Dvergr trade relations: at 'friendly', traders trade with them (buy Mistlands goods, sell crafts); spoiler-light README"}	blake3:HcwXji6j99P6P3LD44DMh0i2o1db6FL4b5TJUAbMujw
1791857846921754	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2ph	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.6 #48-49 (P3, toggle; only after everything else in J6). Plot a course with Wayfinder (mods/Wayfinder) + plant a waystone: builders pave toward it in 8 m stretches using stone from stockpiles, carving a milestone every 100 m. Jarldom has some road code already (Villager/Upkeep.cs, Mover.cs) - extend it.\n# Implementation Approach\n- Wayfinder.Api: read plotted course points (add to Wayfinder's Api if missing; release Wayfinder).\n- Waystone piece (JarldomWaystone, name forever).\n- Builder task paves next 8 m segment (paved_road_v2 terrain op via TerrainComp like `siege mend`), costs stone; milestone piece every 100 m (rune text via Runecarver when present, other bone).\n- ServerSettings toggle.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A road grows toward the waystone over days, stone consumed, milestones every 100 m; toggle off stops it.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nVisible infrastructure linking colony and outposts.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j6","p3","toggle","wayfinder","integration"],"parent":"bn-bvx","size":"m","title":"#48 Roads that grow (P3, toggle): waystone + Wayfinder plotted course; builders pave 8 m stretches from stockpile stone","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:oqHMk4UQoKCsuZKkflB33H4Ovi8WBexsLiwsIhyt9Fs
1791857847001193	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2or	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.6 #48-49: escorts lower the ambush chance on crews outside the radius (road crews, carters).\n# Implementation Approach\n- Ambush roll for crews working outside the radius (Core rule, tests); assigning a guard as escort reduces it; on ambush spawn a small hostile group (biome-appropriate) near the crew.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tests: escort lowers chance; live: an unescorted crew can be ambushed.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nRisk/reward on extending the road network.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j6","p3","toggle"],"parent":"bn-bvx","size":"s","title":"#49 Roads that grow (P3): escorts lower the ambush chance on crews outside the radius","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:P5dmomdYa9i24DDVCzEvVzdpx0oz0bYKemvpPQPnyn4
1791857847079753	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-bfy	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.6 #50 (optional: only if outpost founding accepts an existing structure easily).\n# Implementation Approach\n- Investigate first: can room measuring (Core/RoomRules.cs, Colony/RoomFind.cs) count non-player-built location pieces? If it needs deep changes, close as cut.\n- Else: an outpost founded inside a ruin location treats its standing walls as built.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Investigation result commented; built only if cheap.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nOptional flavour for outposts.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j6","optional"],"parent":"bn-bvx","size":"s","title":"#50 Reclaim ruins (optional): mark a ruined village/tower as an outpost site; standing walls count as built","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:e3Gg838AQWIDhgRGfr-50U30Xf9d73Xub0KfnsH8lT0
1791857847157031	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1ml	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.6 Accept lines. Creative world; ships lie ~25 m out at ~(383-395, 1129); follow test-tools-blast-radius rules.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Lead a 4-person expedition by karve to a new island, make camp, upgrade it to an outpost.\n- [ ] Rescue a scattered soul.\n- [ ] Have the shipwright build a karve from stockpiles.\n- [ ] Complete one Great Work and see its bonus applied.\n- [ ] README playtest checklist; version bump, CHANGELOG, dist + manifest.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nCloses J6.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j6","p2","live-test"],"parent":"bn-bvx","size":"s","title":"J6 live acceptance test in Creative + release"}	blake3:bRTtquemeH5Dabfu2OhtGRSd4aALBfnoAaa-4fpxatE
1791857847233836	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2mt	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.7 (#41-42). Time-boxed 2-day trial with a go/no-go; Bob is unsure about complexity.\n# Goals\nThe smallest playable version, off by default (ServerSettings `LandSpirits`).\n# Implementation Approach\n- Regions: 64 m zones grouped into 512 m cells (pure arithmetic in Core; nothing saved until a cell is claimed).\n- Spirit stone: one per cell at an existing game location in the cell (standing stone, runestone, landmark) chosen by world seed - no new worldgen. Hover text marks it.\n- Win it over: one task chosen by biome - offering (a biome food placed/used on it), clear threats (kill N hostiles within 60 m), or vigil (stand there through one night).\n- Effects when claimed (only two): villagers may work and claim ore there (World/Claims.cs), raids that start in a claimed cell are -25%.\n- Claimed cells stored as global keys (like jarldom_claim_<id>); `jarldom spirits [list|claim|reset]`.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Off by default; with it on, a stone can be found, won over by each task kind, and both effects apply.\n- [ ] Tests for region arithmetic and seeded stone choice.\n- [ ] Timebox respected (2 days); if over, stop and report.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nTests whether territory with personality is worth a full system.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j7","trial"],"parent":"bn-1fn","size":"m","title":"J7 trial build (2 days, behind a setting): 512 m regions, spirit stones at existing locations, 3 win tasks, 2 effects","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:xjL_QnDWOaLVlaOrLMs5p0V5RY9JGplCdKyJdAVcNxE
1791857847312166	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-vs4	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.7: Go if claiming feels like a small adventure and changes where you send people. No-go: cut #42-43 and keep the spirit stones only as a legend source for #34 (true legends).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Bob's verdict commented.\n- [ ] Go: follow-up bones created (polish, #43 unblocked). No-go: trial code reduced to stones-as-legend-sources (or removed), #43 closed as cut.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nAvoids building an expensive system nobody wants.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j7","trial","decision"],"parent":"bn-1fn","size":"xs","title":"J7 trial: Bob playtests land spirits -> go / no-go decision recorded","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:zNp4Z0nLgY_spQR3Kdfuw83izaAJ18AttK7YDXZYVPc
1791857847386691	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1gh	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.7 #43 (the Norse custom of lowering the dragon prow near home shores so as not to frighten land spirits).\n# Implementation Approach\n- Per player ship: Ship sail state (m_speed / sail up) and distance to claimed stone's nearest shore; once per approach -> small spirit favour loss and a one-line hint \"Lower the prow near the land-wights' shore\".\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Sail up near a claimed shore costs favour once with a hint; furled sail costs nothing.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nLore flavour, only if the trial is a go.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j7","trial"],"parent":"bn-1fn","size":"s","title":"#43 Dragon prow (only if J7 goes ahead): sail up within 100 m of a claimed stone's shore -> small favour loss + one-line hint; furl = lowered prow","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:ZMvy_Jtl7S6ToSly-GfnddvdmDw1aOSQcLfHznwatwM
1791857847462635	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1yn	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.8 #82 needs `GraveGoods.Api.Rarity(ItemData)`. GraveGoods (mods/GraveGoods) has rarities incl. Heirloom and Saga; no Api class yet.\n# Implementation Approach\n- mods/GraveGoods/Api.cs: `public static class Api { public const int Version = 1; public static string Rarity(ItemDrop.ItemData item) }` returning \"\" for plain items. Follow the Api convention (bn-1xw doc).\n- Release GraveGoods (version, changelog, dist).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Api returns correct rarity for generated items; tests if rarity read is pure.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nEnables #82 without a hard dependency.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j8","p2","gravegoods","integration"],"parent":"bn-1gf","size":"xs","title":"#82 GraveGoods: add GraveGoods.Api.Rarity(ItemData) (+ Version) upstream in mods/GraveGoods and release it"}	blake3:GUy8hI9ltxBMdGdGIncsFvoBe6B2WyhnhvAbLeEIKJ8
1791857847544124	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-25x	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.8 #82. Ascension deeds: Core/Rules.cs AscensionDeeds(graveGoodsValue, sworn); pyre in Colony/Behaviours.cs; verse is J2 #19 (other bone).\n# Implementation Approach\n- Carried into the colony (player inventory check when entering radius, throttled) -> a villager line + \"Marvel\" moodlet once per item.\n- Grave goods value: Heirloom x3, Saga x10 deeds contribution; the verse/saga line names the item.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] With GraveGoods: line + moodlet; ascension with a Saga item gives x10; verse names it. Without: no errors.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nConnects loot to the colony's story.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j8","p2","gravegoods","integration"],"parent":"bn-1gf","size":"s","title":"#82 GraveGoods x Jarldom: villagers recognize Heirloom/Saga items (line + moodlet); as grave goods Heirloom x3, Saga x10 deeds; verse names the item"}	blake3:4xNqmMP9DMTD5NcPr3hK2l24gPdf2xK5AST5BDWWDds
1791857847624560	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-qs7	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.8 #83 references \"your Arena run\", but there is NO Arena mod in ~/src/valheim-mods/mods or ~/repos/valheim-mods/mods (checked 2026-10-12). It may be planned, a third-party mod, or a different name (Golf? Shieldwall?).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Ask Bob which mod/where; record the answer; adjust the #83 implementation bone (or cut it).\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nAvoids building against a mod that doesn't exist.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j8","p2","arena","integration","decision"],"parent":"bn-1gf","size":"xs","title":"#83 Arena: confirm which mod 'Arena' is (none in mods/ or ~/repos/valheim-mods) and how to detect a player's Arena run"}	blake3:uMYiwsCuA8B9cnIgbUyTpR2WUztDaNOWRR70CGPV-9s
1791857847703582	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3on	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.8 #83: during your Arena run, off-duty villagers (up to 6) stand in the stands; each may bet up to 10% of their hoard on you; wins and losses move coins and mood. Champions get a byname (J2 #15 tally).\n# Implementation Approach\n- Needs an Arena.Api (run started/ended/result, stand positions) - add upstream once the mod is identified.\n- Villagers walk/teleport (if far) to stands; bets from their hoard (Gear/coins); settle on result; moodlets.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Villagers watch, bet, and settle; champion byname awarded; without Arena, nothing happens.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nSocial spectacle tying villagers to the player's feats.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j8","p2","arena","integration"],"parent":"bn-1gf","size":"m","title":"#83 Arena x Jarldom: up to 6 off-duty villagers in the stands, bets up to 10% of hoard, coins+mood move, champion byname"}	blake3:5glFnmMSINOb-GoeJCed1vfpgIdvJMR3GV88NWYDJrY
1791857847781910	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1zx	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.8 #84. mods/Shieldwall/Api.cs has IsSiegeAt, CallOff, StoneAt. Need: list stave tower posts near a point, and a way to add a ward-strength bonus source (+10%) at the Warstone.\n# Implementation Approach\n- Api: `IList<Vector3> TowerPosts(Vector3 at, float radius)`, `void SetWardBonus(string source, float mult, float seconds)`; bump Version; release Shieldwall.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Api methods work in a siege (tool-checked); old callers unaffected.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nEnables guard/gothi roles in sieges.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j8","p2","shieldwall","integration"],"parent":"bn-1gf","size":"s","title":"#84 Shieldwall: Shieldwall.Api additions (stave tower positions, Warstone ward strength modifier) + release Shieldwall"}	blake3:fRaw37jaTXDLrIiH9dTYXh_E3wzB_lyMyN_G-F8aByQ
1791857847862786	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-fdi	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.8 #84. Raid shelter during a Shieldwall siege already works; the gothi exists (World/Faith.cs GothiTask). Note: Bob's Shieldwall staves kill draugr near the Warstone (303,1149) - test away from it when testing draugr; check `siege status` before time jumps.\n# Implementation Approach\n- During IsSiegeAt: guards assigned to TowerPosts (nearest free), fight from there; gothi within range of StoneAt chants (animation + line) and calls SetWardBonus(\"jarldom_gothi\", 1.1).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] In a siege, guards man towers and the ward shows +10% while the gothi chants.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nVillagers defend the home alongside Shieldwall.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j8","p2","shieldwall","integration"],"parent":"bn-1gf","size":"s","title":"#84 Shieldwall x Jarldom: guards take places at stave towers during sieges; gothi in Warstone range chants (+10% ward)"}	blake3:vD2H25oRvM89dORvknGtzQ9SM0bIswX_qs3Eg57LnhM
1791857847947146	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-he3	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.8 #85. Golf is Bob's mod (mods/Golf; tests/Golf.ApiCheck suggests an Api exists - check it). Follow code in Villager/Follow.cs.\n# Implementation Approach\n- Mark caddie in the villager panel; when the player is on a course (Golf.Api), the caddie follows; on each shot event, cosmetic club hand-over; on a bad shot (Golf.Api shot result), a heckle from a line table (Data/Tables.cs).\n- Add needed Golf.Api events if missing; release Golf.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Caddie follows, hands clubs, heckles a bad shot; without Golf, the option is hidden.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nLight-hearted cross-mod fun.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j8","p2","golf","integration"],"parent":"bn-1gf","size":"s","title":"#85 Golf x Jarldom: a villager marked caddie follows a player on the course, hands over clubs (cosmetic), heckles bad shots"}	blake3:OR0kJowB4jnIaBS7q8j6PflUz_01bCm5Sc8UTrj9Ojc
1791857848026868	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-8x9	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.8: connections are picked up along the way; this closes them out.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each of #82-#85 verified with the other mod installed and with it absent (no errors in the log).\n- [ ] Releases for every mod whose Api changed and for Jarldom.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nCloses J8.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j8","p2","live-test"],"parent":"bn-1gf","size":"s","title":"J8 live acceptance test (each connection with and without the other mod) + releases"}	blake3:cdEDzw3M16-6BZ_mIHSJBGFtyLbMJ0Q1Bst7jekbYJc
1791857860590557	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-29x	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.1 #1. Villagers chop, mine, build and smith (Villager/Work.cs, Villager/Crafts.cs, BuildOrders builder) but the colony is silent: their tool swings don't play the sounds a player's would. J1 exists to make the colony feel alive, and sound is the cheapest, biggest lever.\n# Goals\nEvery visible work action plays a matching vanilla clip at the villager, audible up to 30 m.\n# Reasoning/Justification\nGround rule: use the game's own clips where they fit (no licensing work, matches the world). Playing the clip at the work moment (hit/strike) rather than looping keeps it honest and sparse.\n# Implementation Approach\n- Find vanilla effect prefabs by name at load (e.g. the axe/pickaxe hit sfx on the tool's ItemData m_hitEffect / m_triggerEffect, sfx_build_hammer_*, forge/smelter sfx, saw from the workbench craft effect). Resolve once into a small table keyed by work kind (Data/Tables.cs); warn once per missing name (memory: sfx_horn didn't exist).\n- Play through EffectList/ZSFX locally on each client near the villager (no new ZDO data: derive from the body's existing animation/doing state already synced), max distance 30 m (AudioSource maxDistance / rolloff).\n- Rate hook: a per-colony \"work sound rate\" multiplier that #2 halves when miserable.\n- Tool: `jarldom sound <kind>` to play/test and `jarldom sound list` to show which clips resolved.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Axe, pickaxe, hammer, forge and saw work each make a vanilla sound at the villager.\n- [ ] Inaudible beyond 30 m; no sound when the work isn't actually happening.\n- [ ] No extra ZDO keys on villager bodies (network rule: nothing big on moving ZDOs).\n- [ ] Clean F6 reload (no duplicated audio sources).\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFirst half of the J1 acceptance \"the noise is clearly there\"; the rate hook feeds #2.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j1","p1","audio"],"parent":"bn-3je","size":"m","title":"J1 #1a: Work soundscape - villagers' work plays the game's own clips (axe, pickaxe, hammer, forge, saw), heard up to 30 m","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:wUgr7O3xUi-902fDjsV8YibFb61VulyW8gfFHN0OQIg
1791857860667883	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-15b	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.1 #1. The great hall (a room type in Core/RoomRules.cs; villagers lounge and drink there - Villager/Leisure.cs Tankards) should sound like a crowded hall.\n# Goals\nA looping murmur in the hall whose volume scales with how many villagers are present (0-1 of the roster/capacity) and with mood (mood < 0 -> quieter, sparser); during a feast it rises to a roar for the feast's duration.\n# Reasoning/Justification\nA room-bound loop is cheap and reads instantly. Prefer a vanilla crowd/ambience clip (check the game's tavern/Hildir/merchant ambience and dvergr camp loops); anything new must be CC0 or our own and listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.\n# Implementation Approach\n- Pure function in Core (e.g. Core/Rules.cs `Soundscape.HallLevel(present, capacity, mood, feasting)`) returning volume + \"sparseness\" (gaps in the loop); unit-tested.\n- Client-side AudioSource at the hall room centre (from the room record), updated every few seconds from the board snapshot; no new synced data beyond what the board already carries (present count may need adding to the board - keep it small).\n- Feast: read Feast state (Tools `jarldom feast`, ColonyRecord.LastFeast) to switch to the roar for its duration.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Hall at dusk with 8 villagers: murmur clearly audible; empty hall: silent.\n- [ ] Mood < 0 audibly quieter/sparser; feast = roar for its duration, then back.\n- [ ] Unit tests for HallLevel.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nCore of J1 acceptance; #2 turns it off when miserable.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j1","p1","audio"],"parent":"bn-3je","size":"m","title":"J1 #1b: Great hall murmur loop scaled by presence (0-1) and mood; a feast raises it to a roar","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:SdREIzbu1VMpRNPBgSOaKsSin3m_HGtFXgTHcJ8O-Wk
1791857860744714	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-30m	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.1 #2. Sound should reflect the colony's state, so misery is audible as absence.\n# Goals\nWhen colony mood < -40: work sounds play at half the rate, small talk (Villager/Society.cs Talk.Gossip) stops, the hall loop is off, and the colony window (Ui/ColonyWindow.cs) says \"The hall is quiet.\"\n# Implementation Approach\nOne Core predicate `Soundscape.Miserable(colonyMood)` (threshold -40, unit-tested) consumed by #1a rate, #1b loop, Talk.Gossip and the window line. Tool: `jarldom mood` already sets mood for testing.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Push mood below -40 (`jarldom mood ...`): it goes quiet, window shows \"The hall is quiet.\"; raise it: sound and talk return.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nSecond half of J1's acceptance; makes mood felt without UI.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j1","p1","audio"],"parent":"bn-3je","size":"s","title":"J1 #2: Quiet when miserable - at colony mood < -40: work sounds half rate, no small talk, hall loop off, 'The hall is quiet.'","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:ha0B-BiPkDNZthZfBXXmxZ2oALMmp_6RlE94JSc4M64
1791857860824057	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2ef	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.1 #3 (toggle). Paths should emerge where villagers actually walk.\n# Goals\nA pure, saved-state-light model: count footsteps on a 2 m grid within the colony radius; a cell walked >= N times in 3 days becomes painted; cap 400 painted cells per colony (keep the most-walked); cells not walked for 10 days revert to grass.\n# Reasoning/Justification\nPure Core class so the rules are unit-testable and the world layer only samples and paints. Rolling 3-day counts can be stored as per-cell day buckets (3 small counters) to stay compact.\n# Implementation Approach\nCore/Paths.cs (new): `Step(cell, day)`, `Due(day) -> (paint[], revert[])`. Serialized compactly on the colony record or a dedicated still ZDO if large (network rule: never on moving ZDOs; measure with `jarldom netsize`). Raise Plugin.DataVersion if ColonyRecord format changes. N is a server setting (default to tune live, e.g. 20).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Unit tests: threshold, 3-day window, cap 400 keeps the busiest, 10-day revert.\n- [ ] Storage size measured and documented.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFoundation for #3b; the path itself is the J1 acceptance.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j1","p1","toggle"],"parent":"bn-3je","size":"s","title":"J1 #3a: Desire paths core - 2 m footstep grid, threshold N in 3 days, cap 400 cells, 10-day revert (pure logic + tests)","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:ctqCFteLVzOGZtiR1XhizdLNehUzfVAQ6hyXgF5mz-0
1791857860902817	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3bk	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.1 #3. Painting uses the game's terrain paint (paint dirt, no height change).\n# Implementation Approach\n- Sample villager positions on the colony owner (Brain tick) into Paths.Step; players optionally too.\n- Paint/revert via TerrainComp paint operation (the same machinery as Shieldwall `siege mend` / TerrainComp.DoOperation with m_paintCleared/paintType Dirt; no level/raise). Only on the terrain owner and only after `ZNetScene.IsAreaReady` (pitfall in modding-pitfalls.md) - otherwise queue.\n- Revert paints back to grass (Reset paint type).\n- Server setting `DesirePaths` (on/off). Off -> stop counting; existing paint left (document) or reverted gradually.\n- Tool: `jarldom paths [show|clear|step N]` to visualise counts and force days.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Over 3 in-game days a path appears between the longhouse and the woodlot and nowhere random.\n- [ ] Never more than 400 painted cells; untouched cells revert after 10 days.\n- [ ] No terrain height change; no edits when the area isn't ready; toggle works.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nVisible history of colony life; J1 acceptance line 2.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j1","p1","toggle"],"parent":"bn-3je","size":"m","title":"J1 #3b: Desire paths in the world - sample villager steps, paint dirt (no height change) on the terrain owner after IsAreaReady; toggle + tool","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:0F8XuLKsdQU9WY1nq1HMp5NKCgabuv4FCqDrdVUCU_w
1791857860981919	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-17w	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.1 #6 (P3). Pure visuals on pieces that already exist; no new saved data.\n# Implementation Approach\nClient-side: toggle child visuals derived from already-synced state - weaver doing state (Villager/Weaving.cs), stockpile counts (Colony/Stock.cs) for woodpile fill level, hides in stock for tanning racks. Reuse vanilla meshes (e.g. woodpile stack stages, hide/cloth meshes) attached as children; clean up on F6.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Racks show cloth while weaving; woodpiles fill/empty with stock; hides appear on tanning racks.\n- [ ] No new ZDO keys; F6 leaves no orphan children.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nSmall visual life; low priority.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j1","p3"],"parent":"bn-3je","size":"m","title":"J1 #6: Work you can see (P3) - cloth on weaver's racks while weaving, woodpile stacks show stock, hides on tanning racks","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:Lfow3DW57rx96mxeCH8i215Z2AJm3Yu_bf7yRIgEMik
1791857861059852	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2xr	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.1 #7, optional: only if the watch AI makes it trivial. A WatchPost exists (Colony/Behaviours.cs) and a dusk lamplighter exists (Work.Lamplight).\n# Implementation Approach\nIf cheap: at dusk the watch walks to the nearest fireplace/brazier within the watch post's radius and turns it on (reuse Lamplight's fuel/enable), dawn turns it off.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Only if cheap (<= half a day): lamp lights at dusk and goes out at dawn; otherwise close as cut with a comment.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nSmall atmosphere touch.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j1","optional"],"parent":"bn-3je","size":"s","title":"J1 #7 (optional): Watch lamp - the night watch lights a brazier/lamp at the watchtower at dusk, out at dawn","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:IkAG3hQVU-3v_p_LLFO86TMl61TLKpjUkJbnKEKOOJk
1791857861141537	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-qto	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.1 #8. No new pieces, and no new saved data beyond one id per stand.\n# Goals\nA villager may hang up to 2 of their own things (first trophy, a commissioned weapon - Smith commissions exist in Villager/Crafts.cs) on item stands YOU HAVE BUILT within 4 m of their bed. Used stands show \"<Name>'s\" on hover. Removing the item gives it back to their bag.\n# Implementation Approach\n- New leisure/idle task (Villager/Leisure.cs or MakeOwn) to pick an eligible stand (ItemStand, player-built creator, empty, within 4 m of the claimed bed) and an eligible item from the bag (soul ZDO bag).\n- Mark the stand with one ZDO key (e.g. jarldom_owner = villager id, NOT a ZDOID - ZDOIDs renumber on load).\n- Patch ItemStand hover to add \"Sigrid's\"; patch the take-item path so the item goes back to the owner's bag (not the player's inventory) and the key clears. Pitfall: item duplication/loss on stand interactions - test both owner and non-owner clients.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A villager hangs their first trophy on your stand; hover shows their name.\n- [ ] Never more than 2 per villager; only stands within 4 m of their bed; only player-built stands.\n- [ ] Removing the item returns it to their bag (no dupes, no loss).\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nVillagers make the place theirs; J1 acceptance line 3.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j1","p1"],"parent":"bn-3je","size":"m","title":"J1 #8: Personal corners (capped) - a villager hangs up to 2 of their own things on player-built item stands within 4 m of their bed","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:WYgSGcxVgUVTPUeFjRcU-OpzSHZZfCnvb-0Hl3uQyN4
1791857861225533	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3dx	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.1 #9. Example: \"Heill, jarl!\" / Hail, jarl!\n# Implementation Approach\nData table in Data/Tables.cs (pure, testable): situation -> list of (Old Norse, English) pairs, ~40 total, with placeholders for player name/byname (#15). Use real Old Norse (check spelling/diacritics; the game font must render þ ð á é í ó ú æ ö - test glyphs). Unit test: every situation has >= 3 lines, placeholders valid.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] ~40 lines covering greeting, thanks, fear, weather, good night; tests pass; glyphs render in game.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nVoice of the colony; reused by #11 awe lines, #13 dock greeting, #15 bynames.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j1","p1"],"parent":"bn-3je","size":"s","title":"J1 #9a: Greetings line table - ~40 short Old Norse lines with English underneath, by situation (greeting, thanks, fear, weather, good night)","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:PqOxw6V26ROLfctLR2-mlc_Vafcc_0U6hKoZf8XUgNk
1791857861307339	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-c51	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.1 #9. Talk.Say (Villager/Society.cs) already shows overhead text.\n# Implementation Approach\nTriggers: player comes within ~6 m (greeting), gift/payday/heal (thanks), raid/hostile (fear), rain/storm (weather), dusk going to bed (good night). Render Old Norse over English (smaller, italic) in one Chat/overhead entry. Cooldowns per villager and per (villager, player) pair in memory (not saved). Insert the player's byname (#15) when present.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Walking into the colony gets a greeting; no spam (cooldowns hold); each situation seen at least once in a test.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nMakes villagers acknowledge the jarl.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j1","p1"],"parent":"bn-3je","size":"s","title":"J1 #9b: Greetings in the world - two-line overhead text, situational triggers, cooldowns per villager and per player","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:vHLVluLcQ_vBxTvIhrRu8oj8T7pBuxFj01C89NRWZGc
1791857861394179	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-tc4	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.1 #10. Text only, no music. Example: \"Heave, ho, the oak falls slow\".\n# Implementation Approach\n- Core: `WorkSong.Groups(workers)` clusters villagers by job kind within 15 m, size >= 3 (pure, tested).\n- Every ~20 s per group, all members Say the same line (table in Data/Tables.cs keyed by job kind: felling, mining, building, hauling, farming, rowing).\n- +10% work speed while the group lasts: apply in the work-rate path (Villager/Work.cs) via a transient flag, not saved.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Three woodcutters within 15 m show the same line every ~20 s and work 10% faster (measure with a tool readout); two don't.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nCommunal feel; a small reward for clustering work.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j1","p1"],"parent":"bn-3je","size":"m","title":"J1 #10: Work songs (text only) - 3+ villagers on the same job within 15 m: shared rhythm line every ~20 s and +10% work speed","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:oOCChRlpaUKGsBSXAz61_eRFRiaAdCEza_lk_OIVQnk
1791857861477649	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2ab	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.1 #11 requires detecting Omens' aurora night through its Api. mods/Omens/Api.cs has GetFate/AddFate only; the aurora lives in mods/Omens/BloodMoon.cs (class Aurora, SE_BobOmenAurora).\n# Implementation Approach\n`public static bool IsAurora()` true while the aurora night is active (works on clients too, not host-only - check how Omens syncs the state). Bump `Version`. Changelog + release Omens.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `omens` tool forcing an aurora makes IsAurora() true on host and client; false otherwise. Released.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nEnables #11 with no hard dependency.\n","kind":"task","labels":["omens","jarldom","next-saga","j1","p1","integration"],"parent":"bn-3je","size":"xs","title":"J1 #11a: Omens upstream - add Omens.Api.IsAurora() (and bump Omens Api Version, release Omens)","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:3Kcgozl8FiN_WHVC1a98MJurN4AuUq111QUJVepJOWM
1791857861561088	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1pn	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.1 #11. Without Omens it does nothing.\n# Implementation Approach\nVia ApiRef (bn-1xw) read Omens.Api.IsAurora(). When true: a low-priority task for villagers without urgent work (not guards on duty, not fleeing) - walk to an outdoor spot (not under roof: reuse Cover/roof checks), face up (head look target), Say an awe line (Data/Tables.cs, Old Norse + English), add an \"Aurora\" moodlet (Core Mood.Add, Tables.Moodlet).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] With Omens and a forced aurora: idle villagers go outside, look up, awed line, moodlet visible in panel.\n- [ ] Without Omens: no errors, nothing happens.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nCross-mod wonder moment; ties Omens into colony life.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j1","p1","integration"],"parent":"bn-3je","size":"s","title":"J1 #11b: Northern lights - during Omens' aurora, villagers without urgent work go outside, look up, say an awed line; moodlet","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:-TmYlOHjxAnGx7tAw6-SWV27SUYKVoqSoltuVPYto7I
1791857861641604	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3ra	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.1 #12. Wolves are tameable in vanilla. With the Hounds mod (standalone, H1) its trained hounds are used instead (later integration).\n# Implementation Approach\n- Colony window: list tamed wolves within the radius with \"Adopt\" (action routed via Jarldom_Act RPC to the pillars owner).\n- Mark adopted by a small key on the wolf's ZDO (colony id) - wolves move, so keep it tiny (one string); list stored on the record by a stable own id, not ZDOID.\n- Pure Core list logic + tool `jarldom dogs [list|adopt <n>]`.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tame a wolf, adopt it from the window; it persists across a world reload.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nPrerequisite for dog behaviour and raid warnings.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j1","p1"],"parent":"bn-3je","size":"m","title":"J1 #12a: Village dogs - adopt tamed wolves inside the radius from the colony window","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:rkAVh0i15QuI7RgtCpbQAno0Bwj0HkSU-DEnCEE5aQU
1791857861720022	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2dm	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.1 #12.\n# Implementation Approach\nDrive adopted wolves' MonsterAI follow target: by day pick a working villager to tail (rotate every few minutes); at night set follow to a spot by the hall hearth and let them idle/sleep (wolf has no sleep anim: sit/idle). Don't fight the vanilla tame/follow-player command: player \"follow\" overrides until released. Pitfall: freezing when owner 0 past the active area (memory) - keep them within the radius.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Dogs trail villagers by day and lie by the hall hearth at night; player follow command still works.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nVillage life.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j1","p1"],"parent":"bn-3je","size":"m","title":"J1 #12b: Village dogs behaviour - follow villagers about, sleep by the hall hearth at night","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:zF3zvgbtLBVTsevwHgPQavnJzHfcJWMY0BEw485zy6Y
1791857861798578	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-fe1	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.1 #12: \"a raid warning when a hostile comes within 40 m (an alert in the colony window and on the war horn)\".\n# Implementation Approach\nOn the owner, every ~1 s scan for hostile characters within 40 m of each adopted dog (use the cached scans; no FindObjectsOfTypeAll on timers - perf memory). On first sight: wolf bark sfx (vanilla wolf alert), Alerts (Villager/Society.cs) entry, WarHorn (Colony/Behaviours.cs) hint/alert. Cooldown per raid.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A wolf barks and the window alerts before a raid shows up on screen (test with `jarldom raid <event>` and an approaching mob).\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nJ1 acceptance line 4; makes dogs useful.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j1","p1"],"parent":"bn-3je","size":"s","title":"J1 #12c: Village dogs raid warning - bark and alert when a hostile comes within 40 m (colony window + war horn)","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:5QqqQCtsCzs1ud7DWGgkbHsLe8Houa1kzJ0dfGYHAWY
1791857861881694	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-10w	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.1 Accept lines for J1. Run in Bob's Creative world with the ClaudeTools mailbox (see claudetools-live-game memory); mind test-tools blast radius (box-filter), never lose Bob's gear, check `jarldom tribute` and `siege status` before time jumps.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Stand in the hall at dusk with 8 villagers: the noise is clearly there; push mood below -40 and it goes quiet.\n- [ ] Over 3 in-game days, a path appears between the longhouse and the woodlot and nowhere random.\n- [ ] A villager hangs their first trophy on your stand.\n- [ ] A wolf barks before a raid shows up on screen.\n- [ ] README playtest checklist updated; version bumped; CHANGELOG; dist + manifest released.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nCloses J1.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j1","p1","live-test"],"parent":"bn-3je","size":"m","title":"J1 live acceptance test in Creative + release","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:HoIdi5Csek7rnZQc0rDB2pKlInij6lcX85UStsk0lXY
1791857861964692	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1rp	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.2 #13. Coming home by sea at night should light the beacon and bring people to the dock; by day just the dock greeting.\n# Implementation Approach\nPure Core `Return.Detect(shipPos, shipVel, shoreline/colony centre, isNight, lastReturn)`: within 250 m of the colony shore, velocity heading inward, cooldown 10 min (real or game - pick game seconds consistently with Brain.GameDt). Unit tests. Shore = nearest water edge to pillars (reuse Trade.Shore logic).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tests: heading in vs out, 250 m boundary, night vs day, 10 min cooldown.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nTrigger for #13b-d.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j2","p1"],"parent":"bn-11e","size":"s","title":"J2 #13a: Beacon rules core - player ship within 250 m of the colony shore heading in, dusk to dawn, once per return (10 min cooldown)","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:Jdyd3hNA9dtsrQkv54LtpuVHiLsTj47MG9-pqq2JSpo
1791857862050620	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-sqa	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.2 #13: light \"Wayfinder's beacon fire through its API\". Wayfinder has BobBeaconFire in mods/Wayfinder/Pieces.cs but no Api class yet.\n# Implementation Approach\nAdd mods/Wayfinder/Api.cs: `public const int Version = 1; Vector3? NearestBeacon(Vector3 at, float radius); bool LightBeacon(Vector3 at, float radius)` (owner-routed, safe from any client). Follow the convention from bn-1xw. Release Wayfinder.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A test command lights the nearest beacon from a client; released.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nLets Jarldom use Wayfinder's beacon with no hard dependency; also used by the J6 lighthouse.\n","kind":"task","labels":["wayfinder","jarldom","next-saga","j2","p1","integration"],"parent":"bn-11e","size":"s","title":"J2 #13b: Wayfinder upstream - Api to find and light a beacon fire near a point (Wayfinder.Api.LightBeacon / NearestBeacon)","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:771PzdmmFUPkN-tECOf6Jlo70GvefRuUSpjEoRIKz7s
1791857862132231	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3a9	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.2 #13: \"the watch (or any guard) lights the nearest beacon\".\n# Implementation Approach\n- On a detected night return (#13a): pick the watch (WatchPost) or any guard; walk to the nearest beacon; light it: Wayfinder.Api.LightBeacon via ApiRef, else a brazier/fireplace the jarl marked as \"colony beacon\" (designation like the ChestPicker; one key on that piece's ZDO) - enable its fire.\n- It should be lit BEFORE the player lands: if the walk is too long, light it remotely after a short delay (log it) rather than miss.\n- Tool: `jarldom beacon [mark|test]`.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Sail home at night: the beacon is lit before you land (with and without Wayfinder).\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nJ2 acceptance line 1.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j2","p1","integration"],"parent":"bn-11e","size":"m","title":"J2 #13c: The watch lights the colony beacon - Wayfinder beacon via Api, else a Jarldom brazier marked as colony beacon","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:Ck_DN_aAQgrgB-HO9LTDVxJxyTI_ft3PckaJB4ILCS4
1791857862210941	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1xk	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.2 #13: up to 6 free villagers walk to the dock; by day just the dock greeting. Docks: fishing dock zone exists (Data/Tables.cs \"Dock\"); else the shore landing point.\n# Implementation Approach\nOn return detection, choose up to 6 villagers not on urgent work, send them to points near the landing (snap to navmesh with Villager/Nav.cs), face the ship, Say a greeting (#9a table, with byname #15b), then release back to work after landing or 2 min.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Sail home: villagers are at the dock and greet you; at most 6; they go back to work after.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nThe emotional payoff of \"the jarl's return\".\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j2","p1"],"parent":"bn-11e","size":"m","title":"J2 #13d: Dock greeting - up to 6 free villagers walk to the dock and greet you as you land (night and day)","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:yuHQO7xmUL-77HxC6H6MZbELDrz9EYpviVLZynJIV6Q
1791857862291890	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1u6	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.2 #15. Villager bynames exist (Core/Records.cs VillagerState.Byname); players have none. Each colony keeps a tally per player.\n# Implementation Approach\n- ColonyRecord: per player id (stable player id, not name) a compact counter set. Raise Plugin.DataVersion (format change).\n- Hooks: boss kills (Character.OnDeath for bosses with a player attacker near/linked - also count kills far away when the player is a colony member), arm rings given (Items.cs ring give), days away (Away/CatchUp), raids at home (raid end with player present), ascensions overseen (Ascension in World/Faith.cs), feasts held (Feast.Call).\n- Pure Core counters + tests; tool `jarldom tally [player] [key n]`.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each counter increments on its event; persists across reload; record size growth measured.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nData for bynames (#15b), co-jarls (#16), memorial (#25), verse (#19).\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j2","p1","data-version"],"parent":"bn-11e","size":"m","title":"J2 #15a: Player deed tally per colony - bosses slain, rings given, days away, raids fought at home, ascensions overseen, feasts held","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:6zX3-Ny__ct7EYpymsBspLxFHRRkz07_q1BKl-NeIr0
1791857862375151	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2ro	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.2 #15.\n# Implementation Approach\nCore `Bynames.For(tally)`: ordered title table (Data/Tables.cs) with thresholds (per-boss \"-bane\" for latest/most notable boss, Ring-giver, the Absent, Shield of the hall, Soul-guide, Feast-giver...), pick highest rank; unit-tested. Display in greetings (#9b), saga lines (Core/Stories.cs), colony window. Log a saga entry when a byname changes.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] After a boss kill your byname changes (e.g. \"Bob Bonemass-bane\") and shows in window, greetings and saga.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nJ2 acceptance line 2 (first half).\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j2","p1"],"parent":"bn-11e","size":"s","title":"J2 #15b: Player bynames - highest-ranked qualifying title ('Bob Bonemass-bane', 'Ring-giver', 'the Absent') shown in greetings, saga and window","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:XR8itPKZXUlsOTysLRgw8xJrbTubXhZJxKY39Cy-6Lo
1791857862457246	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2ed	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.2 #16. Example: \"They say Bob gives rings, but Quad brings the trophies\". Co-jarl followers exist (memory: co-jarl factions).\n# Implementation Approach\nAdd a Gossip variant in Villager/Society.cs: when the colony has >= 2 players with bynames, occasionally (low chance, cooldown) pick two, phrase from templates keyed by their byname kinds, slant by the villager's opinion of each.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] With two bynamed players, comparison lines appear occasionally and reflect opinion; never with one.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nMultiplayer colonies feel social.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j2","p1"],"parent":"bn-11e","size":"s","title":"J2 #16: Co-jarls compared - with two bynamed players, villagers sometimes compare them in small talk using their opinions","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:LEBX9r3BkifXroDAdcYe7LOC1iD3JWqUBCmfkmqfXZc
1791857862538856	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-fz1	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.2 #17.\n# Implementation Approach\n- Detect the local player sitting (Chair attach) in a seat inside the great hall room at dusk with >= 3 villagers present; 30 s timer (cancel on stand).\n- Apply a custom StatusEffect \"JarldomHallFed\" (+1 comfort while it lasts; extend Rested by 5 min).\n- +2 opinion with villagers present: route via Jarldom_Act RPC to the owner.\n- Once per day per player (key in record or player custom data).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Sit 30 s at dusk with 3 villagers: buff and +2 opinion; second time that day: nothing; fewer than 3: nothing.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nRewards spending time with the colony.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j2","p1"],"parent":"bn-11e","size":"m","title":"J2 #17: Eating in the hall - sit in a hall seat at dusk with >= 3 villagers for 30 s: Hall-fed buff (Rested +5 min, +1 comfort), +2 opinion, once a day","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:m7kIPmThfhxmwAMbDXmqOm4qyPeMHW56uQ8FlOSzoJc
1791857862623332	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-clr2	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.2 #18.\n# Implementation Approach\nOn player wake (Game sleep end / Bed interaction), if the bed is inside a longhouse room of a colony: extend Rested by 5 min; owner gives a small opinion gain with villagers who slept in the same room (room id from the record).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Sleep in a colony longhouse: Rested +5 min and opinion up with roommates only.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nThe jarl lives among their people.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j2","p1"],"parent":"bn-11e","size":"s","title":"J2 #18: Sleeping among them - sleeping in a bed in a colony longhouse: Rested +5 min, small opinion gain with roommates","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:CnHkSfL3Ty4b_DqySrdA0t3VY0rlFZL_jlo-5AjFj4o
1791857862712354	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-gka4	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.2 #19. Example: \"The jarl came home on the black-prowed wave / three trolls fell at the Elder's grave\".\n# Implementation Approach\nCore/Verse.cs: input = today's log entries (Core/Records.cs LogEntry, saga ZDO) + names/bynames; choose up to 4 event kinds (boss slain, return home, raid, birth/arrival, ascension, feast, festival, great work...), one line per kind, from alliterative templates with slots (who, what, where, epithet). Deterministic given a seed (testable). Unit tests for selection, once-per-kind, 2-4 lines.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Given a log with a boss kill, the verse names the boss; tests pass.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nThe verse is reused by J3 (funeral, einherjar), J4 (festivals, Winter Nights names), #14 trophies, #51 runestone legends.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j2","p1"],"parent":"bn-11e","size":"m","title":"J2 #19a: Skald verse engine - 2-4 alliterative lines from today's log, templates keyed by event type, each kind <= once per night (pure + tests)","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:Q7dlTrwMzLt0VNtTAZM-Ch5nxlM07vJKPV7de82crgw
1791857862802046	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2rib	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.2 #19. The Skald profession exists (Villager/Tasks.cs, Villager/Work.cs, Items.cs drum).\n# Implementation Approach\nAfter dusk, the skald (or any villager if none? - spec says the skald; without one, no verse) goes to the hall, plays a short drum/lyre beat (vanilla clip), and speaks the lines one by one as subtitles (overhead + a bottom-of-screen subtitle for players in the hall). Save the verse to the chronicle (Core/Stories.cs; saga ZDO, merge-only). Tool: `jarldom verse [now|preview]`.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] After a boss kill, the next night's verse names the boss and appears in the chronicle.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nJ2 acceptance line 2.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j2","p1"],"parent":"bn-11e","size":"m","title":"J2 #19b: The skald recites after dusk in the hall - subtitles, lines saved to the chronicle","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:agK_hXNSHxxsq4-Rj2RcCx9E0b53qjytXs91cZkLcFQ
1791857862887267	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-dri7	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.2 #14, optional: only if it reuses the existing deposit code (HighSeat in Colony/Behaviours.cs; treasury chest via ChestPicker).\n# Implementation Approach\nE on the high seat with trophies/valuables in hand moves them into the treasure room's chest; deeds +1 per first-of-kind trophy (flag per prefab); add a log entry so tomorrow's verse mentions them.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Only if cheap: deposit works, first-of-kind deeds +1, verse mentions it; otherwise close as cut.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nCeremony around trophies.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j2","optional"],"parent":"bn-11e","size":"s","title":"J2 #14 (optional): Laying trophies at the high seat - E with trophies/valuables: into the treasure chest, deeds +1 per first-of-kind, verse mentions them","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:9KruS5lBcF-obzsv5G_0PS72lM3jfgvc4ycpZhhBaW4
1791857862972895	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-35xu	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.2 Accept lines. Bob's karve and longship lie ~25 m out at ~(383-395, 1129) in Creative.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Sail home at night: the beacon is lit before you land, and villagers are at the dock.\n- [ ] After a boss kill, your byname changes and the next night's verse names the boss.\n- [ ] README playtest checklist; version bump; CHANGELOG; dist + manifest released.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nCloses J2.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j2","p1","live-test"],"parent":"bn-11e","size":"s","title":"J2 live acceptance test in Creative + release","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:FE7KrRiM4fW2Aku-PTq1ukFj8xKt_lNnxwaxsTxFuvo
1791857863056166	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2hg6	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.3 #20: interrupted (F6, the owner leaving) -> finish from where it was; rewards apply EXACTLY ONCE (an idempotency key per ascension). Ascension today: World/Faith.cs Ascension/AscendTask + the Pyre (Colony/Behaviours.cs).\n# Implementation Approach\n- Core: ceremony state machine (stage, started-at, key = soul id + ascension count) stored on a still ZDO (the soul or the pyre/ship piece), not on moving bodies. \"Rewards applied\" set keyed by idempotency key in ColonyRecord; Raise DataVersion.\n- On load/ownership change, resume from the stored stage.\n- Retrofit the pyre to use it.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Unit tests: rewards once even if Apply is called twice / after a simulated reload mid-stage.\n- [ ] Pyre ascension still works live.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nSafety foundation for the funeral ship (#20c).\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j3","p2","data-version"],"parent":"bn-3k3","size":"m","title":"J3 #20a: Ascension idempotency - a key per ascension so rewards apply exactly once; resumable ceremony state (pyre and ship)"}	blake3:OBWLtVvMPDMpr1Vm6v1l4vGWLteOHgQFcOBagySxWxc
1791857863136769	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-18tx	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.3 #20: from Hold rank, a new ascension option alongside the pyre.\n# Implementation Approach\nNew piece JarldomFuneralKarve (prefab name kept forever): clone the karve visual, strip Ship/Rigidbody/WearNTear-ship bits, keep a Container for grave goods (like the Pyre's). Placement rule: at the shore (water depth check at the stern). Hover/E like the Pyre. Unlocked at Hold rank (Core/Rules.cs Ranks).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Buildable only at Hold rank, only at the shore; holds grave goods; F6-clean.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nThe vessel for #20c.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j3","p2"],"parent":"bn-3k3","size":"m","title":"J3 #20b: Funeral karve piece - the game's karve model with no sailing physics, built at the shore, grave goods in its hold"}	blake3:cIMWIMhFSScaDR9OMuqkZkTL-3GPEGzrkmu4uWd1Lio
1791857863220167	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-36x7	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.3 #20.\n# Implementation Approach\nColony window ascension choice: pyre or ship (when a funeral karve exists). At dusk the soul walks aboard; fire effects (vanilla fire vfx), then the piece moves along a scripted path 120 m out (owner moves the ZDO position at a fixed speed - keep ZDO tiny), then sinks and is destroyed with its grave goods consumed. Rewards x1.5 those of the pyre, applied via #20a (exactly once). Resumes after F6/owner leave from the stored stage/progress.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Take one villager from arrival to the funeral ship; the rewards apply once even with F6 mid-ceremony.\n- [ ] Owner leaving mid-ceremony: it finishes when someone returns; rewards once.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nJ3 acceptance line 1; the spectacle of a Viking funeral.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j3","p2"],"parent":"bn-3k3","size":"m","title":"J3 #20c: Funeral ship ceremony - soul boards at dusk, set alight, drifts 120 m out on a scripted path, sinks; rewards x1.5 over the pyre"}	blake3:kiOvmGdzXr3KW0-AxgdavWyjBWI5ZxQ9T-ELCFUyJXU
1791857863303192	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-vqr7	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.3 #21. World/Migration.cs Valkyrie (Flight MonoBehaviour) already flies in arrivals.\n# Implementation Approach\nAdd a \"circle then depart upward\" flight path to Valkyrie.Flight; trigger at the ascension climax (client-visible: drive from the ceremony stage, not a new synced object if possible).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Pyre and ship ascensions both show one circle overhead and a departure skyward.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nValhalla made visible.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j3","p2"],"parent":"bn-3k3","size":"s","title":"J3 #21: Valkyrie flyover - every ascension (pyre or ship) the migration Valkyrie circles once overhead and flies off skyward"}	blake3:FO-L6-stpNUzT3me8m-ddXNtDDOnu2jx_IpkkK16rOI
1791857863391324	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-33ri	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.3 #22 (P3). Anniversary uses the configurable colony year (J4 calendar).\n# Implementation Approach\nAscension date stored already in log/memorial data; on the anniversary day spawn a local-only raven visual (vanilla raven model as used by Hugin, or Wayfinder Raven.cs) on the memorial runestone/wall; E shows a line from the soul (template with their name/deed).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] With `jarldom time` to the anniversary: raven perches for a day; E gives a line.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nQuiet remembrance.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j3","p3"],"parent":"bn-3k3","size":"s","title":"J3 #22 (P3): Raven on the runestone - on an ascended soul's anniversary a raven perches on their memorial runestone for a day; E for a line","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:g_3QFEn2f2zZk63r91bklqAVofWLaTHvJyKRAgSXNyg
1791857863473829	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3445	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.3 #23.\n# Implementation Approach\nCore `Einherjar.Pick(raidState, ascendedSouls)`: losing = hall or pillars under attack or >= 50% fighters down; candidates = ascended souls not yet returned; one per raid. Mark \"returned\" in the record (DataVersion if new field). Unit tests.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tests for the losing conditions, once per soul, one per raid.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nRule core for #23b.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j3","p2"],"parent":"bn-3k3","size":"s","title":"J3 #23a: They answer back - trigger rules (losing raid: hall or pillars attacked, or >= 50% of fighters down), once per soul, max one per raid"}	blake3:JOpdO9rXwUaMa61c8nmDDI7DD6G4kgEhqlBe0Tc3JOA
1791857863558093	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-10zk	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.3 #23.\n# Implementation Approach\nSpawn a temporary villager body (VillagerPrefab clone) with the soul's remembered gear (store the gear list at ascension time, small), a glow material/light, combat AI (Villager/Combat.cs), immortal or high health, despawn after 90 s with a vfx. Shout their name (Say + Chat center message). Saga entry.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] In a losing test raid (`jarldom raid ...` + kill fighters), one ascended soul returns for 90 s, named, logged; never twice for the same soul.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nPays off ascension in later crises.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j3","p2"],"parent":"bn-3k3","size":"m","title":"J3 #23b: Einherjar return - the soul appears glowing in their old gear for 90 s, fights, name called out, saga records it"}	blake3:2otH1ckxvPGycZbdzHdr67eyNqtbnBJPYed6A5q8TlU
1791857863641056	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-34zs	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.3 #24 (redesigned): never permanent, never fatal, always a way back.\n# Implementation Approach\nCore Worth (Core/Rules.cs Worth): track last-worth-rise day per soul (VillagerState; raise DataVersion). `Dimming.Stage(now, lastRise)` 0/1/2; work multiplier; Restless moodlet at stage 2; reason text \"Hasn't done anything worthy in N days\". Unit tests.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tests: 8 and 16-day boundaries, reset on any worth gain, never beyond stage 2, never kills.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nGentle pressure to keep souls growing.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j3","p2","data-version"],"parent":"bn-3k3","size":"s","title":"J3 #24a: The Dimming core - no worth rise for 8 days: stage 1 (-10% work); 16 days: stage 2 (-20% work, Restless moodlet); any worth gain resets"}	blake3:oziyUr3s6B1V53I4bsMZejFthgBJkdEQkFABxE_tfVA
