1791857896405324	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-hc6e	{"description":"# Context & Background\nFirst task of the Bathhouse mod (JARLDOM-NEXT.md). Standalone mods must be useful alone and expose a tiny `Bathhouse.Api` that Jarldom finds by reflection; nothing exists yet. Spec section 3.1 (#81, P1): first in the whole build order because it is small and standalone.\n\n# Goals\nAn empty but buildable, testable, publishable Bathhouse mod that every later Bathhouse bone builds on.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nCopying the repo's existing small-mod layout keeps build/publish/test/manifest automatic and keeps every mod looking the same to Bob and to other agents.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- New project mods/Bathhouse/ copied from a small mod's pattern (mods/Spyglass, mods/Delivery): Bathhouse.csproj (net48, Directory.Build.props), Plugin.cs with `public const string Guid/Name/Version` (scripts/publish.py regexes these), Core/ for pure logic (no Unity), DESCRIPTION.txt, CHANGELOG.txt, cover.jpg, README with a playtest checklist.\n- tests/Bathhouse.Tests console project linking Core/*.cs (same as tests/Spyglass.Tests/Program.cs style); wire into scripts/test.py if it enumerates projects.\n- mods/*/*.csproj is auto-discovered by scripts/build.py and scripts/publish.py, so `mise run build|test|publish|install` pick it up; publish writes the dist/manifest.json entry.\n- RESTART_REQUIRED.txt if pieces/items/recipes need a restart (see reload-levels memory / Quad's Claude Tools rules).\n- ServerSettings: server-authoritative config sync as in Jarldom/ServerSettings.cs.\n- A ClaudeTools command root (`bath ...`) registered like Jarldom/Tools/Tools.cs.\n- Prefab golden list tests/Bathhouse.Tests/prefabs.txt per foundation bone bn-2vn (append-only; names prefixed Bathhouse).\n- Read ~/repos/valheim-claude-tools/docs/modding-pitfalls.md first.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `mise run build` and `mise run test` pass with the new project\n- [ ] `mise run publish` lists Bathhouse in dist/manifest.json (version 0.0.x, not announced)\n- [ ] F6 reload of Bathhouse is clean (no errors, no leftover objects)\n- [ ] `bath help` answers through the ClaudeTools mailbox\n- [ ] Golden prefab list file and test exist (empty list ok)\n\n# Dependencies\nbn-2vn\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFoundation for every Bathhouse milestone.\n","kind":"task","labels":["b1","bathhouse","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-33h","size":"s","title":"Bathhouse: scaffold the standalone mod project (csproj, Plugin, Core, tests, README, tools command, golden prefab list)","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:-0foAp1UGOvjsiQWFjhHWQwnMr25Qc-9wlQJGfqShsI
1791857896489221	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-9t22	{"description":"# Context & Background\nA sauna room = roofed, enclosed, with a sauna stove and a bench. Sitting in it for 60 s gives Bathed. Throwing water on the stones makes steam. These rules must be testable without Unity.\n\n# Goals\nDeterministic, unit-tested rules: room verdict from facts (roof cover %, enclosure, stove present and lit, bench present), per-player sit timer (pauses when you stand, resets when you leave), steam state from the bucket.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nPure logic in Core is a ground rule (testable classes). Separating facts (gathered in game) from the verdict mirrors Jarldom's Core/RoomRules.cs Judge(RoomType, RoomFacts), which has proved robust on real houses.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Core/SaunaRules.cs: `SaunaVerdict Judge(SaunaFacts f)` with failure reasons (\"no roof\", \"open to the wind\", \"no stove\", \"stove cold\", \"no bench\") for hover text.\n- Core/BathTimer.cs: accumulate seconds while seated in a valid room; 60 s -> grant; steam multiplies heat (shortens to e.g. 45 s while steaming, tune in tests).\n- Thresholds as constants/config, server-synced.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tests cover each failure reason, the 60 s grant, pause on stand, reset on leaving, steam effect\n- [ ] Verdict reasons are short human strings usable in hover text\n\n# Dependencies\nba0\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nThe rest of B1 just gathers facts and applies the verdict.\n","kind":"task","labels":["b1","bathhouse","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-33h","size":"s","title":"Bathhouse B1: pure sauna rules in Core (what counts as a sauna room, 60 s sit timer, steam boost) + tests","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:Exjk5QaNUUif-YLPy0bKqyce9PDCDsQnHk97f7y3WlY
1791857896573011	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1a44	{"description":"# Context & Background\nThree buildable pieces: sauna stove (stones on top, burns wood), bench (sit), water bucket (E: throw water on the stones -> hiss + steam cloud).\n\n# Goals\nPieces that look Norse and believable, build from the hammer with sensible costs, and give a satisfying steam moment.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nBob rejected floating-plank kitbashes (Jarldom pillars 0.1.18): if a clone of a vanilla prefab (stone oven, hearth, bench, tankard) does not read right, make a real Blender model (pipeline in blender-anim-pipeline memory). Audio: game clips first (fire/hiss/water splash), anything new CC0 or own recording listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Stove: Fireplace component (fuel wood) on a stone body with a heap of rocks; Smoke like the hearth so it needs ventilation or a smoke-hole (Building kit K1 has one).\n- Bench: Chair component (attach point), long enough for 3 sitters.\n- Bucket: a small piece or hand item; Interact on the stove consumes nothing (or water from a barrel) and starts the steam vfx for N s (sync via ZDO float on the stove).\n- Prefab names BathhouseStove/BathhouseBench/BathhouseBucket - FOREVER (append to golden list).\n- Recipes in the hammer under Furniture/Misc; costs: stone + wood + bronze nails for the stove (tune).\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] All three pieces placeable, snap sensibly, have support values, can be deconstructed with full refund\n- [ ] Steam visible to all players in multiplayer\n- [ ] No pink/red effects (Bob dislikes them)\n- [ ] Prefab names added to the golden list\n\n# Dependencies\nba0\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nThe visible core of the mod.\n","kind":"task","labels":["b1","bathhouse","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-33h","size":"m","title":"Bathhouse B1: sauna stove, sauna bench and water bucket pieces (models, recipes, steam vfx/sfx)","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:1adidKcxCqXEpSkyabE8qjJeztSsyf7q9lJZuDrrF_M
1791857896657108	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3thg	{"description":"# Context & Background\nThe Core verdict needs facts gathered in the world: is the space roofed, is it enclosed, is a stove there and lit, is the player seated on a bench in it.\n\n# Goals\nReliable sauna detection on real player-built rooms, including odd shapes, with hover text on the stove saying why it isn't a sauna yet.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nJarldom's room measuring was hardened on real houses (windows, walls up to 1 m outside the outline, doors in sight, shutters aren't doors; wood_floor colliders are tagged leaky so Cover ignores them; use wood_roof). Reuse the approach, not the code (no hard dependency on Jarldom).\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Gather facts around the stove within ~6 m: Cover.GetCoverForPoint (roof %), ray fan for enclosure, find bench Chair in the same room.\n- Player seated: Player.IsAttached + attach point belongs to a BathhouseBench.\n- Stove hover: \"Sauna: ready\" or the first failure reason.\n- Cache per stove, refresh every few seconds, not per frame (perf-hitches memory).\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A small closed stone hut with stove + bench reads as a sauna; removing a wall or the roof shows the reason\n- [ ] Detection costs < 0.1 ms/frame averaged\n- [ ] Works for the piece owner and other players\n\n# Dependencies\nb1core, b1pieces\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nMakes the Bathed buff fair and understandable.\n","kind":"task","labels":["b1","bathhouse","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-33h","size":"m","title":"Bathhouse B1: in-game room check (roof + enclosure + stove + bench) and sitting detection","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:Lsr6uLsWWTqj9ejrCrO-MGtkzp6AOgU-WrFTa9WfDPE
1791857896735560	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3g83	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSitting 60 s in a valid sauna grants Bathed.\n\n# Goals\nA clear buff with an icon and tooltip listing every effect.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nStatus effects are the game's own mechanism; extending Rested by adding time to the existing Rested SE (rather than a separate rested) keeps it compatible with beds and food.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- SE_Stats subclass BathhouseBathed: stamina regen x1.10, cold resistance (like the fire's warm/cold immunity: remove Cold/Freezing while active), comfort +2 applied when Rested is computed (patch SE_Rested.CalculateComfortLevel or add +2 to the comfort tally).\n- On grant: remove Wet; add 10 min to Rested (add it if missing).\n- Duration ~20 min (tune); icon from game sprites or a simple new one.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tooltip lists: comfort +2, Rested +10 min, stamina regen +10%, cold resistance, cures Wet\n- [ ] Wet is removed on grant\n- [ ] Rested gains 10 min (or starts) on grant\n- [ ] Buff survives logout/login (SE saving) or is documented as not doing so\n\n# Dependencies\nb1core\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nThe reward that makes building a sauna worth it.\n","kind":"task","labels":["b1","bathhouse","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-33h","size":"s","title":"Bathhouse B1: the Bathed status effect (comfort +2, Rested +10 min, stamina regen +10%, cold resistance, cures Wet)","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:A4e7J2I0_58Kc-Aei5ptBFuvvV3UQ0lmp2dqB5YLY30
1791857896827634	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-p0so	{"description":"# Context & Background\nGround rule: a ClaudeTools command for every system, so agents can test without Bob.\n\n# Goals\nRead-only inspection of saunas and test helpers to grant/clear buffs.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nLive testing goes through the mailbox; without commands each check needs Bob at the keyboard.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- `bath status`: nearby stoves, verdicts, seated players, timers.\n- `bath room <x z>`: verdict facts at a point.\n- `bath grant bathed|invigorated` / `bath clear`.\n- `bath steam`: trigger steam on the nearest stove.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each command returns JSON through the mailbox\n- [ ] Commands that change state are marked as cheats like Jarldom's\n\n# Dependencies\nb1room, b1buff\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nMakes live acceptance fast and repeatable.\n","kind":"task","labels":["b1","bathhouse","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-33h","size":"s","title":"Bathhouse B1: ClaudeTools commands (bath status, bath room <x z>, bath grant, bath steam)","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:8no2-lu6k7KOlFmru5pU5DXS1qMZDv5sL9WjXcWqFPc
1791857896916349	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1fr3	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone B1 of Bathhouse. Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, `mise run publish`, install, push dist.\n\n# Goals\nBathhouse 0.1.0 published with milestone B1 verified in the game.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nBob wants every change built, installed and released, and milestone acceptance checked live, not only in unit tests.\n\n# Implementation Approach\nTest in Bob's Creative world via the ClaudeTools mailbox (see claudetools-live-game memory): never lose Bob's gear, check `siege status` and Jarldom tribute before time jumps, tag test spawns and remove them by tag. Update the README playtest checklist with what was verified and what was not.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Build a stone hut with stove + bench, sit 60 s: Bathed with all listed effects\n- [ ] Steam from the bucket visible to a second player\n- [ ] Stove hover explains a missing roof/wall\n- [ ] Unit tests pass\n- [ ] F6 reload clean\n- [ ] Version 0.1.0 in Plugin.cs, CHANGELOG entry, dist/manifest.json updated and pushed\n\n# Dependencies\nb1core, b1pieces, b1room, b1buff, b1tools\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nMilestone gate: the next milestone's work is blocked on this.\n","kind":"task","labels":["b1","bathhouse","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-33h","size":"s","title":"Bathhouse B1: live test in Creative + release Bathhouse 0.1.0","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:NcORveisqNSDTBDOtzEaHar_AjZnyw8LWzaSPTA1CTE
1791857897003096	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1bgr	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: an outdoor cold plunge (a tub, or a dip in water) RIGHT AFTER bathing gives Invigorated.\n\n# Goals\nPlunge detection with a short window after Bathed (e.g. 60 s after leaving the sauna).\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nAllowing natural water too (lakes, sea) keeps it cheap and fun; the tub makes it buildable anywhere.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Plunge tub piece BathhousePlungeTub (water surface visual; interact or walk in to plunge).\n- Natural water: Character.InWater / liquid depth >= ~0.8 m.\n- Window starts when the player leaves the sauna with Bathed; plunge inside the window -> Invigorated; outside -> nothing (hover hint).\n- Window logic in Core with tests.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Plunge within the window grants Invigorated; after the window it doesn't\n- [ ] Works in the tub and in sea/lake water\n- [ ] Tub piece snaps, has support, refunds\n\n# Dependencies\nb1rel\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nCompletes the Norse sauna ritual.\n","kind":"task","labels":["b2","bathhouse","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-33h","size":"m","title":"Bathhouse B2: cold plunge (tub piece or a dip in water) right after Bathed -> Invigorated","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:aOUb7p69ZuZfaTxy_0V5WlqA_PvrPeSor98SSoksy6A
1791857897093653	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2e08	{"description":"# Context & Background\nReward for the cold plunge.\n\n# Goals\nBuff with icon/tooltip: +5% move speed, +10% max stamina, 10 min.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nSeparate SE so it stacks with Bathed and expires on its own timer.\n\n# Implementation Approach\nSE_Stats BathhouseInvigorated: m_speedModifier 0.05, max stamina +10% (patch GetMaxStamina or SE stat), duration 600 s.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tooltip shows +5% move speed, +10% stamina, 10 min\n- [ ] Expires at 10 min\n- [ ] Stacks with Bathed\n\n# Dependencies\nb1rel\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nThe plunge's payoff.\n","kind":"task","labels":["b2","bathhouse","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-33h","size":"s","title":"Bathhouse B2: Invigorated status effect (+5% move speed, +10% stamina, 10 min)","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:0EzeT62tIfHkI2a-vfNYB66ButRwTksjivrd5qvkqqQ
1791857897177469	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-20gs	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: shared bathing (2+ players) lengthens it.\n\n# Goals\nWhen two or more players complete a sauna session in the same room, Bathed (and the following Invigorated) last longer, e.g. +25% per extra bather up to +50%.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nEncourages the social bath without complicating the solo case. Each client grants its own SE, so the head-count must come from synced state, not local guesses.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Count seated players per stove (stove ZDO owner writes a seated count, or each client counts Player list in the room).\n- Multiplier in Core with tests (cap).\n- Tooltip mentions \"Shared bath\".\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Two players sitting together each get the longer duration\n- [ ] Solo bathing unchanged\n- [ ] No desync when one leaves early\n\n# Dependencies\nb1rel\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nSocial play.\n","kind":"task","labels":["b2","bathhouse","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-33h","size":"s","title":"Bathhouse B2: shared bathing - 2+ players in the same sauna lengthen the buffs (multiplayer-safe)","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:RTrQb-P-tHYCK4hTFaWSy-CiZR8rpII4xkI7fjsGJLo
1791857897264214	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-8d5z	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone B2 of Bathhouse. Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, `mise run publish`, install, push dist.\n\n# Goals\nBathhouse 0.2.0 published with milestone B2 verified in the game.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nBob wants every change built, installed and released, and milestone acceptance checked live, not only in unit tests.\n\n# Implementation Approach\nTest in Bob's Creative world via the ClaudeTools mailbox (see claudetools-live-game memory): never lose Bob's gear, check `siege status` and Jarldom tribute before time jumps, tag test spawns and remove them by tag. Update the README playtest checklist with what was verified and what was not.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Sauna then sea dip: Invigorated\n- [ ] Sauna then tub: Invigorated\n- [ ] Two players: longer buffs\n- [ ] Unit tests pass\n- [ ] F6 reload clean\n- [ ] Version 0.2.0 in Plugin.cs, CHANGELOG entry, dist/manifest.json updated and pushed\n\n# Dependencies\nb2plunge, b2buff, b2shared\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nMilestone gate: the next milestone's work is blocked on this.\n","kind":"task","labels":["b2","bathhouse","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-33h","size":"s","title":"Bathhouse B2: live test in Creative + release Bathhouse 0.2.0","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:CgYfAA59kwp3-d6H4CbJe3hu2LbaZHAhMPmDajRBB7I
1791857897345908	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-398f	{"description":"# Context & Background\nGround rule: each standalone mod publishes a tiny `<Mod>.Api` static class Jarldom finds by reflection. Spec names `Bathhouse.Api.IsSauna(pos)`.\n\n# Goals\nA stable public static Api with `public const int Version = 1`.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nKeeps Jarldom free of a hard dependency; matches the foundation convention (bn-1xw).\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- mods/Bathhouse/Api.cs: `public static class Api { public const int Version = 1; public static bool IsSauna(Vector3 pos); public static Vector3[] SaunasNear(Vector3 pos, float r); public static void GrantBathed(Character c) /* for villagers if needed */ }`.\n- Reads the cached verdicts from B1.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Api compiles into the Bathhouse dll under namespace Bathhouse\n- [ ] Calls are cheap (cached) and never throw\n\n# Dependencies\nb2rel, bn-1xw\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nLets Jarldom see saunas.\n","kind":"task","labels":["b3","bathhouse","integration","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-33h","size":"s","title":"Bathhouse B3: Bathhouse.Api (Version, IsSauna(pos), maybe SaunasNear(pos, r)) for Jarldom","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:2UMX26U82dRxO7QlK1pGN5HO0JbI3vsEiK8zluMFGG8
1791857897428524	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-15do	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: Jarldom gets a Bathhouse room type (Beauty + Rested). Room types live in mods/Jarldom/Data/Tables.cs `enum RoomType` and Core/RoomRules.cs (Judge/Points).\n\n# Goals\nPlayers can designate a sauna as a Bathhouse room; it is judged and graded and adds Beauty and Rested to the colony.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nDetecting through Bathhouse.Api keeps Jarldom installable alone; without Bathhouse the room type is hidden.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Append RoomType.Bathhouse at the END of the enum (serialized as int) and raise Plugin.DataVersion if any record format changes.\n- RoomRules.Judge: valid if Bathhouse.Api.IsSauna(room centre) (via ApiRef); Points: Beauty + Rested contributions.\n- Designate/RoomEditor UI lists it only when Bathhouse is present.\n- Unit tests in tests/Jarldom.Tests for judge/points with fake facts.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] With Bathhouse installed, a sauna can be designated and grades\n- [ ] Without Bathhouse, the type is absent and nothing errors\n- [ ] Existing colonies load unchanged\n\n# Dependencies\nb3api, bn-1xw\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nNew room type for colony comfort.\n","kind":"task","labels":["b3","bathhouse","integration","jarldom","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-33h","size":"m","title":"Jarldom: Bathhouse room type (Beauty + Rested) via Bathhouse.Api, scored in room grades","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:IzapMcDBVzIEYmnTaVkbjVMe9la0UK5XtWVbe9Y1lmE
1791857897509241	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1td8	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: villagers bathe after work (mood +, Social +).\n\n# Goals\nAfter the work day, villagers with free time walk to the Bathhouse, sit on the bench for a bit, and gain a moodlet and Social need.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nFits the existing leisure system (Villager/Leisure.cs: tafl, glima, dummy, archery, stones, stroll, hall) as one more evening activity; bathing together feeds Social.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Leisure option \"bathe\" when a Bathhouse room exists and has a free bench seat; occupy seats (attach) like hall seats.\n- Moodlet \"Bathed\" (Data/Tables.cs moodlets) + Social gain scaled by others present.\n- Cap bathers to bench seats; don't block players' seats.\n- Doors handled by existing door logic.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Over an evening, villagers visit the sauna and get the moodlet\n- [ ] No villager gets stuck in the bathhouse (watchdog)\n- [ ] Perf unchanged at 40 villagers\n\n# Dependencies\nb3room\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nMakes colony life richer.\n","kind":"task","labels":["b3","bathhouse","integration","jarldom","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-33h","size":"m","title":"Jarldom: villagers bathe after work (mood +, Social +) in the colony's Bathhouse","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:K6PXAplmrF9cwh6zzTambAyusP_ml4BziMXXljHSmF4
1791857897596377	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3t81	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec says the Bathhouse answers the \"Build a sauna\" petition; no such petition exists in code yet (petitions: World/Events.cs, ColonyRecord.Petitions, Ui/ThingPanel.cs).\n\n# Goals\nVillagers occasionally petition for a sauna (only when Bathhouse is installed and none exists); building one resolves it with an opinion bump.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nTies the standalone mod into colony politics with a small, existing mechanism.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Add the petition template (text in Data/Tables.cs) gated on Api presence and no Bathhouse room.\n- Resolve automatically when a Bathhouse room is designated.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Petition appears only with Bathhouse installed and no bathhouse\n- [ ] Designating one resolves it and logs to the saga\n\n# Dependencies\nb3room\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nIntegration polish.\n","kind":"task","labels":["b3","bathhouse","integration","jarldom","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-33h","size":"s","title":"Jarldom: a 'Build a sauna' petition at the Thing, answered by a Bathhouse room","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:33eNKFjwbpvH2votzLp5XZcaeTJA33gatj27QPHoGuU
1791857897683961	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2b06	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone B3 of Bathhouse. Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, `mise run publish`, install, push dist.\n\n# Goals\nBathhouse 0.3.0 (+ Jarldom release) published with milestone B3 verified in the game.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nBob wants every change built, installed and released, and milestone acceptance checked live, not only in unit tests.\n\n# Implementation Approach\nTest in Bob's Creative world via the ClaudeTools mailbox (see claudetools-live-game memory): never lose Bob's gear, check `siege status` and Jarldom tribute before time jumps, tag test spawns and remove them by tag. Update the README playtest checklist with what was verified and what was not.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Designate a sauna as a Bathhouse room in the colony; villagers bathe after work\n- [ ] Sauna petition raised then answered\n- [ ] Jarldom alone (no Bathhouse) loads with no errors\n- [ ] Unit tests pass\n- [ ] F6 reload clean\n- [ ] Version 0.3.0 (+ Jarldom release) in Plugin.cs, CHANGELOG entry, dist/manifest.json updated and pushed\n\n# Dependencies\nb3api, b3room, b3bathe, b3petition\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nMilestone gate: the next milestone's work is blocked on this.\n","kind":"task","labels":["b3","bathhouse","jarldom","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-33h","size":"s","title":"Bathhouse B3: live test in Creative + release Bathhouse 0.3.0 (+ Jarldom release)","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:BXUbc9JrpnTR3QIUR5B5O-St0-0F_r-lSaEQwToNR0Q
1791857897768424	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-5xhx	{"description":"# Context & Background\nFirst task of the Byre mod (JARLDOM-NEXT.md). Standalone mods must be useful alone and expose a tiny `Byre.Api` that Jarldom finds by reflection; nothing exists yet. Spec section 3.2 (#59, #60): livestock - sheep, goats, cattle, geese, pigs.\n\n# Goals\nAn empty but buildable, testable, publishable Byre mod that every later Byre bone builds on.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nCopying the repo's existing small-mod layout keeps build/publish/test/manifest automatic and keeps every mod looking the same to Bob and to other agents.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- New project mods/Byre/ copied from a small mod's pattern (mods/Spyglass, mods/Delivery): Byre.csproj (net48, Directory.Build.props), Plugin.cs with `public const string Guid/Name/Version` (scripts/publish.py regexes these), Core/ for pure logic (no Unity), DESCRIPTION.txt, CHANGELOG.txt, cover.jpg, README with a playtest checklist.\n- tests/Byre.Tests console project linking Core/*.cs (same as tests/Spyglass.Tests/Program.cs style); wire into scripts/test.py if it enumerates projects.\n- mods/*/*.csproj is auto-discovered by scripts/build.py and scripts/publish.py, so `mise run build|test|publish|install` pick it up; publish writes the dist/manifest.json entry.\n- RESTART_REQUIRED.txt if pieces/items/recipes need a restart (see reload-levels memory / Quad's Claude Tools rules).\n- ServerSettings: server-authoritative config sync as in Jarldom/ServerSettings.cs.\n- A ClaudeTools command root (`byre ...`) registered like Jarldom/Tools/Tools.cs.\n- Prefab golden list tests/Byre.Tests/prefabs.txt per foundation bone bn-2vn (append-only; names prefixed Byre).\n- Read ~/repos/valheim-claude-tools/docs/modding-pitfalls.md first.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `mise run build` and `mise run test` pass with the new project\n- [ ] `mise run publish` lists Byre in dist/manifest.json (version 0.0.x, not announced)\n- [ ] F6 reload of Byre is clean (no errors, no leftover objects)\n- [ ] `byre help` answers through the ClaudeTools mailbox\n- [ ] Golden prefab list file and test exist (empty list ok)\n\n# Dependencies\nbn-2vn\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFoundation for every Byre milestone.\n","kind":"task","labels":["byre","next-saga","s1","standalone"],"parent":"bn-24c","size":"s","title":"Byre: scaffold the standalone mod project (csproj, Plugin, Core, tests, README, tools command, golden prefab list)"}	blake3:WAwGlCHzrJBOIg1H25WSTbOS7ZGB3iy8fQWevDWCNpw
1791857897855116	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2pv7	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSheep regrow wool after shearing; goats/cattle refill milk; animals eat from troughs; taming and procreation follow the game's own model.\n\n# Goals\nUnit-tested timers and rules every animal type reuses.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nPure logic first (ground rule) makes multiplayer/ZDO code thin: the ZDO stores timestamps, Core decides readiness.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Core/Husbandry.cs: `Ready(lastHarvest, now, period, fed)`; feed decay; yield by fed state; per-species table in Core/Species.cs (biome, wild herd size, tame food, yields, periods).\n- Times as game seconds (ZNet time), robust to sleep skips.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tests for regrowth, fed/unfed yields, sleep skip, species table sanity\n\n# Dependencies\nby0\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nShared base for all five species.\n","kind":"task","labels":["byre","next-saga","s1","standalone"],"parent":"bn-24c","size":"m","title":"Byre S1: pure herd rules in Core (shear/milk regrowth timers, trough feeding, taming, breeding caps) + tests"}	blake3:EEmI1UombHUG5-4PI0fVx03g3oW-ArH4derNOY8GekA
1791857897944109	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3nt1	{"description":"# Context & Background\nVanilla Valheim has no sheep or goats. Options: (a) re-skin/re-proportion an existing quadruped (deer, boar, lox) or (b) Blender model rigged to an existing creature skeleton so its animator works. Bob rejects visible kitbash shortcuts.\n\n# Goals\nBelievable sheep (shorn and woolly states) and goat models that play idle/walk/run/eat/death animations.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nRigging to an existing skeleton (deer for goat, boar-ish for sheep) reuses the animator controller and avoids a full anim set; the blender-anim-pipeline memory documents custom clips via JSON + bone override if needed.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Blender: model, weight to the chosen donor skeleton, export mesh; load as embedded asset like Jarldom's carved meshes (gzip JSON) or an AssetBundle.\n- Sheep wool state: separate fleece mesh toggled by a ZDO bool.\n- License note in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md if any external asset is used (CC0 only).\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Both animals animate correctly in all states\n- [ ] Sheep visibly shorn after shearing\n- [ ] Bob approves the look in game\n\n# Dependencies\nby0\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nVisual foundation for S1.\n","kind":"task","labels":["assets","byre","next-saga","s1","standalone"],"parent":"bn-24c","size":"m","title":"Byre S1: sheep and goat models + animations (Blender pipeline), no kitbash"}	blake3:prKeUszAru31BcdRO77RgysaGtb_qrJuwSyXhMXFONs
1791857898027324	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1z77	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: wild herds to tame in the right biomes; breeding with the game's procreation; goats climb steep slopes.\n\n# Goals\nPrefabs ByreSheep, ByreGoat cloned from a donor animal with Tameable/Procreation/AnimalAI, spawning as herds via SpawnSystem entries.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nUsing the game's Tameable + Procreation keeps behaviour familiar and compatible with taming mods.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Clone donor (boar/deer) prefab, swap visuals from s1models, set food items (grass? use vanilla items like dandelion/carrot/barley), drops (raw meat, hide/wool).\n- Goats: higher slope limit on the nav agent / Character m_maxSlope? (check), jumpier.\n- SpawnSystem: add entries for herds (Meadows sheep 2-4, Mountains goats 2-5), rare enough not to crowd.\n- Prefab names FOREVER; golden list.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Wild herds appear in the right biomes\n- [ ] Tame by feeding; tamed pairs breed\n- [ ] Goats walk slopes sheep/players can't easily climb\n\n# Dependencies\ns1core, s1models\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nThe animals themselves.\n","kind":"task","labels":["byre","next-saga","s1","standalone"],"parent":"bn-24c","size":"m","title":"Byre S1: sheep and goat creatures (Tameable, Procreation, animal AI, drops) + wild herd spawns (Meadows sheep, Mountains goats)"}	blake3:fXxNqQ-Ws696Rov-O8SEpb6GmvXPyYxe0fQ66ku9Ofc
1791857898110916	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-7p74	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: milk pail and shears; sheep shear -> wool, goats milk.\n\n# Goals\nTwo craftable tools; E with the tool on a tame animal harvests when ready, with hover showing readiness.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nInteraction via the animal's hover/Interact keeps it discoverable; readiness from Core rules.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Items ByreShears, ByreMilkPail (workbench recipes); outputs ByreWool, ByreGoatMilk (new items, names forever).\n- Hover: \"Wool: ready\" / \"regrows in N h\".\n- Store last-harvest time on the animal ZDO (small: one long).\n- Wool must be usable by Loom/Jarldom weaver later (note in the Api).\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Shear a tame sheep: wool drops, fleece mesh hides, regrows on schedule\n- [ ] Milk a tame goat with the pail: milk item\n- [ ] Wild animals can't be harvested\n\n# Dependencies\ns1creatures\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFirst real products.\n","kind":"task","labels":["byre","next-saga","s1","standalone"],"parent":"bn-24c","size":"m","title":"Byre S1: shears and milk pail items; shear sheep for wool, milk goats for milk (ZDO timers)"}	blake3:eaySLQmHPEtgMnN1zmMol-Yl8vy4Ey2svBHHz8CHMSE
1791857898197299	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-24mi	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: feeding troughs.\n\n# Goals\nA container-like piece that tame animals nearby eat from (like vanilla's feeding of tames from ground items).\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nSaves players dropping food on the floor; feeds the fed/unfed yield rule.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- ByreTrough piece with a Container (small); tames within ~10 m consume an item every N min when hungry (patch MonsterAI/AnimalAI food search to include trough contents, or a tick on the trough owner).\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tame animals eat from the trough\n- [ ] Fed animals yield per Core rules\n- [ ] Trough is a valid build piece with support/refund\n\n# Dependencies\ns1creatures\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nAnimal care loop.\n","kind":"task","labels":["byre","next-saga","s1","standalone"],"parent":"bn-24c","size":"s","title":"Byre S1: feeding trough piece (animals within range eat from it; fed state boosts yields)"}	blake3:F-trm6XLTlpUFHKAEenLTIHynjDL23Gnf4hqMrfjo4A
1791857898281580	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2ne7	{"description":"# Context & Background\nGround rule: tool commands for every system.\n\n# Goals\nInspect herds, spawn tame test animals (tagged), fast-forward readiness.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nLive tests without waiting days.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- `byre herds` nearby animals + state; `byre spawn sheep tame`; `byre ready` sets all timers ready; tag spawns for cleanup (test-tools-blast-radius memory: box-filter always).\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Commands return JSON; spawns are tagged and removable by tag only\n\n# Dependencies\ns1creatures\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nTestability.\n","kind":"task","labels":["byre","next-saga","s1","standalone"],"parent":"bn-24c","size":"s","title":"Byre S1: ClaudeTools commands (byre herds, byre spawn <species> [tame], byre ready, byre age)"}	blake3:J4-RiENalXLRj96b5OwTuOPM2n9WjvlyfgJJn4leSgw
1791857898370171	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3i19	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone S1 of Byre. Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, `mise run publish`, install, push dist.\n\n# Goals\nByre 0.1.0 published with milestone S1 verified in the game.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nBob wants every change built, installed and released, and milestone acceptance checked live, not only in unit tests.\n\n# Implementation Approach\nTest in Bob's Creative world via the ClaudeTools mailbox (see claudetools-live-game memory): never lose Bob's gear, check `siege status` and Jarldom tribute before time jumps, tag test spawns and remove them by tag. Update the README playtest checklist with what was verified and what was not.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tame a wild sheep and goat, breed them, shear and milk, feed from a trough\n- [ ] Unit tests pass\n- [ ] F6 reload clean\n- [ ] Version 0.1.0 in Plugin.cs, CHANGELOG entry, dist/manifest.json updated and pushed\n\n# Dependencies\ns1core, s1models, s1creatures, s1harvest, s1trough, s1tools\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nMilestone gate: the next milestone's work is blocked on this.\n","kind":"task","labels":["byre","next-saga","s1","standalone"],"parent":"bn-24c","size":"s","title":"Byre S1: live test in Creative + release Byre 0.1.0"}	blake3:Uj7vWA_oGUtxXM7E9uo07-qjGQHG4Oe1ygfoQi-U21c
1791857898455374	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-259w	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: cattle give milk and hides and pull a plow if Fields is installed.\n\n# Goals\nByreCow (and bull) with milking, hide drops, breeding, and an Api hook Fields can use to harness one to a plow.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nPlow pulling belongs to Fields/Horses harness code; Byre only exposes 'this animal can pull' via its Api.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Model (lox-scaled? no - real cow mesh via Blender on a donor skeleton), creature setup as S1.\n- Milk with pail (shared code), hides on slaughter.\n- Byre.Api.CanPull(Character) for Fields F2 plow / Horses R3.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Cattle spawn/tame/breed, milk and hides work\n- [ ] CanPull true for adult tame cattle\n\n# Dependencies\ns1rel\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nDairy and draft power.\n","kind":"task","labels":["byre","next-saga","s2","standalone"],"parent":"bn-24c","size":"m","title":"Byre S2: cattle (model, creature, milk, hides; plow-pull hook for Fields)"}	blake3:WhsfGwc3Z2uAOxrZMp5sQ5qTfhFt1LHbrB4bkqkoLYo
1791857898539305	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1308	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: geese lay eggs, give feathers, and chase strangers.\n\n# Goals\nByreGoose that lays eggs near its home, drops feathers, and honks/charges at non-tamed creatures and unfamiliar players (harmless or tiny damage).\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nGives an early-game feather source and a comic guard animal.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Small bird model on a donor (hen exists in vanilla since Ashlands? check: Hen / Chicken exist with eggs - reuse heavily).\n- 'Stranger' = player not on the tamer's list / not the owner's group; chase = short aggro with no damage (or 1).\n- Egg laying timer via Core.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Eggs appear over time\n- [ ] Feathers drop\n- [ ] Geese chase a stranger and stop at range\n\n# Dependencies\ns1rel\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nVariety and fun.\n","kind":"task","labels":["byre","next-saga","s2","standalone"],"parent":"bn-24c","size":"m","title":"Byre S2: geese (eggs, feathers; chase strangers)"}	blake3:93jsRtw1RX4Rss-ojk1kt8uusQwCzisNIVv3A5SQWyI
1791857898625963	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-vc0i	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: pigs (bred from tamed boars; truffles in the Black Forest).\n\n# Goals\nTamed boar pairs in a pen produce piglets that grow into ByrePig (domestic look); pigs led into the Black Forest occasionally root up a truffle item.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nBuilds on a vanilla tame everyone already has; truffles give a reason to take animals out.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Patch Procreation of tame boars: offspring prefab ByrePiglet (with a chance, or after N generations).\n- Truffle: while a tame pig is in BlackForest biome and following, roll per minute -> drop ByreTruffle (food ingredient).\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tame boars produce pigs\n- [ ] Pigs in the Black Forest find truffles at a sensible rate\n\n# Dependencies\ns1rel\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFood variety.\n","kind":"task","labels":["byre","next-saga","s2","standalone"],"parent":"bn-24c","size":"m","title":"Byre S2: pigs bred from tamed boars; truffles dug up in the Black Forest"}	blake3:RwPpBu9VhYJeMdnBNWNECATjgHvyRmG0XmVBTMqrBMU
1791857898717382	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2mpi	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone S2 of Byre. Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, `mise run publish`, install, push dist.\n\n# Goals\nByre 0.2.0 published with milestone S2 verified in the game.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nBob wants every change built, installed and released, and milestone acceptance checked live, not only in unit tests.\n\n# Implementation Approach\nTest in Bob's Creative world via the ClaudeTools mailbox (see claudetools-live-game memory): never lose Bob's gear, check `siege status` and Jarldom tribute before time jumps, tag test spawns and remove them by tag. Update the README playtest checklist with what was verified and what was not.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Cattle milked, geese lay and chase, pigs bred and truffle in the Black Forest\n- [ ] Unit tests pass\n- [ ] F6 reload clean\n- [ ] Version 0.2.0 in Plugin.cs, CHANGELOG entry, dist/manifest.json updated and pushed\n\n# Dependencies\ns2cattle, s2geese, s2pigs\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nMilestone gate: the next milestone's work is blocked on this.\n","kind":"task","labels":["byre","next-saga","s2","standalone"],"parent":"bn-24c","size":"s","title":"Byre S2: live test in Creative + release Byre 0.2.0"}	blake3:m5kfURCz-ffpo0l5TNtMgRJJUq4xpSzxj1Kq1DjmitA
1791857898802868	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-tnn3	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: a stall barn piece set.\n\n# Goals\nStall dividers, stall gate (door), hay rack/manger, and a barn floor that animals stay in.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nPens today are fences; stalls make a Norse byre (longhouse animal end) buildable and recognisable by Jarldom's Byre room.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Pieces with WearNTear support values and snap points matching vanilla 1 m/2 m grids; gate as a Door.\n- Models: Blender (no floating planks).\n- Names forever.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Pieces snap to vanilla walls/floors\n- [ ] Stall gate opens/closes for players, animals don't path through it\n\n# Dependencies\ns2rel\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nBuilding block for the Byre room.\n","kind":"task","labels":["byre","next-saga","s3","standalone"],"parent":"bn-24c","size":"m","title":"Byre S3: stall barn piece set (stalls, gates, hay rack) with snap points and support"}	blake3:XzHIlB6a1U1X9s49kdCeIy1C5IQYbuEa_qoKxFR_4vA
1791857898887879	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-erc9	{"description":"# Context & Background\nGround rule Api; Jarldom herders/dairymaids, Fields (manure, plow), Larder (dairy), Hounds (herding dogs) all read Byre through it.\n\n# Goals\nStable reflection-friendly static Api with Version = 1.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nOne Api serves every consumer and keeps them optional.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- `bool IsLivestock(Character)`, `bool CanPull(Character)`, `string[] Ready(Character)` (wool/milk/eggs), `bool Harvest(Character animal, Humanoid by, out ItemDrop.ItemData item)`, `Character[] HerdsNear(Vector3, float)`, `bool IsStall(Vector3)`.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Api documented in the README and stable\n- [ ] Harvest works when called for a non-player Humanoid (villager)\n\n# Dependencies\ns2rel, bn-1xw\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nIntegration point.\n","kind":"task","labels":["byre","integration","next-saga","s3","standalone"],"parent":"bn-24c","size":"s","title":"Byre S3: Byre.Api (Version, IsLivestock, CanPull, Products, HerdsNear, Harvest(animal) for villagers)"}	blake3:7e-ntXJBlNDDrOTrOAlD0snq2A8S-j0Q03KQuEBeFzc
1791857898972245	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3gvi	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: a Byre room type (the longhouse's animal end: stalls + trough + roof), whose warmth adds +1 comfort to a longhouse that shares a wall with it, as historically.\n\n# Goals\nByre rooms recognised and graded; adjacent longhouses get +1 comfort.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nHistorical longhouses kept animals at one end for warmth; rewarding it nudges authentic layouts.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Append RoomType.Byre to Data/Tables.cs enum (end), Judge in Core/RoomRules.cs via Byre.Api.IsStall + trough present + roofed.\n- Shared wall: rooms are measured outlines; adjacency = outlines touching along >= 2 m (pure geometry in Core with tests).\n- Comfort +1 for the longhouse's sleepers.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Byre room designatable and graded with Byre installed; absent without\n- [ ] A longhouse sharing a wall shows +1 comfort; one 3 m away doesn't\n- [ ] Tests for adjacency\n\n# Dependencies\ns3api, s3barn, bn-1xw\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nColony room depth.\n","kind":"task","labels":["byre","integration","jarldom","next-saga","s3","standalone"],"parent":"bn-24c","size":"m","title":"Jarldom: Byre room type (stalls + trough + roof) and +1 comfort to a longhouse sharing a wall with it"}	blake3:t5igT8F81kiSJ3ODFFw3-VB_kAwIOxweJ3kMWJD4acM
1791857899052399	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2441	{"description":"# Context & Background\nJarldom has a Herder profession and Pasture zone (vanilla animals). Spec: herder and dairymaid work; wool -> the weaver; dairy -> the cook.\n\n# Goals\nHerders tend Byre animals; a dairymaid (new profession or herder sub-role) milks; products go to stockpiles where the weaver and cook pick them up.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nProducts through stockpiles reuses the existing hauling/stock system (Colony/Stock.cs).\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Villager/Work.cs: harvest tasks via Byre.Api.Ready/Harvest within Pasture zones.\n- Profession table entry for dairymaid (Data/Tables.cs) or extend herder.\n- Weaver (Villager/Weaving.cs) accepts ByreWool as input; Cook recipes accept milk (later Larder dairy).\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Herders shear and milk without player help\n- [ ] Wool reaches the weaver and becomes cloth\n- [ ] Milk reaches the cook's stores\n\n# Dependencies\ns3api, bn-1xw\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFeeds the colony economy.\n","kind":"task","labels":["byre","integration","jarldom","next-saga","s3","standalone"],"parent":"bn-24c","size":"m","title":"Jarldom: herder and dairymaid work on Byre animals (shear, milk, collect eggs; wool to the weaver, dairy to the cook)"}	blake3:XNkbVACq_Smp0OglF3NBmS7zn-Z9iN5GqVTUQGlrL8g
1791857899137971	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-6gty	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone S3 of Byre. Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, `mise run publish`, install, push dist.\n\n# Goals\nByre 0.3.0 (+ Jarldom release) published with milestone S3 verified in the game.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nBob wants every change built, installed and released, and milestone acceptance checked live, not only in unit tests.\n\n# Implementation Approach\nTest in Bob's Creative world via the ClaudeTools mailbox (see claudetools-live-game memory): never lose Bob's gear, check `siege status` and Jarldom tribute before time jumps, tag test spawns and remove them by tag. Update the README playtest checklist with what was verified and what was not.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Build a byre end on a longhouse: room recognised, +1 comfort next door\n- [ ] Herder shears and milks, weaver uses the wool\n- [ ] Unit tests pass\n- [ ] F6 reload clean\n- [ ] Version 0.3.0 (+ Jarldom release) in Plugin.cs, CHANGELOG entry, dist/manifest.json updated and pushed\n\n# Dependencies\ns3barn, s3api, s3room, s3work\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nMilestone gate: the next milestone's work is blocked on this.\n","kind":"task","labels":["byre","jarldom","next-saga","s3","standalone"],"parent":"bn-24c","size":"s","title":"Byre S3: live test in Creative + release Byre 0.3.0 (+ Jarldom release)"}	blake3:9_nMZ6xAKZCjup6gTJU6-1oray82n5tQ_6EiZzX7mMM
1791857899219610	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1pjh	{"description":"# Context & Background\nFirst task of the BuildKit mod (JARLDOM-NEXT.md). Standalone mods must be useful alone and expose a tiny `BuildKit.Api` that Jarldom finds by reflection; nothing exists yet. Spec section 3.7 (#73): Viking building kit (working name; rename freely before the first public release - prefab names, once released, are forever).\n\n# Goals\nAn empty but buildable, testable, publishable BuildKit mod that every later BuildKit bone builds on.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nCopying the repo's existing small-mod layout keeps build/publish/test/manifest automatic and keeps every mod looking the same to Bob and to other agents.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- New project mods/BuildKit/ copied from a small mod's pattern (mods/Spyglass, mods/Delivery): BuildKit.csproj (net48, Directory.Build.props), Plugin.cs with `public const string Guid/Name/Version` (scripts/publish.py regexes these), Core/ for pure logic (no Unity), DESCRIPTION.txt, CHANGELOG.txt, cover.jpg, README with a playtest checklist.\n- tests/BuildKit.Tests console project linking Core/*.cs (same as tests/Spyglass.Tests/Program.cs style); wire into scripts/test.py if it enumerates projects.\n- mods/*/*.csproj is auto-discovered by scripts/build.py and scripts/publish.py, so `mise run build|test|publish|install` pick it up; publish writes the dist/manifest.json entry.\n- RESTART_REQUIRED.txt if pieces/items/recipes need a restart (see reload-levels memory / Quad's Claude Tools rules).\n- ServerSettings: server-authoritative config sync as in Jarldom/ServerSettings.cs.\n- A ClaudeTools command root (`kit ...`) registered like Jarldom/Tools/Tools.cs.\n- Prefab golden list tests/BuildKit.Tests/prefabs.txt per foundation bone bn-2vn (append-only; names prefixed BuildKit).\n- Read ~/repos/valheim-claude-tools/docs/modding-pitfalls.md first.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `mise run build` and `mise run test` pass with the new project\n- [ ] `mise run publish` lists BuildKit in dist/manifest.json (version 0.0.x, not announced)\n- [ ] F6 reload of BuildKit is clean (no errors, no leftover objects)\n- [ ] `kit help` answers through the ClaudeTools mailbox\n- [ ] Golden prefab list file and test exist (empty list ok)\n\n# Dependencies\nbn-2vn\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFoundation for every BuildKit milestone.\n","kind":"task","labels":["buildkit","k1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3ik","size":"s","title":"BuildKit: scaffold the standalone mod project (csproj, Plugin, Core, tests, README, tools command, golden prefab list)"}	blake3:ylKK_kr9v4CITALkAUYh2OiekCavmR201p7pnXiQYqc
1791857899303818	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2ct4	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: turf roofs (sod on birch bark, insulating: +comfort under it).\n\n# Goals\nA turf roof family that snaps like vanilla roofs and gives +1 comfort to anyone under it.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nTurf is the iconic Norse roof; comfort under it gives a mechanical reason over thatch. Real models (Blender) - Bob rejected floating-plank kitbashes.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Pieces: turf roof 26, 45, ridge, top, corner/inner corner, edge trims; 2x2 m grid matching vanilla roof snap points.\n- WearNTear: wood-like support; roof tag so Cover counts it (not 'leaky').\n- Comfort: piece with a comfort group? Vanilla comfort comes from pieces in range; implement +1 as a check \"is the player under turf\" (raycast up) in the rested comfort calc.\n- Materials: wood + 'sod' (dirt? use vanilla items: wood, stone, maybe resin) - tune.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Snaps to vanilla walls/roofs both ways\n- [ ] Support values tested with a long span (wood_roof shed roofs over 12 m collapsed in Jarldom tests - match vanilla behaviour)\n- [ ] Cover/rain protection works\n- [ ] +1 comfort shown under turf\n\n# Dependencies\nbk0\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nSignature piece of the kit.\n","kind":"task","labels":["buildkit","k1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3ik","size":"m","title":"Building kit K1: turf roof pieces (sod on birch bark; 26/45 degree, ridge, edges) that insulate (+comfort under them)"}	blake3:po6bh_R0L_h1t3MPv3kmyiyF4fbk-F_FTPC0iuHqhnQ
1791857899384319	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-192o	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: wall benches (sleep on them: bed-tier comfort). Longhouses had raised benches along the walls used as beds.\n\n# Goals\nA bench piece along a wall that acts as a Bed (spawn point, sleep) and as a seat, with bed-tier comfort.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nLets players build authentic longhouses; Jarldom later treats them as longhouse beds (K4c).\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Bench with Bed component (sleep, set spawn) and a Chair attach; comfort group 'bed' with value like the vanilla bed.\n- Snap along walls; length 2 m.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Sleep and set spawn on a bench\n- [ ] Comfort counts as a bed tier\n- [ ] Sit works too\n\n# Dependencies\nbk0\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nAuthentic sleeping halls.\n","kind":"task","labels":["buildkit","k1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3ik","size":"m","title":"Building kit K1: wall benches you can sleep on (bed-tier comfort)"}	blake3:sR6eUtaAom3Ajabk-lLoiV-Ax7cTV_MJxpQWGVJ8VUs
1791857899468871	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-wb1c	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: smoke-hole roof pieces (vent a hearth with no chimney). Vanilla fires choke indoors without an opening (Smoke particles collide and 'smoke' damage).\n\n# Goals\nA roof piece with an opening that clears smoke, so central hearths work under turf/thatch roofs.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nVanilla smoke uses physical smoke objects blocked by colliders; an opening in the mesh/collider is the honest fix.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Roof piece variants with a hole and a raised louvre; collider shaped so Smoke objects rise through; verify Fireplace m_smokeSpawner behaviour.\n- Test: hearth under turf roof + smoke-hole doesn't choke.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A hearth under a smoke-hole burns indefinitely without the 'smoke' warning\n- [ ] Rain cover still counts around the hole\n\n# Dependencies\nbk0\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nLets longhouses have central fires (Bathhouse stove needs it too).\n","kind":"task","labels":["buildkit","k1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3ik","size":"m","title":"Building kit K1: smoke-hole roof pieces that vent a hearth with no chimney"}	blake3:xkvZ2sHeogrtPu89Mkblu_gcnC_GIeYqeUGari0s41M
1791857899557023	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-d660	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: all pieces with proper snap points and support values. Many pieces across K1-K3 need the same checks.\n\n# Goals\nA tool command that places each kit piece in a test pad and reports snap points, support propagation and cover.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nAutomating the check makes every later piece cheaper to verify and catches bad support values before Bob builds with them.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- `kit test all|<piece>` in a box-filtered area; report JSON; cleanup by tag.\n- Golden prefab list maintained.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Command reports for every kit piece\n- [ ] Leaves nothing behind\n\n# Dependencies\nbk0\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nQuality gate for all milestones.\n","kind":"task","labels":["buildkit","k1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3ik","size":"s","title":"Building kit K1: snap/support test command (kit test <piece>: snap points, support chain, cover) + golden prefab list"}	blake3:PjChPAuKKH-q98ueUHACTT_5Kqhz8m48cchupKjZUGM
1791857899639614	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-15va	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone K1 of BuildKit. Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, `mise run publish`, install, push dist.\n\n# Goals\nBuildKit 0.1.0 published with milestone K1 verified in the game.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nBob wants every change built, installed and released, and milestone acceptance checked live, not only in unit tests.\n\n# Implementation Approach\nTest in Bob's Creative world via the ClaudeTools mailbox (see claudetools-live-game memory): never lose Bob's gear, check `siege status` and Jarldom tribute before time jumps, tag test spawns and remove them by tag. Update the README playtest checklist with what was verified and what was not.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Build a small turf longhouse with wall benches and a smoke-hole over a central hearth; sleep there\n- [ ] Unit tests pass\n- [ ] F6 reload clean\n- [ ] Version 0.1.0 in Plugin.cs, CHANGELOG entry, dist/manifest.json updated and pushed\n\n# Dependencies\nk1turf, k1bench, k1smoke, k1check\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nMilestone gate: the next milestone's work is blocked on this.\n","kind":"task","labels":["buildkit","k1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3ik","size":"s","title":"BuildKit K1: live test in Creative + release BuildKit 0.1.0"}	blake3:J6fD5ePPdnCmi8OGsi7q1Mo4NhYhqCa6InRujNMMEDE
1791857899722177	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2c9j	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: stave-church pieces (staves, carved portals, shingle roofs).\n\n# Goals\nCorner staves, wall planks (stave wall), sill beams and carved dragon-style portals.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nThe stave church is the other iconic Norse building; needed for the Hallwright stave-church temple style (K4).\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Blender models with real carving (Jarldom's carve pipeline: mods/Jarldom/Models/carve/carve.py shows boolean carving into game meshes).\n- Support: staves as poles (high support), walls as wood.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Pieces snap to each other and vanilla\n- [ ] Carved portal is a working Door\n\n# Dependencies\nk1rel\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nTemple architecture.\n","kind":"task","labels":["buildkit","k2","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3ik","size":"m","title":"Building kit K2: stave-church staves and carved portals"}	blake3:wQy9lSWC-CUkycPGJHrG4RV4oSCjEn1YDjZxQ9xBobw
1791857899809991	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2b0w	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: shingle roofs for the stave church.\n\n# Goals\nSteep shingle roof family with ridge and finials.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nStave churches use steep stacked roofs; vanilla has no 60-degree roof.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Pieces 45/60 deg, ridge, finial; roof tag for Cover; snap to staves.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Snaps and covers\n- [ ] Supports a multi-tier roof\n\n# Dependencies\nk1rel\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nCompletes the church.\n","kind":"task","labels":["buildkit","k2","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3ik","size":"m","title":"Building kit K2: shingle roofs (steep 45/60 degree, ridge with dragon finials)"}	blake3:QIRrmtXnbjc25_pPpXk90njJTV3oxX9hV6OcYAW8hpQ
1791857899898035	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-fwg4	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone K2 of BuildKit. Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, `mise run publish`, install, push dist.\n\n# Goals\nBuildKit 0.2.0 published with milestone K2 verified in the game.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nBob wants every change built, installed and released, and milestone acceptance checked live, not only in unit tests.\n\n# Implementation Approach\nTest in Bob's Creative world via the ClaudeTools mailbox (see claudetools-live-game memory): never lose Bob's gear, check `siege status` and Jarldom tribute before time jumps, tag test spawns and remove them by tag. Update the README playtest checklist with what was verified and what was not.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Build a small stave church with a carved portal and shingle roof\n- [ ] Unit tests pass\n- [ ] F6 reload clean\n- [ ] Version 0.2.0 in Plugin.cs, CHANGELOG entry, dist/manifest.json updated and pushed\n\n# Dependencies\nk2staves, k2shingle\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nMilestone gate: the next milestone's work is blocked on this.\n","kind":"task","labels":["buildkit","k2","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3ik","size":"s","title":"BuildKit K2: live test in Creative + release BuildKit 0.2.0"}	blake3:u8L71jj3nrTzqVEE1KNGaBmutVWrfzg4GP0uZgjr0to
1791857899985779	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-29z7	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: wattle fences and walls.\n\n# Goals\nWoven fence and wall pieces (cheap, low support).\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nCheap early walls and pasture fences that look right next to Byre pens.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Models, snap points, low WearNTear support; fence works as a pen boundary for animals.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Fences block tame animals\n- [ ] Walls snap to vanilla\n\n# Dependencies\nk2rel\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nDetail.\n","kind":"task","labels":["buildkit","k3","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3ik","size":"s","title":"Building kit K3: wattle fences and wattle-and-daub walls"}	blake3:YylaoLQiMiUMQcCrqB0mtArYkk8fkBbPgEJ3ymdFYqQ
1791857900074270	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1seu	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: granary on stilts.\n\n# Goals\nA storehouse piece raised on posts with a chest inside.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nHistorical stabbur; Hounds' cats and Larder spoilage can treat it as dry storage later.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Piece with Container (size like a reinforced chest); Classes so Jarldom counts it as storage.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Usable container\n- [ ] Snaps on uneven ground\n\n# Dependencies\nk2rel\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nStorage with character.\n","kind":"task","labels":["buildkit","k3","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3ik","size":"s","title":"Building kit K3: granary on stilts (container piece raised on posts)"}	blake3:xUseBvD96T_JFIhfd2BLwxM7NUoXWXsAILvfDL2RumQ
1791857900158699	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1hsq	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: market stalls.\n\n# Goals\nDecorative/functional stall pieces (counter with a small container).\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nJarldom traders/visitors can stand at them later; Beauty for plazas.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Models, snap points; optional item display on the counter (ItemStand-like slots).\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Placeable, snaps, holds a few items\n\n# Dependencies\nk2rel\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nTown life.\n","kind":"task","labels":["buildkit","k3","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3ik","size":"s","title":"Building kit K3: market stalls (awning + counter)"}	blake3:4Y68lTCvfcspk2oydaRYm7axi5SmkWYokZyyz-ioJ2E
1791857900238781	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-28q4	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: shutters, carved door frames, runic lintels.\n\n# Goals\nWindow shutters (open/close), carved door frames around vanilla doors, lintels with runes (static; Runecarver later can make custom text).\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nSmall details make room grades and Hallwright output look finished.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Shutters as Door-like pieces (note: Jarldom room measuring treats shutters as not-doors; keep that working).\n- Lintel: fixed rune inscription carved via the Blender carve pipeline.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Shutters open/close and don't count as doors in Jarldom rooms\n- [ ] Frames snap around vanilla doors\n\n# Dependencies\nk2rel\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nPolish.\n","kind":"task","labels":["buildkit","k3","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3ik","size":"m","title":"Building kit K3: shutters, carved door frames and runic lintels"}	blake3:BKx4By-omBSinFaiFpC0rZDvuYe3LDMTQdUILcbF2Ic
1791857900328135	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3vyr	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone K3 of BuildKit. Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, `mise run publish`, install, push dist.\n\n# Goals\nBuildKit 0.3.0 published with milestone K3 verified in the game.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nBob wants every change built, installed and released, and milestone acceptance checked live, not only in unit tests.\n\n# Implementation Approach\nTest in Bob's Creative world via the ClaudeTools mailbox (see claudetools-live-game memory): never lose Bob's gear, check `siege status` and Jarldom tribute before time jumps, tag test spawns and remove them by tag. Update the README playtest checklist with what was verified and what was not.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Build a market corner with stalls, a granary and shuttered windows\n- [ ] Unit tests pass\n- [ ] F6 reload clean\n- [ ] Version 0.3.0 in Plugin.cs, CHANGELOG entry, dist/manifest.json updated and pushed\n\n# Dependencies\nk3wattle, k3granary, k3market, k3details\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nMilestone gate: the next milestone's work is blocked on this.\n","kind":"task","labels":["buildkit","k3","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3ik","size":"s","title":"BuildKit K3: live test in Creative + release BuildKit 0.3.0"}	blake3:f8ZXSAn9_I3BrK58OgUHFflHJdE828tAyinhKeYBZl0
1791857900415351	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2n27	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: Hallwright (mods/BuildShapes) adds the kit to its material styles: turf longhouse.\n\n# Goals\nWhen BuildKit is installed, Hallwright offers a turf-longhouse style that lays turf roofs, wall benches and a smoke-hole.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nHallwright generates buildings; using kit pieces makes them authentic. Optional dependency by prefab lookup (ZNetScene.GetPrefab returns null when absent) or a BuildKit.Api.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Find where BuildShapes defines material styles; add a style entry gated on prefab existence.\n- Tests in tests/Hallwright.Tests for the style's piece mapping.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Style listed only with BuildKit installed\n- [ ] Generated longhouse uses turf roof + benches + smoke-hole and stands (support)\n\n# Dependencies\nk3rel\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nKit reaches players who build with Hallwright.\n","kind":"task","labels":["buildkit","buildshapes","hallwright","integration","k4","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3ik","size":"m","title":"Hallwright K4: 'turf longhouse' material style using the kit (optional when the kit is present)"}	blake3:S1dHnQ4oawtGhpY1vDM1Dr3-7c8RzojEkxhCUK6Ss8s
1791857900503055	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3sn6	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: stave church temple style.\n\n# Goals\nA Hallwright style that builds a temple from staves, portal and shingle roofs.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nGives Jarldom temples an authentic look via the same generator.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- As k4turf, mapping walls->staves, roof->shingle, door->carved portal.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Generated temple stands and is recognised by Jarldom as a temple room\n\n# Dependencies\nk3rel\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nTemples.\n","kind":"task","labels":["buildkit","buildshapes","hallwright","integration","k4","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3ik","size":"m","title":"Hallwright K4: 'stave church temple' material style"}	blake3:DeUYLEyr5eRD2tt_fG0QDPxbxeXok4fdS7acbVoFBMs
1791857900589389	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-i4ld	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: Jarldom gets more pieces for room grades; wall benches as longhouse beds. Colony/Classes.cs decides what a piece is for the whole mod.\n\n# Goals\nClasses recognises kit pieces (bench = bed, granary = storage, carved portal = door, turf = roof) so rooms grade higher and villagers sleep on benches.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nPrefab-name based classes with no hard dependency.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Add kit prefab names to Classes (bed, seat, storage, beauty) and AutoBeds; tests in tests/Jarldom.Tests (one test per class exists).\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Villagers claim and sleep on wall benches\n- [ ] Turf/stave pieces raise room grade beauty\n\n# Dependencies\nk3rel, bn-1xw\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nColony integration.\n","kind":"task","labels":["buildkit","integration","jarldom","k4","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3ik","size":"s","title":"Jarldom: kit pieces count in room grades (Colony/Classes.cs), wall benches as longhouse beds"}	blake3:CK7m_HAp4h1VY5KqaQjHZ3UTki79QlSOGJ9TRYz5Dic
1791857900670550	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3njo	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone K4 of BuildKit. Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, `mise run publish`, install, push dist.\n\n# Goals\nBuildKit 0.4.0 (+ Hallwright, Jarldom releases) published with milestone K4 verified in the game.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nBob wants every change built, installed and released, and milestone acceptance checked live, not only in unit tests.\n\n# Implementation Approach\nTest in Bob's Creative world via the ClaudeTools mailbox (see claudetools-live-game memory): never lose Bob's gear, check `siege status` and Jarldom tribute before time jumps, tag test spawns and remove them by tag. Update the README playtest checklist with what was verified and what was not.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Hallwright builds a turf longhouse; villagers sleep on its benches\n- [ ] Unit tests pass\n- [ ] F6 reload clean\n- [ ] Version 0.4.0 (+ Hallwright, Jarldom releases) in Plugin.cs, CHANGELOG entry, dist/manifest.json updated and pushed\n\n# Dependencies\nk4turf, k4church, k4jarldom\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nMilestone gate: the next milestone's work is blocked on this.\n","kind":"task","labels":["buildkit","hallwright","jarldom","k4","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3ik","size":"s","title":"BuildKit K4: live test in Creative + release BuildKit 0.4.0 (+ Hallwright, Jarldom releases)"}	blake3:mUSjcl9ugD0tB08AoEwWR3bwf-0VIXn5PLWPzwk5PZ0
1791857900755132	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-39i0	{"description":"# Context & Background\nFirst task of the Shipyard mod (JARLDOM-NEXT.md). Standalone mods must be useful alone and expose a tiny `Shipyard.Api` that Jarldom finds by reflection; nothing exists yet. Spec section 3.8 (#74, #75): slipway with staged builds, faering, knarr, boathouse. Built just before J6.\n\n# Goals\nAn empty but buildable, testable, publishable Shipyard mod that every later Shipyard bone builds on.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nCopying the repo's existing small-mod layout keeps build/publish/test/manifest automatic and keeps every mod looking the same to Bob and to other agents.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- New project mods/Shipyard/ copied from a small mod's pattern (mods/Spyglass, mods/Delivery): Shipyard.csproj (net48, Directory.Build.props), Plugin.cs with `public const string Guid/Name/Version` (scripts/publish.py regexes these), Core/ for pure logic (no Unity), DESCRIPTION.txt, CHANGELOG.txt, cover.jpg, README with a playtest checklist.\n- tests/Shipyard.Tests console project linking Core/*.cs (same as tests/Spyglass.Tests/Program.cs style); wire into scripts/test.py if it enumerates projects.\n- mods/*/*.csproj is auto-discovered by scripts/build.py and scripts/publish.py, so `mise run build|test|publish|install` pick it up; publish writes the dist/manifest.json entry.\n- RESTART_REQUIRED.txt if pieces/items/recipes need a restart (see reload-levels memory / Quad's Claude Tools rules).\n- ServerSettings: server-authoritative config sync as in Jarldom/ServerSettings.cs.\n- A ClaudeTools command root (`yard ...`) registered like Jarldom/Tools/Tools.cs.\n- Prefab golden list tests/Shipyard.Tests/prefabs.txt per foundation bone bn-2vn (append-only; names prefixed Shipyard).\n- Read ~/repos/valheim-claude-tools/docs/modding-pitfalls.md first.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `mise run build` and `mise run test` pass with the new project\n- [ ] `mise run publish` lists Shipyard in dist/manifest.json (version 0.0.x, not announced)\n- [ ] F6 reload of Shipyard is clean (no errors, no leftover objects)\n- [ ] `yard help` answers through the ClaudeTools mailbox\n- [ ] Golden prefab list file and test exist (empty list ok)\n\n# Dependencies\nbn-2vn\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFoundation for every Shipyard milestone.\n","kind":"task","labels":["n1","next-saga","shipyard","standalone"],"parent":"bn-2n2","size":"s","title":"Shipyard: scaffold the standalone mod project (csproj, Plugin, Core, tests, README, tools command, golden prefab list)"}	blake3:dyvRdLT5WLolkC89k4EfdWUFFcYVmJRZbiI2s7I58kY
1791857900846819	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2omx	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: ships built in visible stages, each stage paid in full (modding pitfall: partial payment paths lose items), buildable by several players.\n\n# Goals\nA Core state machine: hull type -> stage list with costs; contributions add to a stage's pot; a stage completes only when fully paid and materials are consumed atomically.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nThe pitfalls doc lists item-loss bugs from partial payments; making 'pay in full or nothing' a tested invariant prevents them.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Core/Stages.cs: `Stage[] For(hull)`, `Contribute(state, item, count) -> accepted`, `CanAdvance(state)`; state serialisable to a small byte[] on the slipway ZDO.\n- Owner-authoritative: clients send contributions by RPC; owner validates and removes items only after acceptance (or refunds).\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tests: overpay refused/refunded, two contributors, advance only when full, serialization round-trip\n- [ ] No path removes items without crediting them\n\n# Dependencies\nsy0\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nCorrectness core.\n","kind":"task","labels":["n1","next-saga","shipyard","standalone"],"parent":"bn-2n2","size":"m","title":"Shipyard N1: pure staged-build state machine (keel -> ribs -> strakes -> deck -> mast), each stage paid IN FULL, multi-player contributions + tests"}	blake3:F116RrcOgbFHNRXee0mT-YD8yiRlwchz0YaI0Y0Hjv8
1791857900932323	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2ihv	{"description":"# Context & Background\nThe slipway shows the ship growing stage by stage.\n\n# Goals\nA slipway piece placed at the shore; child visuals per stage switch on as stages complete.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nStage meshes can be derived from the game's karve/longship meshes in Blender (keel only, ribs, etc.) via `jarldom dumpmesh`-style export (memory: dump into BepInEx/claude dir); real meshes, no floating planks.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Slipway: ramp into water, snap to ground; hover shows current stage and missing materials.\n- Per hull: 5 stage GameObjects enabled by stage index from the ZDO.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each stage visibly different\n- [ ] Hover lists remaining materials\n- [ ] Placeable only at a shore (water within N m)\n\n# Dependencies\nsy0\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nThe visible heart of the mod.\n","kind":"task","labels":["assets","n1","next-saga","shipyard","standalone"],"parent":"bn-2n2","size":"m","title":"Shipyard N1: slipway piece + stage visuals (keel, ribs, strakes, deck, mast meshes per hull)"}	blake3:UK1kOOWVbgRQux2H3ibWAnjICTIXA_ecC8DWvoc7ZTI
1791857901022504	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-cqx9	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSeveral players build together; the slipway ZDO owner is authoritative.\n\n# Goals\nE to choose a hull (when empty); E with materials to contribute; works for multiple players at once without dupes or losses.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nOwner validation by RPC mirrors Jarldom's Jarldom_Act pattern (actions routed to the owner).\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- RPC Shipyard_Contribute(item, count): owner applies Core.Contribute, replies accepted count; client removes exactly that many.\n- Disconnect mid-contribution: no loss (client only removes after reply).\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Two players contribute simultaneously; totals correct\n- [ ] Kill the client mid-RPC: no item loss\n\n# Dependencies\nn1core, n1slipway\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nMultiplayer safety.\n","kind":"task","labels":["n1","next-saga","shipyard","standalone"],"parent":"bn-2n2","size":"m","title":"Shipyard N1: slipway interaction and networking (choose hull, contribute from inventory, owner validation, any player can help)"}	blake3:vChVOww7ndYYczFsR1Uk_OmD8Sq5aV1J2mCgHvbGBYU
1791857901110972	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-if10	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: new hull faering, a fast little rowboat.\n\n# Goals\nA ShipyardFaering ship prefab (2 seats, small cargo, fast rowing) launched into the water when the mast/last stage completes.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nA small first hull proves the whole pipeline before the big knarr.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Clone the raft/karve Ship setup; new mesh; tune Ship forces (rowing speed high, sail small or none).\n- Launch: spawn the ship at the slipway's water end, reset slipway.\n- Name forever.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Built in 5 stages and launched\n- [ ] Rows faster than a karve, holds a small cargo\n- [ ] Survives save/reload\n\n# Dependencies\nn1interact\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFirst new hull.\n","kind":"task","labels":["assets","n1","next-saga","shipyard","standalone"],"parent":"bn-2n2","size":"m","title":"Shipyard N1: the faering (fast little rowboat) hull + launch from the slipway"}	blake3:XQawS8TcRUFtnX8O8ceK3zqPg6VwMQNP6L-poGgKd-k
1791857901202568	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3sf5	{"description":"# Context & Background\nTool commands for every system.\n\n# Goals\nInspect slipways, pay a stage from nowhere (cheat), force launch, list hulls.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nLive testing without gathering materials each time.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Commands JSON; cheats flagged; spawns tagged.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Commands work through the mailbox\n\n# Dependencies\nn1interact\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nTestability.\n","kind":"task","labels":["n1","next-saga","shipyard","standalone"],"parent":"bn-2n2","size":"s","title":"Shipyard N1: ClaudeTools commands (yard status, yard pay <stage>, yard launch, yard ships)"}	blake3:wxVN2pX_xhJytWl6PIF7NEk2yNWfZ8YJHn_8C5Zm3ow
1791857901291409	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-29fq	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone N1 of Shipyard. Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, `mise run publish`, install, push dist.\n\n# Goals\nShipyard 0.1.0 published with milestone N1 verified in the game.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nBob wants every change built, installed and released, and milestone acceptance checked live, not only in unit tests.\n\n# Implementation Approach\nTest in Bob's Creative world via the ClaudeTools mailbox (see claudetools-live-game memory): never lose Bob's gear, check `siege status` and Jarldom tribute before time jumps, tag test spawns and remove them by tag. Update the README playtest checklist with what was verified and what was not.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Two players build a faering on a slipway stage by stage and row it away\n- [ ] Unit tests pass\n- [ ] F6 reload clean\n- [ ] Version 0.1.0 in Plugin.cs, CHANGELOG entry, dist/manifest.json updated and pushed\n\n# Dependencies\nn1core, n1slipway, n1interact, n1faering, n1tools\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nMilestone gate: the next milestone's work is blocked on this.\n","kind":"task","labels":["n1","next-saga","shipyard","standalone"],"parent":"bn-2n2","size":"s","title":"Shipyard N1: live test in Creative + release Shipyard 0.1.0"}	blake3:2oxgnA4b1thKJSVpXndSO1PZ30K5qf-Dbrdc_kdb9O8
1791857901376750	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3rop	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: the knarr - a wide cargo ship that holds far more than the longship. \"The knarr is the sea answer to 'no ore through portals.'\"\n\n# Goals\nKnarr mesh + 5 stage meshes and a ShipyardKnarr prefab.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nReal model needed (no vanilla equivalent).\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Blender model, deep hull, one big square sail; stage meshes as in N1.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Model approved by Bob in game\n\n# Dependencies\nn1rel\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nCargo ship.\n","kind":"task","labels":["assets","n2","next-saga","shipyard","standalone"],"parent":"bn-2n2","size":"m","title":"Shipyard N2: knarr hull model and stages (wide cargo ship)"}	blake3:2LBwRD4oY1NXzsxAZ32h1Njs98PrYN78Tz6oZtvfQBg
1791857901460798	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1uad	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: holds far more than the longship, slower, sails well in strong wind.\n\n# Goals\nShip physics tuned: cargo container much larger than the longship's (e.g. 8x6 vs 6x3), lower top speed in light wind, better in strong wind.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nGives a real trade-off vs the longship, and a sea route for ore.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Ship: patch force by wind strength for this hull (curve in Core with tests).\n- Container size; weight handling.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Hold capacity clearly above the longship\n- [ ] Slower in light wind, competitive in strong wind (measured)\n\n# Dependencies\nn1rel\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nOre logistics.\n","kind":"task","labels":["n2","next-saga","shipyard","standalone"],"parent":"bn-2n2","size":"m","title":"Shipyard N2: knarr handling and cargo (huge hold, slower, sails well in strong wind)"}	blake3:JRqxlWenG6_C-VJJZJVV3Z-wJWWdwENkapExDaNtcCc
1791857901548526	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-14j6	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: Wayfinder's ship names and fittings apply to the new hulls (mods/Wayfinder).\n\n# Goals\nNaming and fittings work on Shipyard hulls.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nWayfinder likely keys fittings by vanilla ship prefab names; it needs to accept any Ship component or a list from Shipyard.Api.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Find Wayfinder's ship detection; generalise to any Ship or add Shipyard hull names; per-hull fitting anchor offsets.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Name and fit a knarr and a faering with Wayfinder\n- [ ] Wayfinder alone unchanged\n\n# Dependencies\nn1rel\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nMods work together.\n","kind":"task","labels":["integration","n2","next-saga","shipyard","standalone","wayfinder"],"parent":"bn-2n2","size":"s","title":"Wayfinder: ship names and fittings apply to faering and knarr"}	blake3:n0mQM6N_sT1aOV3EDeR3uyRkDSqGXtdojis2gvaOauw
1791857901636186	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2u4t	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone N2 of Shipyard. Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, `mise run publish`, install, push dist.\n\n# Goals\nShipyard 0.2.0 (+ Wayfinder release) published with milestone N2 verified in the game.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nBob wants every change built, installed and released, and milestone acceptance checked live, not only in unit tests.\n\n# Implementation Approach\nTest in Bob's Creative world via the ClaudeTools mailbox (see claudetools-live-game memory): never lose Bob's gear, check `siege status` and Jarldom tribute before time jumps, tag test spawns and remove them by tag. Update the README playtest checklist with what was verified and what was not.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Build a knarr, load it with ore, sail it home in strong wind, name it with Wayfinder\n- [ ] Unit tests pass\n- [ ] F6 reload clean\n- [ ] Version 0.2.0 (+ Wayfinder release) in Plugin.cs, CHANGELOG entry, dist/manifest.json updated and pushed\n\n# Dependencies\nn2knarr, n2tune, n2wayfinder\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nMilestone gate: the next milestone's work is blocked on this.\n","kind":"task","labels":["n2","next-saga","shipyard","standalone","wayfinder"],"parent":"bn-2n2","size":"s","title":"Shipyard N2: live test in Creative + release Shipyard 0.2.0 (+ Wayfinder release)"}	blake3:p5aLZF0JmyPZDx9m8I4x21W6i0UaZOHOaP4VA9nJMCw
1791857901724976	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1u28	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: boathouse (naust) protects moored ships from wear.\n\n# Goals\nA naust shelter at the waterline; ships inside take no weather/water wear (WearNTear damage from being in water).\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nHistorical boat sheds; solves ship decay at home.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Piece with a trigger volume; patch Ship/WearNTear water damage when the ship is inside a naust.\n- Real model; snap and support values.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A ship in the naust takes no wear over days; outside it does\n\n# Dependencies\nn2rel\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFleet care.\n","kind":"task","labels":["n3","next-saga","shipyard","standalone"],"parent":"bn-2n2","size":"m","title":"Shipyard N3: boathouse (naust) piece that protects moored ships from wear"}	blake3:Xhcqi2tuVUE6HAesix4asBEyc1wgHsQkgbTOOkjGRa4
1791857901813394	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1brx	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: repairs at the slipway.\n\n# Goals\nA damaged ship near a slipway can be repaired (hammer or E) using materials.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nShips otherwise need a workbench nearby.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Treat the slipway as a crafting station for repair purposes (CraftingStation in range).\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Repair a damaged ship at the slipway\n\n# Dependencies\nn2rel\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFleet care.\n","kind":"task","labels":["n3","next-saga","shipyard","standalone"],"parent":"bn-2n2","size":"s","title":"Shipyard N3: repair ships at the slipway"}	blake3:0dVKxV7v-c0yCpXciJ2bro1XjnLWep0bXZX74AlsYcE
1791857901900437	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1k5q	{"description":"# Context & Background\nJarldom J6 #46 shipwright builds boats at a boatyard zone - with Shipyard, its staged builds and the knarr.\n\n# Goals\nA stable static Api so a villager (not a player) can choose a hull and contribute materials from stockpiles.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nVillagers can't press E; an Api-driven contribution path keeps the shipwright simple and safe (owner-validated).\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- `int Version`; `Vector3[] SlipwaysNear(pos, r)`; `bool StartBuild(slipway, hull)`; `int Contribute(slipway, prefab, count)` (owner only); `int Stage(slipway)`; `string[] Hulls`; `int CargoSlots(hull)`.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Api documented; contribution through the Api obeys pay-in-full\n\n# Dependencies\nn2rel, bn-1xw\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nLets Jarldom build ships.\n","kind":"task","labels":["integration","n3","next-saga","shipyard","standalone"],"parent":"bn-2n2","size":"s","title":"Shipyard N3: Shipyard.Api (Version, Slipways near, StartBuild(hull), Contribute, Stage, Hulls, CargoOf) for the Jarldom shipwright"}	blake3:-ELBcFdNBhOb1lq5LIKTBuWF52_jl1odDAFttnyPH7c
1791857901992170	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3dos	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone N3 of Shipyard. Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, `mise run publish`, install, push dist.\n\n# Goals\nShipyard 0.3.0 published with milestone N3 verified in the game.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nBob wants every change built, installed and released, and milestone acceptance checked live, not only in unit tests.\n\n# Implementation Approach\nTest in Bob's Creative world via the ClaudeTools mailbox (see claudetools-live-game memory): never lose Bob's gear, check `siege status` and Jarldom tribute before time jumps, tag test spawns and remove them by tag. Update the README playtest checklist with what was verified and what was not.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Moor in a naust for days without wear; repair at the slipway; Api build test via a tool command\n- [ ] Unit tests pass\n- [ ] F6 reload clean\n- [ ] Version 0.3.0 in Plugin.cs, CHANGELOG entry, dist/manifest.json updated and pushed\n\n# Dependencies\nn3naust, n3repair, n3api\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nMilestone gate: the next milestone's work is blocked on this.\n","kind":"task","labels":["n3","next-saga","shipyard","standalone"],"parent":"bn-2n2","size":"s","title":"Shipyard N3: live test in Creative + release Shipyard 0.3.0"}	blake3:M0AEgLfSOw5-Zy4YZkfX5OHSoGa2vdCDOoR8J6rTdYE
1791857902075946	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2hlu	{"description":"# Context & Background\nFirst task of the Loom mod (JARLDOM-NEXT.md). Standalone mods must be useful alone and expose a tiny `Loom.Api` that Jarldom finds by reflection; nothing exists yet. Spec section 3.13 (#55): the clothing items and crafting move OUT of Jarldom (spin-out rule: only items and crafting leave). The prefab names stay Jarldom* forever - this is the documented exception.\n\n# Goals\nAn empty but buildable, testable, publishable Loom mod that every later Loom bone builds on.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nCopying the repo's existing small-mod layout keeps build/publish/test/manifest automatic and keeps every mod looking the same to Bob and to other agents.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- New project mods/Loom/ copied from a small mod's pattern (mods/Spyglass, mods/Delivery): Loom.csproj (net48, Directory.Build.props), Plugin.cs with `public const string Guid/Name/Version` (scripts/publish.py regexes these), Core/ for pure logic (no Unity), DESCRIPTION.txt, CHANGELOG.txt, cover.jpg, README with a playtest checklist.\n- tests/Loom.Tests console project linking Core/*.cs (same as tests/Spyglass.Tests/Program.cs style); wire into scripts/test.py if it enumerates projects.\n- mods/*/*.csproj is auto-discovered by scripts/build.py and scripts/publish.py, so `mise run build|test|publish|install` pick it up; publish writes the dist/manifest.json entry.\n- RESTART_REQUIRED.txt if pieces/items/recipes need a restart (see reload-levels memory / Quad's Claude Tools rules).\n- ServerSettings: server-authoritative config sync as in Jarldom/ServerSettings.cs.\n- A ClaudeTools command root (`loom ...`) registered like Jarldom/Tools/Tools.cs.\n- Prefab golden list tests/Loom.Tests/prefabs.txt per foundation bone bn-2vn (append-only; names prefixed Loom).\n- Read ~/repos/valheim-claude-tools/docs/modding-pitfalls.md first.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `mise run build` and `mise run test` pass with the new project\n- [ ] `mise run publish` lists Loom in dist/manifest.json (version 0.0.x, not announced)\n- [ ] F6 reload of Loom is clean (no errors, no leftover objects)\n- [ ] `loom help` answers through the ClaudeTools mailbox\n- [ ] Golden prefab list file and test exist (empty list ok)\n\n# Dependencies\nbn-2vn\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFoundation for every Loom milestone.\n","kind":"task","labels":["loom","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3kf","size":"s","title":"Loom: scaffold the standalone mod project (csproj, Plugin, Core, tests, README, tools command, golden prefab list)"}	blake3:twge_hNGgM0neHBQOzMs1n_wmodN_Hd3FTa2HF-oacM
1791857902166221	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3nw1	{"description":"# Context & Background\nToday Jarldom (Items.cs, Villager/Weaving.cs) registers the tunics, dresses, caps (and cloth/flax items, if any) as colony-only recipes. Renaming a prefab deletes it from players' saves.\n\n# Goals\nLoom registers exactly the same prefabs (same names, same stats, same icons) and makes them player-craftable.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nKeeping names is the only save-safe move; a comment in code explains why a Loom file registers Jarldom* names, so a later agent doesn't 'fix' the prefix.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Move the item definitions to a pure Data table shared by both mods (copied file with a sync test, or Loom owns it and Jarldom keeps a copy for fallback).\n- Golden prefab list (bn-2vn): Loom's list includes these Jarldom* names; Jarldom's test allows them to be registered by either mod.\n- Clothing slots and warmth exactly as Jarldom has them now.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every clothing prefab registered by Loom with an identical name and stats\n- [ ] Code comment documents the naming exception\n- [ ] Golden list updated\n\n# Dependencies\nlo0, bn-2vn\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nSave-safe spin-out.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","loom","next-saga","save-safety","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3kf","size":"m","title":"Loom: register the clothing items and recipes in Loom, KEEPING their Jarldom* prefab names (documented exception)"}	blake3:FC382FwVtf2opxEUeU7w6e21EQVkiuEuk_mipFssduM
1791857902248693	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2pd8	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec moves out flax processing, spinning wheel use, the loom, and the tunics, dresses and caps, all craftable by players.\n\n# Goals\nA player without Jarldom can grow flax, spin it, weave cloth on a loom piece and craft clothes.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nStandalone usefulness rule.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Loom station piece (LoomLoom? pick a forever name carefully; or reuse an existing Jarldom loom piece name if one exists).\n- Recipes on the loom; spinning wheel (vanilla, from Mistlands) for thread; flax from vanilla Flax.\n- Byre wool (Byre.Api / prefab lookup) accepted as an alternative fibre when present.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Full chain playable without Jarldom: flax -> thread -> cloth -> tunic\n- [ ] Recipes visible only at the right stations\n\n# Dependencies\nlo1move\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nStandalone value.\n","kind":"task","labels":["loom","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3kf","size":"m","title":"Loom: player crafting - flax processing, spinning wheel use, the loom station, tunics/dresses/caps recipes"}	blake3:pBd7BY8qvS0WS7FcToFgU3loPtW08JBxzAA_YTdFmZ8
1791857902335711	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2qhh	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: dyes (berries, bark).\n\n# Goals\nCraft dyes (raspberry/blueberry/cloudberry, bark) and dye clothing items.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nColour is the main reason to craft clothes beyond warmth.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Dye items; colour as item custom data (m_customData) not new prefabs (avoids prefab explosion and naming risk); shader tint at equip.\n- Villager outfits in Jarldom can read the same custom data.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Dye a tunic; colour persists through save/reload and shows to other players\n\n# Dependencies\nlo2craft\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nCustomization.\n","kind":"task","labels":["loom","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3kf","size":"m","title":"Loom: dyes from berries and bark, applied to clothing (colour variants)"}	blake3:-TewdE7zDGTX-vnVHROdyMZ89LbjOck2J0NqXslM3O4
1791857902423990	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-33ek	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec: Loom registers them; Jarldom stops registering them when Loom is present. Double registration of the same prefab name would clash.\n\n# Goals\nExactly one registrar per prefab, decided at load regardless of plugin load order.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nLoad order is not guaranteed; check via BepInEx Chainloader.PluginInfos (Loom GUID) or ApiRef(\"Loom.Api\").\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Jarldom checks Loom presence before ObjectDB/ZNetScene registration; logs which mod owns clothing.\n- Weaver AI (Villager/Weaving.cs) keeps working against the prefab names either way.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Both installed: no duplicate-prefab warnings; items exist once\n- [ ] Weaver still crafts outfits with Loom installed\n\n# Dependencies\nlo1move, bn-1xw\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nClean coexistence.\n","kind":"task","labels":["integration","jarldom","loom","next-saga","save-safety","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3kf","size":"s","title":"Jarldom: detect Loom and stop registering the clothing prefabs (Loom owns them when present)"}	blake3:RUZrlheLEe72xkCcUyHra5YUVlUIUQ1I7_4ZevefPf4
1791857902512711	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-hgg1	{"description":"# Context & Background\nOpen decision bn-zfl. Recommendation: (a) for one release with a deprecation note, then (b). Whatever the choice, no player may lose clothing items.\n\n# Goals\nThe no-Loom path implemented as decided.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nUnder (b) a registration-only stub or a loud warning is needed so saves don't drop items.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- (a): keep Jarldom's registration path when Loom is absent; log + window note \"clothing moves to Loom\".\n- (b): hide the weaver profession without Loom; still register prefabs (no recipes) to protect saves, or refuse to load with a clear message.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Matches the recorded decision\n- [ ] No clothing item lost in the no-Loom path\n\n# Dependencies\nlo4detect, bn-zfl\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nSave safety.\n","kind":"task","labels":["decision","jarldom","loom","next-saga","save-safety","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3kf","size":"s","title":"Jarldom: clothing fallback without Loom, per Bob's decision (a: keep registering for one release with a deprecation note, or b: require Loom)"}	blake3:QS2q3iE3PbgkpnVqbVaSTfZjdwvR1bT958L4lzbp5mY
1791857902603709	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3tn9	{"description":"# Context & Background\nThe spin-out moves item registration between mods; the classic failure is items vanishing from chests/inventories when the registrar changes.\n\n# Goals\nProof, on real saves, that no clothing item is lost in any order.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nThis is exactly the 'renaming deletes items' class of bug; it must be tested before release, not after.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Prepare a test character + chest holding every clothing item under the current released Jarldom.\n- Cases: (1) update Jarldom, add Loom; (2) update Jarldom without Loom; (3) Loom only (no Jarldom); (4) both then remove Loom; (5) both then remove Jarldom. Check inventory + chest contents after each load (ClaudeTools inventory dump vs baseline JSON).\n- Use a copy of a world/character, never Bob's live gear (backup first).\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] All five cases keep every item (or the documented decision case behaves as agreed)\n- [ ] Results recorded as a bone comment\n\n# Dependencies\nlo2craft, lo3dyes, lo4detect, lo5fallback\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nRelease gate.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","loom","next-saga","save-safety","standalone","testing"],"parent":"bn-3kf","size":"m","title":"Loom: install/uninstall-order save-safety test matrix (Loom only, Jarldom only, both, upgrade from old Jarldom, remove Loom)"}	blake3:GqX6Q6s0vRMdWcPf2om106JTCYwFXd_67_COopo6YtY
1791857902693203	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-11z2	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone LOOM of Loom. Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, `mise run publish`, install, push dist.\n\n# Goals\nLoom 0.1.0 (+ Jarldom release) published with milestone LOOM verified in the game.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nBob wants every change built, installed and released, and milestone acceptance checked live, not only in unit tests.\n\n# Implementation Approach\nTest in Bob's Creative world via the ClaudeTools mailbox (see claudetools-live-game memory): never lose Bob's gear, check `siege status` and Jarldom tribute before time jumps, tag test spawns and remove them by tag. Update the README playtest checklist with what was verified and what was not.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Craft and dye clothes without Jarldom\n- [ ] Jarldom weaver still dresses villagers with Loom installed\n- [ ] Unit tests pass\n- [ ] F6 reload clean\n- [ ] Version 0.1.0 (+ Jarldom release) in Plugin.cs, CHANGELOG entry, dist/manifest.json updated and pushed\n\n# Dependencies\nlo6matrix\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nMilestone gate: the next milestone's work is blocked on this.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","loom","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3kf","size":"s","title":"Loom LOOM: live test in Creative + release Loom 0.1.0 (+ Jarldom release)"}	blake3:jljPfmtERkNTEPTnwYftYdUdDRbJj1Hj8biSrAjkZnw
1791857907852059	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1jxo	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.3 #26. Grief for bond-mates may not exist as a named moodlet yet (grep found no \"Grief\") - add a \"Grief\" moodlet on loss for bond-mates if missing.\n# Implementation Approach\nBurial ground zone/graves (GraveTask exists). E on a grave marker with remains in inventory consumes them: remove Grief moodlet from bond-mates, Favour.Add hel, add a memorial entry \"rests with Hel\", saga line, clear the lost state.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Kill and bury a lost soul: the memorial updates and grief ends; Hel favour rises.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nJ3 acceptance line 3.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j3","p2"],"parent":"bn-3k3","size":"m","title":"J3 #26b: Laying the lost to rest - E on a grave marker at the burial ground with the remains: grief ends, Hel's favour rises, memorial 'rests with Hel'"}	blake3:ybUGgMYiwyBIGJaHf3oyl7eVZf_LG9Rgw_V9Zoatltc
1791857907935979	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3pxh	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.3 Accept lines.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Take one villager from arrival to the funeral ship; the rewards apply once even with F6 mid-ceremony.\n- [ ] A Dimmed villager shows a request in their panel, and completing it clears the Dimming.\n- [ ] Kill and bury a lost soul: the memorial updates and grief ends.\n- [ ] README playtest checklist; DataVersion raised if formats changed; version bump; CHANGELOG; dist released.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nCloses J3.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j3","p2","live-test"],"parent":"bn-3k3","size":"m","title":"J3 live acceptance test in Creative + release"}	blake3:1k89e8nBqXEogvIdDM4U4cza2Qh1h8jSUMWrg1mDEjA
1791857908018933	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2wzz	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.4 #27. Default length pending decision bn-2mm. Core/Rules.cs has Clock.\n# Implementation Approach\nCore/Calendar.cs: from colony day (founding day offset) -> year, season (winter/spring/summer/autumn), day in season, next festival + days until. Festivals: Yule = midwinter, Midsummer, Winter Nights = start of winter, Sigrblot = start of summer. Server setting YearLength. An override source interface so Seasons (#72) can drive it.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Unit tests for lengths 40 and other values; festival days correct; override hook tested.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nBackbone for festivals, anniversaries (#22), shielings, crops.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j4","p2"],"parent":"bn-12d","size":"s","title":"J4 #27a: Colony calendar core - configurable year (default 40 days, four 10-day seasons), day-of-year, season, festival dates (pure + tests)"}	blake3:r41hZ39ex6Maam8FBSH-WFh-H54wI3LayN5MQok8_pg
1791857908107443	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-k35g	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.4 #27: shown in the colony window.\n# Implementation Approach\nUi/ColonyWindow.cs header line: \"Winter, day 4 of 10 - Yule in 6 days\"; festival list with preparation status (#F0).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Window shows the season/day and next festival, matching Core.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nPlayer-facing rhythm.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j4","p2"],"parent":"bn-12d","size":"s","title":"J4 #27b: Show the calendar in the colony window (season, day, next festival)"}	blake3:Nkzn1Yr48xs4UOOu2f2XHlm_7AvFYi_ZOisRPrRc-10
1791857908192846	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-388l	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.4 #27: \"on Wayfinder's primstav (add Wayfinder.Api.AddFeastDay() upstream)\". Primstav lives in mods/Wayfinder (Items.cs, Hud.cs, Weather.cs). The Api.cs file is created by the J2 beacon task.\n# Implementation Approach\n`AddFeastDay(string key, int dayOfYear or absolute day, string name)` / `ClearFeastDays(string source)`; bump Version; release Wayfinder.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Feast days added via a test command appear on the primstav; released.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nLets the calendar show in Bob's other mod.\n","kind":"task","labels":["wayfinder","jarldom","next-saga","j4","p2","integration"],"parent":"bn-12d","size":"s","title":"J4 #27c: Wayfinder upstream - add Wayfinder.Api.AddFeastDay(day, name) so the primstav shows colony feast days"}	blake3:DD8-ld6q6DlLIJX4QDWH-7DM33pWnYJNN6k2QSafCg0
1791857908282291	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-npc2	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.4 #27.\n# Implementation Approach\nVia ApiRef, on calendar load/change call Wayfinder.Api.AddFeastDay for the four festivals of the local player's colony. No-op without Wayfinder.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Primstav shows Yule, Midsummer, Winter Nights, Sigrblot on the right days; no errors without Wayfinder.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nIntegration polish.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j4","p2","integration"],"parent":"bn-12d","size":"s","title":"J4 #27d: Push colony festival dates onto Wayfinder's primstav via Api"}	blake3:Yjy6b5TrhlTLye6lFrRf5XRKsD4N6IbbKC9Hqz5fSBc
1791857908369272	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3t0m	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.4 #72: use the existing mod (https://thunderstore.io/c/valheim/p/shudnal/Seasons/), don't build seasons ourselves.\n# Implementation Approach\nDownload Seasons, decompile its public API/state (ilspycmd), find current season + day (likely a static/public property or a ZoneSystem global key). Read via reflection (ApiRef-style; it has no <Mod>.Api of ours). Feed the Calendar override. Document the version tested against.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] With Seasons installed, the dates follow its seasons; without, our calendar; no errors on a Seasons version mismatch.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nJ4 acceptance line 2.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j4","p2","integration","seasons"],"parent":"bn-12d","size":"m","title":"J4 #72: Seasons soft integration - if shudnal's Seasons is installed, read its season and day and line the festivals up with it"}	blake3:dfXDCSIxGJ9swhiv8qraCB0DHNcFu4xJuM_hkkPgj54
1791857908455721	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3f07	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.4: every festival has preparation (goods brought to the hall in the 2 days before), the event (dusk to dawn), and a blessing (lasts until the next festival, scaled by how well it was prepared). Skipping one gives a small neglect penalty. No festival code exists today (only Feast).\n# Implementation Approach\nCore/Festivals.cs: festival definitions (id, needs list with amounts, event hooks, blessing effects table), state per colony (phase, goods delivered %, active blessing + strength). Blessing strength = f(prep %). Neglect = small mood/favour penalty. ColonyRecord fields (raise DataVersion). Unit tests.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tests: phases by calendar day, scaling, blessing replaced at next festival, neglect when skipped.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nShared machinery for #28-31.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j4","p2","data-version"],"parent":"bn-12d","size":"m","title":"J4 #F0a: Festival framework core - preparation (2 days before), event (dusk to dawn), blessing scaled by preparation until the next festival, neglect penalty"}	blake3:0tBSt9n6bPgT9YQFW4sCmEj0GO3pI9fSlFQDyVVaoBo
1791857908548412	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-247x	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.4.\n# Implementation Approach\nAnnounce preparation (top-left news, Colony.Short), create hauling jobs from stockpiles to a hall chest (JobBoard), start at dusk, end at dawn, apply blessing effects through existing hooks (comfort, work speed, damage, worth gain), remove at next festival. Skald verse (#19) gets a festival event kind. Tool: `jarldom festival [list|prep <id>|start <id>|end]` plus `jarldom time` for a full year run.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A generic test festival goes prep -> event -> blessing -> removed, with announcements.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nRuntime for all four festivals.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j4","p2"],"parent":"bn-12d","size":"m","title":"J4 #F0b: Festival runtime - announcements, haulers bring goods to the hall, event start/end at dusk/dawn, blessing apply/remove, tool command"}	blake3:0v-nNEQADjAwhYHSG2deO8QNsA9Wjl4iXKBJpFAbdB8
1791857908636734	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1dqw	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.4 #28 (midwinter).\n# Implementation Approach\nPreparation: 50 wood, feast food, mead. Event: a JarldomYuleLog piece/visual in the hall hearth burning 3 days (fuel-free fire visual; prefab name forever if a piece), a long feast (reuse Feast.Call with longer duration), toasts (Skal.cs toast lines). Blessing: +1 comfort everywhere in the radius (patch SE_Rested comfort calc within radius) and cold resistance in the radius.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Prep announced, log burns 3 days, feast + toasts, blessing applied and removed at the next festival.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nThe biggest festival.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j4","p2"],"parent":"bn-12d","size":"m","title":"J4 #28: Yule - 50 wood Yule log, a feast's worth of food, mead; Yule log burns 3 days in the hall hearth; long feast; toasts; comfort +1 everywhere, cold resistance in radius"}	blake3:V9l4Xztr_8Y93ztvsgBf15A90Ua1MlQUWe0XmZgSOTI
1791857908728101	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-19pe	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.4 #29. Horses mod adds races at Midsummer later (integration, other goal).\n# Implementation Approach\nPrep: wood + dandelions. Event: bonfire at an open outdoor spot near the hall (vanilla bonfire visual, temporary), villagers gather and play the \"dance\" emote animation. Blessing: mood moodlet + 5% work speed.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Bonfire lit, villagers dance, blessing applied/removed.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nSummer joy.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j4","p2"],"parent":"bn-12d","size":"m","title":"J4 #29: Midsummer - wood for a bonfire, dandelions; outdoor bonfire, villagers dance (game dance emote); mood +, work speed +5%"}	blake3:uC_lqsWSqzhjWmf487ozu87J6XlLHey8Ykyok3vTb4o
1791857908815116	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3eq6	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.4 #30 (start of winter). Uses the memorial (#25a) and the skald (#19b).\n# Implementation Approach\nPrep: offerings delivered to the burial ground (grave markers). Event: glow on memorial runestones/wall (emissive/light), the skald reads the names of the ascended (subtitles), Favour.Add hel/odin. Blessing: worth gain x1.2 (Core Worth).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Names read aloud, glow, favour up, worth gain +20% while blessed.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nTies the year to the afterlife.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j4","p2"],"parent":"bn-12d","size":"m","title":"J4 #30: Winter Nights - offerings at the burial ground; memorial runestones glow; names of the ascended read aloud; Hel and Odin favour +; worth gain +20%"}	blake3:wZXn1cemGSjB7I2owUek3i4yX_lZiffDBCMy7SLR0Rs
1791857908904268	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-26ce	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.4 #31 (start of summer).\n# Implementation Approach\nPrep: trophies or meat at Odin's shrine (altar container). Event: gothi blesses the fighters at the shrine (guards gather). Blessing: +10% damage for guards (Combat) and the players of the colony (status effect while in/linked to the colony), +10% to trade run income and expedition outcomes (Trading in Core/Rules.cs; expeditions when J6 exists).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Sacrifice -> blessing; guards and players deal +10%; trade run +10%; removed at the next festival.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nWar-season ritual.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j4","p2"],"parent":"bn-12d","size":"m","title":"J4 #31: Sigrblot - sacrifice at Odin's shrine (trophies or meat); blessing of the fighters; guards and party +10% damage; trade runs and expeditions +10%"}	blake3:I8ZwxOsq-bj2grBpfXXFbdGCGHYx462c8mfImc16TeE
1791857908999640	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2fcm	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 2.4 Accept lines. Before time jumps: `jarldom tribute`, `siege status` (Bob died twice to raids triggered by time skips).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A full colony year in test (`jarldom time`): each festival announces its preparation, runs, and applies and removes its blessing.\n- [ ] With Seasons installed, the dates follow its seasons.\n- [ ] README playtest checklist; DataVersion; version bump; CHANGELOG; dist released.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nCloses J4.\n","kind":"task","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j4","p2","live-test"],"parent":"bn-12d","size":"m","title":"J4 live acceptance test in Creative + release"}	blake3:pZ2Yql3zp5N57wes-WnNmSlf0N7LfAee5Vzm27xmY_Q
