1791857917876224	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2uzt	{"description":"# Context & Background\nFirst task of the Hounds standalone mod (spec section 3.3, goal bn-10n). Nothing exists yet. Repo pattern: small mods like mods/Spyglass and mods/Delivery (csproj net48 via mods/Directory.Build.props, Plugin.cs, pure logic files, CHANGELOG.txt, DESCRIPTION.txt, cover.jpg), tests in tests/<Mod>.Tests (Program.cs check-style runner), mise tasks build/test/verify/publish/install, dist/manifest.json catalog for the F7 mod manager.\n\n# Goals\nAn empty-but-loadable Hounds plugin that every later Hounds task drops code into, with the ground rules wired in from day one.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nDoing the scaffold once up front means each feature task stays s/m and the ground rules (prefix names, server-authoritative settings, F6 reload, pure Core logic, tool command, golden prefab list) are not forgotten per feature. Hounds covers three animals (hounds, cats, hawks); one mod, three milestones.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- mods/Hounds/Hounds.csproj, Plugin.cs (BepInEx plugin com.bobisme.hounds, server-synced ConfigEntries, clean OnDestroy for F6 reload).\n- mods/Hounds/Core/ for pure C# (no Unity) linked into tests/Hounds.Tests.\n- A ClaudeTools command root `hounds` (status/help first) following Jarldom's Tools/Tools.cs pattern.\n- README with a playtest checklist section, DESCRIPTION.txt, CHANGELOG.txt, cover.jpg placeholder, dist/manifest.json entry.\n- tests/Hounds.Tests/prefabs.txt golden list (empty to start) + the superset test from foundation bone bn-2vn.\n- Read ~/repos/valheim-claude-tools/docs/modding-pitfalls.md before writing items.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `mise run build` and `mise run test` pass with Hounds included\n- [ ] Plugin loads and F6-reloads cleanly in game with no errors\n- [ ] `hounds status` tool command answers\n- [ ] Golden prefab list test exists\n- [ ] No dependency on Jarldom or any other Bob mod\n\n# Dependencies\nbn-2vn\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFoundation for the whole Hounds goal; keeps it useful on its own per the standalone ground rule.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.3; parent goal bn-10n.\n","kind":"task","labels":["hounds","h1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-10n","size":"s","title":"Hounds: scaffold mods/Hounds project (csproj, Plugin, Core/, tests/Hounds.Tests, README checklist, manifest entry, tool command, prefab golden list)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:TfPaazNV6_J9LjIp1ANSuoV3RHqzirgQsv4xtYkByUE
1791857917903512	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-zf6n	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.3: raise a tamed wolf pup into a herding dog or a war hound. Vanilla wolves already breed (Procreation) and pups grow (Growup) into tame wolves; there is no training.\n\n# Goals\nA tamed wolf pup gets a raising state (bond, training progress, chosen path) that survives growth into an adult and world reloads.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nHooking the vanilla Growup swap (pup prefab -> adult prefab) lets us reuse the game's breeding instead of new creatures; storing a few small ZDO keys keeps network cost low (nothing big on moving ZDOs).\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Patch Growup to copy Hounds keys (hounds_path, hounds_bond, hounds_train) from pup to adult ZDO.\n- Core/Raising.cs: pure bond/training progression (feeding, petting, time together) with tests.\n- Hover text shows path and training progress.\n- Tool: `hounds pup` spawns a tame pup near the player; `hounds state` prints keys.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Pup -> adult keeps bond/training keys\n- [ ] Training progress rises with feeding/petting and is unit-tested\n- [ ] State survives a world reload\n\n# Dependencies\nHounds: scaffold mods/Hounds project (csproj, Plugin, Core/, tests/H\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nBase for both hound paths and for Jarldom's village dogs (#12).\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.3; parent goal bn-10n.\n","kind":"task","labels":["hounds","h1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-10n","size":"m","title":"Hounds H1: wolf pups grow up as trainable hounds (pup -> young -> adult, raising state saved on the creature ZDO)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:MyEivu4uo2zwSVOAra9hnUacg39x8aZfcAZUy9biU3E
1791857917922467	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3l5h	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.3: herding dog keeps livestock together and brings strays home; war hound follows you, fights, tracks wounded game. Commands by whistle.\n\n# Goals\nA whistle item with a small command set; trained adults obey according to their path.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nA whistle (one item, cycle command with a modifier key) avoids a UI and fits the Norse low-tech theme. Commands go via an RPC to the creature owner (server-authoritative pattern).\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Prefab `Hounds_Whistle` (name kept forever; add to golden list) crafted at workbench.\n- Commands: follow, stay, home (return to a marked kennel/bed point), and path-specific: herd (herding) / track (war).\n- Use vanilla game sounds for the whistle if one fits; otherwise CC0 and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.\n- Choosing the path: E on a fully trained young hound opens a two-choice prompt.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Whistle crafts and cycles commands\n- [ ] Follow/stay/home work for both paths\n- [ ] Path choice is permanent and saved\n- [ ] Commands work in multiplayer (non-owner whistler)\n\n# Dependencies\nHounds H1: wolf pups grow up as trainable hounds (pup -> young -> adult\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nGives players control of their hounds; the Jarldom side reuses the same command RPCs.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.3; parent goal bn-10n.\n","kind":"task","labels":["hounds","h1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-10n","size":"m","title":"Hounds H1: choose herding dog or war hound; whistle item + whistle commands (follow, stay, home, fetch/herd)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:3EtJwSxzHymM7hVOa5S9tURERRypy0cotJ38-u9IWYw
1791857917945166	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-12ki	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.3 herding dog. Works on any tamed animals (vanilla boars/wolves/lox/chickens, and Byre's sheep/goats/cattle when installed).\n\n# Goals\nA herding dog patrols around its home point and pushes tame animals that wander beyond a radius back toward it.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nPushing by approaching from the far side (flee/avoid behaviour) is cheaper and more robust than teleporting or rewriting animal AI; vanilla MonsterAI already flees from scary things for some prey.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Core/Herding.cs: pure geometry (pick stray furthest outside radius, approach point behind it) + tests.\n- Behaviour on the hound: periodic scan (no FindObjectsOfTypeAll on timers - perf-hitches memory; use Character.GetAllCharacters / BaseAI lists), move to approach point, nudge animal's AI target/flee.\n- Byre animals detected by tame flag, no Byre dependency.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Strays beyond radius are returned within a minute in a test pen\n- [ ] Scan cost measured (<0.1 ms/frame per dog)\n- [ ] No effect on untamed animals\n\n# Dependencies\nHounds H1: choose herding dog or war hound; whistle item + whistle comm\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFeeds Jarldom herders (herding dogs) and pairs with the Byre mod.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.3; parent goal bn-10n.\n","kind":"task","labels":["hounds","h1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-10n","size":"m","title":"Hounds H1: herding dog AI - keep tamed livestock inside a radius, bring strays back","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:g8q-_JxIQ35rjh7gkm9OiFKk223BIGB3puvHBgQlvwU
1791857917962737	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1kcn	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.3 war hound: follows you, fights, tracks wounded game.\n\n# Goals\nA war hound that is a useful combat companion and finds animals you wounded that fled.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nVanilla tame wolves already follow and fight; the new part is tracking. Tracking = remember creatures the owner damaged that fled, lead the player there.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Patch Character.Damage: when the owner hits a non-boss animal, remember it on the hound (local only).\n- 'track' command: hound runs toward the nearest remembered wounded creature, barking; vanilla bark/howl clip.\n- Damage/HP scaling with training level in Core/Raising.cs.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] War hound follows and fights\n- [ ] Track leads to a wounded deer that fled out of sight\n- [ ] Tracking memory cleared on death of the target\n\n# Dependencies\nHounds H1: choose herding dog or war hound; whistle item + whistle comm\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nA hunting companion for players; Jarldom hunters later benefit.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.3; parent goal bn-10n.\n","kind":"task","labels":["hounds","h1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-10n","size":"m","title":"Hounds H1: war hound - follow and fight beside the player, track wounded game (blood trail marker)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:H-qJ1JWPdJa4K0XTVpWdILYDtKcVJhUR6-9IYAfmJZw
1791857917982534	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1hnn	{"description":"# Context & Background\nGround rule: each standalone mod publishes a tiny static Api found by reflection. Jarldom's village dogs (#12) should use trained hounds when Hounds is installed.\n\n# Goals\nA stable Api: `int Version`, `bool IsTrainedHound(Character)`, `string PathOf(Character)` (herding/war/none), `void Command(Character, string)`.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nKeeping the Api tiny and string-based avoids leaking Hounds types into Jarldom.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- mods/Hounds/Api.cs following the convention documented in bn-1xw.\n- Unit-testable parts in Core.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Api compiles with Version=1\n- [ ] Calling it with a non-hound returns safe defaults\n\n# Dependencies\nHounds H1: herding dog AI - keep tamed livestock inside a radius, bring, Hounds H1: war hound - follow and fight beside the player, track wounde, bn-1xw\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nEnables J1 #12 village dogs and Jarldom herders to use real hounds.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.3; parent goal bn-10n.\n","kind":"task","labels":["hounds","h1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-10n","size":"s","title":"Hounds H1: publish Hounds.Api (Version, IsTrainedHound, PathOf, Command) for Jarldom","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:5MzolgLGQxtXZOpzEgF18HnCgAnGYU6CxQ5PlY2qk6c
1791857918002630	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-249l	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.3 Jarldom side + J1 #12 village dogs (adopt tamed wolves; follow villagers, bark a raid warning at 40 m, sleep by the hall hearth). With Hounds installed its trained hounds are used instead; herders get herding dogs.\n\n# Goals\nJarldom villagers use the standalone mod's features when it is installed, and nothing changes (no errors) when it is not.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nGround rule: no hard dependency in either direction; Jarldom resolves `<Mod>.Api` by reflection through the ApiRef helper (bn-1xw) and degrades to vanilla behaviour. Villager behaviour stays in Jarldom (spin-out rule).\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Compat: ApiRef('Hounds.Api'). In the adoption list prefer IsTrainedHound.\n- Herder work (existing Herder + Pasture zone) assigns a herding dog to the pasture via Command(home at pasture).\n- War hounds join guards' raid warning.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] With Hounds: adopting lists trained hounds first; a herding dog keeps the pasture together\n- [ ] Raid bark still works for hounds\n- [ ] Without the mod installed Jarldom behaves exactly as before (no errors)\n- [ ] Jarldom released (version, changelog, dist); raise Plugin.DataVersion if record/soul formats change\n\n# Dependencies\nHounds H1: publish Hounds.Api (Version, IsTrainedHound, PathOf, Command, bn-1xw\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nConnects the Hounds mod to the colony.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.3; parent goal bn-10n.\n","kind":"task","labels":["hounds","h1","next-saga","standalone","jarldom","integration"],"parent":"bn-10n","size":"m","title":"Jarldom: village dogs (#12) and herders use Hounds' trained hounds when Hounds is installed","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:cNLidnwANBMkHNebQZcVKT_loACFTytqhpwb0ZfmCV4
1791857918022227	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-13os	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone H1 of Hounds (spec section 3.3). Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, dist + manifest, for this mod only.\n\n# Goals\nProve H1 works in a real game and ship it.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nUnit tests cover pure logic but taming, AI, physics and status effects only show their problems live (see claudetools-live-game memory: mailbox commands, `reload <Mod>`). Never lose Bob's gear; check `siege status` and tributes before time jumps.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Run the README playtest checklist items for this milestone in Bob's Creative world via ClaudeTools.\n- Fix what breaks (file bugs as bones if not fixed now).\n- Update README checklist, CHANGELOG, DESCRIPTION; bump version; `mise run publish`; update dist/manifest.json.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Raise a pup into each path\n- [ ] Whistle commands work\n- [ ] Herding dog returns strays\n- [ ] War hound tracks a wounded deer\n- [ ] Works with Jarldom NOT installed\n- [ ] F6 reload mid-test leaves no duplicates/errors\n- [ ] Released as Hounds 0.1.0 in dist/manifest.json\n\n# Dependencies\nHounds H1: herding dog AI - keep tamed livestock inside a radius, bring, Hounds H1: war hound - follow and fight beside the player, track wounde, Hounds H1: publish Hounds.Api (Version, IsTrainedHound, PathOf, Command, Jarldom: village dogs (#12) and herders use Hounds' trained hounds wh\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nShips a usable slice of Hounds so players get value before the whole goal is done.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.3; parent goal bn-10n.\n","kind":"task","labels":["hounds","h1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-10n","size":"s","title":"Hounds H1: live test in Creative + release Hounds 0.1.0","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:mA-xMFCl6iG_d2lWHYSMIOtm6yVAMz470AwJGYk7Um4
1791857918041717	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1rj1	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.3 cats: a wild cat in the Meadows to tame; on their own they give comfort +1 and purr.\n\n# Goals\nA new small tameable creature with idle cat behaviour.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nCloning a small vanilla creature rig is risky for looks; check for a usable model (e.g. a scaled/retextured fox-like body from existing assets) or Blender-made mesh via the existing Blender pipeline (blender-anim-pipeline memory). Keep prefab name forever (Hounds_Cat).\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Prefab Hounds_Cat (golden list), SpawnSystem entry for Meadows (rare), Tameable with fish as food.\n- Idle: wander near home, sit, purr (vanilla soft clip or CC0).\n- Comfort +1: patch SE_Rested comfort calc to add 1 when a tame cat is within ~5 m (capped at +1).\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Cats spawn rarely in Meadows and can be tamed with fish\n- [ ] Tame cat near the bed gives +1 comfort (once)\n- [ ] Purr audible near\n\n# Dependencies\nHounds H1: live test in Creative + release Hounds 0.1.0\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nCozy home companion; foundation for granary protection.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.3; parent goal bn-10n.\n","kind":"task","labels":["hounds","h2","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-10n","size":"m","title":"Hounds H2: wild cats in the Meadows - spawn, tame with fish, follow/idle/purr, comfort +1 nearby","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:JTrHR05X9oTU5DKmRbXdAamBo_AsH7hld33CnJqj9Ls
1791857918062033	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-wsa5	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.3: cats near food storage stop a pests loss, only if the Larder's spoilage is on.\n\n# Goals\nWhen Larder exposes a pests hook, a tame cat within range of a container prevents that loss.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nCoupling through Larder.Api (reflection) keeps both mods independent; Hounds simply answers 'is a cat guarding this position?'.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Hounds.Api: `bool CatGuards(Vector3 pos)` (Version 2).\n- Larder side calls it from its pests step (coordinate with Larder L3 spoilage task).\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] With Larder spoilage on, a chest with a cat nearby has no pests loss over 3 days; without the cat it does\n- [ ] Without Larder nothing happens\n\n# Dependencies\nHounds H2: wild cats in the Meadows - spawn, tame with fish, follow/idl\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nGives cats a real job; Jarldom's granary benefits via Larder.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.3; parent goal bn-10n.\n","kind":"task","labels":["hounds","h2","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-10n","size":"s","title":"Hounds H2: cats near food storage stop Larder's pests loss (only when Larder spoilage is on)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:NCUqJv4aUsIcTW3Z-RGphqcpdCi_pknmlzy3PlLUCGs
1791857918081062	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-77ts	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.3 Jarldom side: cats protect the granary.\n\n# Goals\nJarldom villagers use the standalone mod's features when it is installed, and nothing changes (no errors) when it is not.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nGround rule: no hard dependency in either direction; Jarldom resolves `<Mod>.Api` by reflection through the ApiRef helper (bn-1xw) and degrades to vanilla behaviour. Villager behaviour stays in Jarldom (spin-out rule).\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Store/stockpile rooms with a tame cat within range report 'guarded' in the colony window (via Hounds.Api.CatGuards).\n- Small comfort moodlet for villagers whose longhouse has a cat.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Colony window shows a guarded store when a cat is near\n- [ ] Without the mod installed Jarldom behaves exactly as before (no errors)\n- [ ] Jarldom released (version, changelog, dist); raise Plugin.DataVersion if record/soul formats change\n\n# Dependencies\nHounds H2: cats near food storage stop Larder's pests loss (only when L, bn-1xw\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nTies cats into colony life.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.3; parent goal bn-10n.\n","kind":"task","labels":["hounds","h2","next-saga","standalone","jarldom","integration"],"parent":"bn-10n","size":"s","title":"Jarldom: cats protect the granary (store rooms); a cat moodlet for villagers who keep one","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:4Ey1GgC7pBryZh8CdioXrlw6ip8IUmYbj_9IyL5KTQc
1791857918100307	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-389e	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone H2 of Hounds (spec section 3.3). Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, dist + manifest, for this mod only.\n\n# Goals\nProve H2 works in a real game and ship it.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nUnit tests cover pure logic but taming, AI, physics and status effects only show their problems live (see claudetools-live-game memory: mailbox commands, `reload <Mod>`). Never lose Bob's gear; check `siege status` and tributes before time jumps.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Run the README playtest checklist items for this milestone in Bob's Creative world via ClaudeTools.\n- Fix what breaks (file bugs as bones if not fixed now).\n- Update README checklist, CHANGELOG, DESCRIPTION; bump version; `mise run publish`; update dist/manifest.json.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tame a cat; comfort +1 near the bed\n- [ ] Works with Jarldom NOT installed\n- [ ] F6 reload mid-test leaves no duplicates/errors\n- [ ] Released as Hounds 0.2.0 in dist/manifest.json\n\n# Dependencies\nHounds H2: wild cats in the Meadows - spawn, tame with fish, follow/idl, Hounds H2: cats near food storage stop Larder's pests loss (only when L, Jarldom: cats protect the granary (store rooms); a cat moodlet for vi\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nShips a usable slice of Hounds so players get value before the whole goal is done.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.3; parent goal bn-10n.\n","kind":"task","labels":["hounds","h2","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-10n","size":"s","title":"Hounds H2: live test in Creative + release Hounds 0.2.0","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:88eCQAcvlUegHErZ-gJAzwvufDAJna2C-BqTZ5oym04
1791857918120996	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2rtv	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.3 falconry: catch a young hawk in the Mountains (BirdTrap-style bait trap if present). BirdTrap is Quad's mod at ~/repos/valheim-mods/mods/BirdTrap.\n\n# Goals\nA way to obtain a young hawk.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nIf BirdTrap is installed, reuse its trap (reflection/soft); otherwise ship our own simple bait trap piece. Avoid a hard dependency on Quad's mod.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Read BirdTrap's code for its trap and catch flow.\n- Hounds_HawkTrap piece (golden list) placed in Mountains with meat bait; after N in-game hours chance to hold Hounds_YoungHawk creature/item.\n- Hawk model: vanilla bird (seagull/crow) re-skin or Blender asset.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A baited trap in the Mountains yields a young hawk within a day or two\n- [ ] Works without BirdTrap installed\n\n# Dependencies\nHounds H2: live test in Creative + release Hounds 0.2.0\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nStart of the falconry loop.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.3; parent goal bn-10n.\n","kind":"task","labels":["hounds","h3","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-10n","size":"m","title":"Hounds H3: catch a young hawk in the Mountains with a bait trap (BirdTrap-style when present)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:pUEAi28EpQsfRLycA6dY97CARZ5YX7qjy7elKELR3og
1791857918141002	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3mes	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.3: train it, fly it from your glove at birds and small game; it returns with the kill.\n\n# Goals\nA falconry glove item: aim at a bird/hare, release the hawk, it strikes and brings back the drop.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nA scripted flight (curve to target, kill, curve back) is more reliable than physics AI and cheap on the network (one flight event, not a moving ZDO stream).\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Hounds_Glove item; Core/Flight.cs pure path math with tests.\n- Valid targets: birds, hares, small game; not bosses, not tames.\n- Training level raises success chance and range.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Hawk catches a hare/bird and returns the drop to the player\n- [ ] Missed strike returns empty\n- [ ] Path math unit-tested\n\n# Dependencies\nHounds H3: catch a young hawk in the Mountains with a bait trap (BirdTr\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nUnique hunting activity; Jarldom hunters get a hawk.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.3; parent goal bn-10n.\n","kind":"task","labels":["hounds","h3","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-10n","size":"m","title":"Hounds H3: train the hawk and fly it from your glove at birds and small game; it returns with the kill","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:JST101TwprQnDd7VWzLjhVwShZh7Xdgdp_Jc9_MfoZI
1791857918158690	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3gwc	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.3 Jarldom side: hunters a hawk.\n\n# Goals\nJarldom villagers use the standalone mod's features when it is installed, and nothing changes (no errors) when it is not.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nGround rule: no hard dependency in either direction; Jarldom resolves `<Mod>.Api` by reflection through the ApiRef helper (bn-1xw) and degrades to vanilla behaviour. Villager behaviour stays in Jarldom (spin-out rule).\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Hounds.Api: `bool HasHawk(owner)`/assign a hawk to a villager; Jarldom hunt task adds an abstract small-game yield when the hunter has one.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A hunter with a hawk yields extra hare/feathers over a day\n- [ ] Without the mod installed Jarldom behaves exactly as before (no errors)\n- [ ] Jarldom released (version, changelog, dist); raise Plugin.DataVersion if record/soul formats change\n\n# Dependencies\nHounds H3: train the hawk and fly it from your glove at birds and small, bn-1xw\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nRounds out the colony's use of the mod.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.3; parent goal bn-10n.\n","kind":"task","labels":["hounds","h3","next-saga","standalone","jarldom","integration"],"parent":"bn-10n","size":"s","title":"Jarldom: hunters with a trained hawk bring back extra small game","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:pUQeTKHKrU4Mvd-XzXzrXfBuv0Qp73JjC1gHPJ47dnY
1791857918178766	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2o5j	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone H3 of Hounds (spec section 3.3). Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, dist + manifest, for this mod only.\n\n# Goals\nProve H3 works in a real game and ship it.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nUnit tests cover pure logic but taming, AI, physics and status effects only show their problems live (see claudetools-live-game memory: mailbox commands, `reload <Mod>`). Never lose Bob's gear; check `siege status` and tributes before time jumps.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Run the README playtest checklist items for this milestone in Bob's Creative world via ClaudeTools.\n- Fix what breaks (file bugs as bones if not fixed now).\n- Update README checklist, CHANGELOG, DESCRIPTION; bump version; `mise run publish`; update dist/manifest.json.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Catch, train and fly a hawk\n- [ ] Works with Jarldom NOT installed\n- [ ] F6 reload mid-test leaves no duplicates/errors\n- [ ] Released as Hounds 0.3.0 in dist/manifest.json\n\n# Dependencies\nHounds H3: train the hawk and fly it from your glove at birds and small, Jarldom: hunters with a trained hawk bring back extra small game\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nShips a usable slice of Hounds so players get value before the whole goal is done.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.3; parent goal bn-10n.\n","kind":"task","labels":["hounds","h3","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-10n","size":"s","title":"Hounds H3: live test in Creative + release Hounds 0.3.0","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:lZ96PAvQIKvBJdHEkrAzORFAYlIt1HZXmd2hn5slXmA
1791857918198531	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1ou8	{"description":"# Context & Background\nFirst task of the Horses standalone mod (spec section 3.4, goal bn-1k8). Nothing exists yet. Repo pattern: small mods like mods/Spyglass and mods/Delivery (csproj net48 via mods/Directory.Build.props, Plugin.cs, pure logic files, CHANGELOG.txt, DESCRIPTION.txt, cover.jpg), tests in tests/<Mod>.Tests (Program.cs check-style runner), mise tasks build/test/verify/publish/install, dist/manifest.json catalog for the F7 mod manager.\n\n# Goals\nAn empty-but-loadable Horses plugin that every later Horses task drops code into, with the ground rules wired in from day one.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nDoing the scaffold once up front means each feature task stays s/m and the ground rules (prefix names, server-authoritative settings, F6 reload, pure Core logic, tool command, golden prefab list) are not forgotten per feature. Horses needs a creature model; budget asset work early (Blender pipeline, see blender-anim-pipeline memory).\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- mods/Horses/Horses.csproj, Plugin.cs (BepInEx plugin com.bobisme.horses, server-synced ConfigEntries, clean OnDestroy for F6 reload).\n- mods/Horses/Core/ for pure C# (no Unity) linked into tests/Horses.Tests.\n- A ClaudeTools command root `horses` (status/help first) following Jarldom's Tools/Tools.cs pattern.\n- README with a playtest checklist section, DESCRIPTION.txt, CHANGELOG.txt, cover.jpg placeholder, dist/manifest.json entry.\n- tests/Horses.Tests/prefabs.txt golden list (empty to start) + the superset test from foundation bone bn-2vn.\n- Read ~/repos/valheim-claude-tools/docs/modding-pitfalls.md before writing items.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `mise run build` and `mise run test` pass with Horses included\n- [ ] Plugin loads and F6-reloads cleanly in game with no errors\n- [ ] `horses status` tool command answers\n- [ ] Golden prefab list test exists\n- [ ] No dependency on Jarldom or any other Bob mod\n\n# Dependencies\nbn-2vn\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFoundation for the whole Horses goal; keeps it useful on its own per the standalone ground rule.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.4; parent goal bn-1k8.\n","kind":"task","labels":["horses","r1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-1k8","size":"s","title":"Horses: scaffold mods/Horses project (csproj, Plugin, Core/, tests/Horses.Tests, README checklist, manifest entry, tool command, prefab golden list)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:_LnYWFns1pOEb0bwg9y2c4TIX9nX8hIdmUK3bZ2oBXE
1791857918219570	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1f59	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.4: wild herds in the Meadows and Plains. No horse exists in vanilla.\n\n# Goals\nA horse creature that spawns in herds and behaves like skittish prey.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nAsset is the long pole: either adapt the Lox rig (riding already works on Lox via Sadle) with a new mesh, or a Blender-built model with clips via the Blender -> JSON clip pipeline. Lox rig reuse gives riding/saddle code for free.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Investigate Lox prefab (Sadle, Tameable, Procreation) as the base; prefab Horses_Horse (golden list).\n- SpawnSystem herds 3-6 in Meadows/Plains; flee AI (AnimalAI).\n- Vanilla hoof/neigh-like clips if any, else CC0 listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Herds spawn and flee\n- [ ] Model and animations look right walking/running\n- [ ] No errors on F6 reload\n\n# Dependencies\nHorses: scaffold mods/Horses project (csproj, Plugin, Core/, tests/H\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nEverything else in Horses rides on this.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.4; parent goal bn-1k8.\n","kind":"task","labels":["horses","r1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-1k8","size":"m","title":"Horses R1: horse creature (model, animations, herds) spawning wild in Meadows and Plains","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:9LeRkLtcejAN2LPZJibPEdflOhS1ceD6VBg_Z5OjTMY
1791857918239240	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2n21	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.4: catch with a rope, break in by riding (it bucks, you hold on with stamina).\n\n# Goals\nA rope item to catch a wild horse, then a breaking-in ride where bucking drains stamina; success tames it.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nReplaces vanilla feed-taming with something horse-like; pure state machine is testable.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Horses_Rope item (golden list); throw/use on a horse within range to lasso (holds it in place briefly).\n- Core/Breaking.cs: buck intensity vs player stamina; thrown off -> horse escapes; win -> Tameable.Tame().\n- Tool: `horses spawn`, `horses tame`.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Rope catches a wild horse\n- [ ] Breaking ride can be won and lost\n- [ ] State machine unit-tested\n\n# Dependencies\nHorses R1: horse creature (model, animations, herds) spawning wild in M\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nThe signature horse interaction.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.4; parent goal bn-1k8.\n","kind":"task","labels":["horses","r1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-1k8","size":"m","title":"Horses R1: catch with a rope and break in by riding (bucking minigame drains stamina)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:JCQN_UfLPoXc9dvvbtwyV6TSOyMmOR6ohb1ROxg99iA
1791857918259611	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1t81	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.4: saddles in tiers; stamina and speed.\n\n# Goals\nTiered saddles (e.g. leather, bronze-fitted, iron-fitted) that improve the ride.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nReuse vanilla Sadle component as Lox does for controls and stamina; tiers adjust speed/stamina values.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Horses_Saddle_T1..T3 items (golden list), recipes at workbench/forge.\n- Sadle values per tier from a pure table with tests.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each tier rides with distinct speed/stamina\n- [ ] Mount/dismount works in multiplayer\n\n# Dependencies\nHorses R1: catch with a rope and break in by riding (bucking minigame d\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nMakes horses a real travel option.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.4; parent goal bn-1k8.\n","kind":"task","labels":["horses","r1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-1k8","size":"m","title":"Horses R1: saddles in tiers (stamina and speed) + riding controls","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:QieJFvG-dFi2D7nysv-Gp5D_RcGugQRoRkeDR4XF5kk
1791857918278982	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2k0y	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone R1 of Horses (spec section 3.4). Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, dist + manifest, for this mod only.\n\n# Goals\nProve R1 works in a real game and ship it.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nUnit tests cover pure logic but taming, AI, physics and status effects only show their problems live (see claudetools-live-game memory: mailbox commands, `reload <Mod>`). Never lose Bob's gear; check `siege status` and tributes before time jumps.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Run the README playtest checklist items for this milestone in Bob's Creative world via ClaudeTools.\n- Fix what breaks (file bugs as bones if not fixed now).\n- Update README checklist, CHANGELOG, DESCRIPTION; bump version; `mise run publish`; update dist/manifest.json.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Catch, break in, saddle and ride a horse\n- [ ] Works with Jarldom NOT installed\n- [ ] F6 reload mid-test leaves no duplicates/errors\n- [ ] Released as Horses 0.1.0 in dist/manifest.json\n\n# Dependencies\nHorses R1: saddles in tiers (stamina and speed) + riding controls\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nShips a usable slice of Horses so players get value before the whole goal is done.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.4; parent goal bn-1k8.\n","kind":"task","labels":["horses","r1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-1k8","size":"s","title":"Horses R1: live test in Creative + release Horses 0.1.0","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:dZoTaWuOjgBSGtMvQ3-VZoLH_VsVyagrQZZiR1XNRPc
1791857918298140	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2kvl	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.4: breeding with inherited speed and stamina.\n\n# Goals\nFoals inherit speed and stamina from parents with some variance.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nA pure inheritance function (parent average + bounded noise) is easy to test and balance; stored as two small ZDO floats.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Core/Genes.cs: Inherit(a, b, rng) with tests for bounds and mean.\n- Patch Procreation to stamp foal keys; Growup copies them.\n- Hover shows speed/stamina grades.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Foal stats lie between parents +/- variance\n- [ ] Stats survive growth and reload\n\n# Dependencies\nHorses R1: live test in Creative + release Horses 0.1.0\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nLong-term goal for horse players.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.4; parent goal bn-1k8.\n","kind":"task","labels":["horses","r2","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-1k8","size":"m","title":"Horses R2: breeding with inherited speed and stamina (pure genetics + tests)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:gkSqBQhIzAJZ3xpql24eN-qlJ7IULIMpSfpSca9w2oE
1791857918316360	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3one	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.4: brushing for a bond bonus.\n\n# Goals\nA brush item; brushing daily raises bond; bond adds a small bonus and decays slowly.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nGives a daily care ritual without punishing absence harshly.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Horses_Brush item; Core bond decay/gain table with tests.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Brushing raises bond (once per day)\n- [ ] Bonus visible on hover and applied when riding\n\n# Dependencies\nHorses R2: breeding with inherited speed and stamina (pure genetics + t\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nAdds attachment to individual horses.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.4; parent goal bn-1k8.\n","kind":"task","labels":["horses","r2","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-1k8","size":"s","title":"Horses R2: brushing gives a bond bonus (small speed/stamina boost while bond is high)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:U9nLlL9SuwmpzPM13hXUN_kroAAIt-v_WYG6uN88Bwg
1791857918335207	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1stv	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone R2 of Horses (spec section 3.4). Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, dist + manifest, for this mod only.\n\n# Goals\nProve R2 works in a real game and ship it.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nUnit tests cover pure logic but taming, AI, physics and status effects only show their problems live (see claudetools-live-game memory: mailbox commands, `reload <Mod>`). Never lose Bob's gear; check `siege status` and tributes before time jumps.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Run the README playtest checklist items for this milestone in Bob's Creative world via ClaudeTools.\n- Fix what breaks (file bugs as bones if not fixed now).\n- Update README checklist, CHANGELOG, DESCRIPTION; bump version; `mise run publish`; update dist/manifest.json.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Breed two horses; foal stats inherit\n- [ ] Brush bonus applies\n- [ ] Works with Jarldom NOT installed\n- [ ] F6 reload mid-test leaves no duplicates/errors\n- [ ] Released as Horses 0.2.0 in dist/manifest.json\n\n# Dependencies\nHorses R2: brushing gives a bond bonus (small speed/stamina boost while\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nShips a usable slice of Horses so players get value before the whole goal is done.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.4; parent goal bn-1k8.\n","kind":"task","labels":["horses","r2","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-1k8","size":"s","title":"Horses R2: live test in Creative + release Horses 0.2.0","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:_lnryw1VaGMvvBB1Z7nxteDMuTa39VF5OmWiZl7yiT8
1791857918354911	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-27re	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.4 teams: harness one horse to a cart (PassengerCart through its API, or the game's cart). Open decision #57 (bn-1jv) says carts stay Jarldom behaviour on the game's cart and integrate via Horses/PassengerCart APIs.\n\n# Goals\nA horse pulls a vanilla Cart or PassengerCart instead of the player.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nVanilla Vagon attaches to a player; attaching to a horse means driving the horse's position as the attach point. PassengerCart (mods/PassengerCart) is a cart clone with seats, so the same attach works through a PassengerCart.Api.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Harness: E on a cart while riding/leading a tamed horse attaches it (Vagon attach joint to horse rigidbody).\n- PassengerCart.Api: add if missing (Version, IsPassengerCart) - release PassengerCart.\n- Gotcha: PassengerCart's public-field Instantiate (see passengercart-design memory).\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Horse pulls a loaded vanilla cart over Meadows\n- [ ] Horse pulls a PassengerCart with passengers\n- [ ] Detach works; no physics explosions\n\n# Dependencies\nHorses R2: live test in Creative + release Horses 0.2.0, bn-1jv\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nOverland transport; Jarldom carters can ride/drive.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.4; parent goal bn-1k8.\n","kind":"task","labels":["horses","r3","next-saga","standalone","passengercart"],"parent":"bn-1k8","size":"m","title":"Horses R3: harness a horse to a cart (PassengerCart via its Api, or the game's cart)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:IXebyG-Br5iyJbx-BK5CktcWV4f3kwXy3_STHGZxB-w
1791857918373992	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3v00	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.4: harness to a plow (Fields). The plow is Fields F2 (fork-owned elsewhere in this goal set).\n\n# Goals\nWhen Fields is installed, a harnessed horse pulls its plow faster than an ox/player.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nSoft reflection to Fields.Api so neither mod depends on the other.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Horses.Api `bool IsHarnessable(Character)`; Fields plow asks it.\n- Coordinate with the Fields plow task.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] With Fields installed, a horse tills a strip\n- [ ] Without Fields nothing breaks\n\n# Dependencies\nHorses R3: harness a horse to a cart (PassengerCart via its Api, or the, Fields F2: plow - a horse or ox team tills a strip at once\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFarming power for both players and Jarldom farmers.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.4; parent goal bn-1k8.\n","kind":"task","labels":["horses","r3","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-1k8","size":"s","title":"Horses R3: harness a horse to the Fields plow (via Fields.Api)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:A_uAjCpAEBUotKYDfPop8A2AVWnUjZ0YJ5yG8t-WZXg
1791857918393370	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1ra0	{"description":"# Context & Background\nGround rule: tiny static Api for Jarldom.\n\n# Goals\nA stable reflection Api for Jarldom carters/scouts/races.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nSmall and string/primitive-typed.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- mods/Horses/Api.cs per bn-1xw convention.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Api compiles; safe defaults for non-horses\n\n# Dependencies\nHorses R3: harness a horse to a cart (PassengerCart via its Api, or the, bn-1xw\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nEnables the Jarldom side.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.4; parent goal bn-1k8.\n","kind":"task","labels":["horses","r3","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-1k8","size":"s","title":"Horses R3: publish Horses.Api (Version, IsHorse, IsTame, Speed, Stamina, Harness)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:JKzSUcZFCc9YZLcvb6R9jUKqrXugF3J0fU1vO9Lrkv4
1791857918412593	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-ra1z	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.4 Jarldom side: carters and scouts ride; plowed fields yield more. Carters live in World/Carts.cs (abstract trips); scouts in ScoutTask.\n\n# Goals\nJarldom villagers use the standalone mod's features when it is installed, and nothing changes (no errors) when it is not.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nGround rule: no hard dependency in either direction; Jarldom resolves `<Mod>.Api` by reflection through the ApiRef helper (bn-1xw) and degrades to vanilla behaviour. Villager behaviour stays in Jarldom (spin-out rule).\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- A colony with tamed horses assigns them to carters (faster/abstract trip time shortened) and scouts (larger map reveal radius per trip).\n- Plowed fields (Fields.Api plowed flag) give a yield bonus to Jarldom farmers.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Carter trip time drops with a horse\n- [ ] Scout reveals more with a horse\n- [ ] Without the mod installed Jarldom behaves exactly as before (no errors)\n- [ ] Jarldom released (version, changelog, dist); raise Plugin.DataVersion if record/soul formats change\n\n# Dependencies\nHorses R3: publish Horses.Api (Version, IsHorse, IsTame, Speed, Stamina, bn-1xw\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nMakes horses matter to the colony.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.4; parent goal bn-1k8.\n","kind":"task","labels":["horses","r3","next-saga","standalone","jarldom","integration"],"parent":"bn-1k8","size":"m","title":"Jarldom: carters and scouts ride horses; plowed fields yield more","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:xWEPPpkAimzXA4S5QlL9iSkV2TTTkU8NKDuScdWgDxQ
1791857918432112	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-28r3	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.4: horse races at Midsummer. The festival itself is J4 #29 (another fork's bone).\n\n# Goals\nDuring Midsummer, villagers with horses race a short course; winner gets a moodlet and a byname line.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nSimulated/abstract race (speed stats + noise) shown as horses running a loop; low risk.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Hook into Jarldom's Midsummer event; uses Horses.Api.Speed.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Midsummer with 2+ horses runs a race and announces a winner\n\n# Dependencies\nJarldom: carters and scouts ride horses; plowed fields yield more, bn-1xw\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFestival colour.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.4; parent goal bn-1k8.\n","kind":"task","labels":["horses","r3","next-saga","standalone","jarldom","integration","j4"],"parent":"bn-1k8","size":"s","title":"Jarldom + Horses: horse races at Midsummer (J4 #29)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:O7pJf__2SY8BF8LqH8mEDQJTIQq35bnWCPNytTdPRvc
1791857918451511	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1kpz	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone R3 of Horses (spec section 3.4). Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, dist + manifest, for this mod only.\n\n# Goals\nProve R3 works in a real game and ship it.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nUnit tests cover pure logic but taming, AI, physics and status effects only show their problems live (see claudetools-live-game memory: mailbox commands, `reload <Mod>`). Never lose Bob's gear; check `siege status` and tributes before time jumps.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Run the README playtest checklist items for this milestone in Bob's Creative world via ClaudeTools.\n- Fix what breaks (file bugs as bones if not fixed now).\n- Update README checklist, CHANGELOG, DESCRIPTION; bump version; `mise run publish`; update dist/manifest.json.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Harness to a cart and a plow\n- [ ] Works with Jarldom NOT installed\n- [ ] F6 reload mid-test leaves no duplicates/errors\n- [ ] Released as Horses 0.3.0 in dist/manifest.json\n\n# Dependencies\nHorses R3: harness a horse to a cart (PassengerCart via its Api, or the, Horses R3: harness a horse to the Fields plow (via Fields.Api), Jarldom: carters and scouts ride horses; plowed fields yield more, Jarldom + Horses: horse races at Midsummer (J4 #29)\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nShips a usable slice of Horses so players get value before the whole goal is done.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.4; parent goal bn-1k8.\n","kind":"task","labels":["horses","r3","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-1k8","size":"s","title":"Horses R3: live test in Creative + release Horses 0.3.0","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:ZEM_NmhYYXyQ-Sd0NQ88iNvZvNRLKvsg64TCKtEb4ss
1791857918471160	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-vxo8	{"description":"# Context & Background\nFirst task of the Larder standalone mod (spec section 3.5, goal bn-3ci). Nothing exists yet. Repo pattern: small mods like mods/Spyglass and mods/Delivery (csproj net48 via mods/Directory.Build.props, Plugin.cs, pure logic files, CHANGELOG.txt, DESCRIPTION.txt, cover.jpg), tests in tests/<Mod>.Tests (Program.cs check-style runner), mise tasks build/test/verify/publish/install, dist/manifest.json catalog for the F7 mod manager.\n\n# Goals\nAn empty-but-loadable Larder plugin that every later Larder task drops code into, with the ground rules wired in from day one.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nDoing the scaffold once up front means each feature task stays s/m and the ground rules (prefix names, server-authoritative settings, F6 reload, pure Core logic, tool command, golden prefab list) are not forgotten per feature. Larder adds many food items; golden prefab list matters most here.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- mods/Larder/Larder.csproj, Plugin.cs (BepInEx plugin com.bobisme.larder, server-synced ConfigEntries, clean OnDestroy for F6 reload).\n- mods/Larder/Core/ for pure C# (no Unity) linked into tests/Larder.Tests.\n- A ClaudeTools command root `larder` (status/help first) following Jarldom's Tools/Tools.cs pattern.\n- README with a playtest checklist section, DESCRIPTION.txt, CHANGELOG.txt, cover.jpg placeholder, dist/manifest.json entry.\n- tests/Larder.Tests/prefabs.txt golden list (empty to start) + the superset test from foundation bone bn-2vn.\n- Read ~/repos/valheim-claude-tools/docs/modding-pitfalls.md before writing items.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `mise run build` and `mise run test` pass with Larder included\n- [ ] Plugin loads and F6-reloads cleanly in game with no errors\n- [ ] `larder status` tool command answers\n- [ ] Golden prefab list test exists\n- [ ] No dependency on Jarldom or any other Bob mod\n\n# Dependencies\nbn-2vn\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFoundation for the whole Larder goal; keeps it useful on its own per the standalone ground rule.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.5; parent goal bn-3ci.\n","kind":"task","labels":["larder","l1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3ci","size":"s","title":"Larder: scaffold mods/Larder project (csproj, Plugin, Core/, tests/Larder.Tests, README checklist, manifest entry, tool command, prefab golden list)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:A4Ko2bEwcuRBrEY1uMke2F1PryN3tELyGo6xHlRaV5E
1791857918491965	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1vnb	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.5: new mid-tier preserved foods made for long voyages; preserved food never spoils.\n\n# Goals\nA small, balanced set of preserved foods (Larder_Stockfish, Larder_SmokedMeat, Larder_SmokedFish, Larder_SaltMeat ...).\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nBalanced against vanilla mid-tier (Black Forest/Swamp) foods; long duration, modest stats = the voyage niche.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Data table in Core/Foods.cs (hp/stam/regen/duration) with tests that they sit inside a band of vanilla tiers.\n- Item clones of vanilla food prefabs with new icons/meshes; golden list.\n- 'Preserved' flag readable by Larder.Api and Jarldom.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Foods eat and show stats\n- [ ] Balance test passes\n- [ ] Prefab names in golden list\n\n# Dependencies\nLarder: scaffold mods/Larder project (csproj, Plugin, Core/, tests/L\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nThe payoff for the preservation stations.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.5; parent goal bn-3ci.\n","kind":"task","labels":["larder","l1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3ci","size":"m","title":"Larder L1: mid-tier preserved foods for long voyages (stockfish, smoked meat/fish, salted meat) with balanced stats","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:AjFOEqp-CKf4uCiVuM8P5dNy4fPdSvnI6KLiAKTcQSQ
1791857918511618	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1p8b	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.5 smokehouse (meat and fish).\n\n# Goals\nA station that converts raw meat/fish to smoked versions over time while fuelled.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nClone the vanilla Smelter/kiln pattern (fuel + input queue + timer) - proven, saves its state on the ZDO.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Larder_Smokehouse piece from Smelter component; conversions table.\n- Needs a roof? No - works outdoors; smoke vfx from vanilla.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Fuelled smokehouse produces smoked meat/fish\n- [ ] Queue survives reload\n\n# Dependencies\nLarder L1: mid-tier preserved foods for long voyages (stockfish, smoked\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFirst preservation station.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.5; parent goal bn-3ci.\n","kind":"task","labels":["larder","l1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3ci","size":"m","title":"Larder L1: smokehouse piece (fuel + raw meat/fish -> smoked over time)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:bVcZzG5Vsjw3foawIWWQd6UQS4hbq6zvd2fzDaZLqfA
1791857918531914	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-ooc0	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.5 salting barrel.\n\n# Goals\nA barrel that salts meat over time.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nFermenter-like component (input, timer, output). Salt source: decide (sea water boiled? a coastal rock pickable?) and note it in the README.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Larder_SaltBarrel piece (Fermenter clone); salt item Larder_Salt from a coastal pickable or boiled from sea water at a cauldron.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Barrel produces salted meat\n\n# Dependencies\nLarder L1: mid-tier preserved foods for long voyages (stockfish, smoked\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nSecond preservation route.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.5; parent goal bn-3ci.\n","kind":"task","labels":["larder","l1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3ci","size":"s","title":"Larder L1: salting barrel (salt source + meat -> salted meat)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:awL5flV3Dnx5YOS8qQgJWDwQLMaPIc7tZgidkBsSAbU
1791857918550308	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2xo6	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.5 stockfish drying racks: fish dries outdoors over days.\n\n# Goals\nA rack where hung fish turns into stockfish after N in-game days outdoors (not under a roof).\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nOutdoor-only matches real stockfish and gives a building choice.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Larder_DryingRack piece with slots (ItemStand-like) and a timer per slot; roof check via vanilla Cover.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Fish on an outdoor rack becomes stockfish after the set days\n- [ ] Under a roof it does not dry\n\n# Dependencies\nLarder L1: mid-tier preserved foods for long voyages (stockfish, smoked\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nIconic Norse food.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.5; parent goal bn-3ci.\n","kind":"task","labels":["larder","l1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3ci","size":"s","title":"Larder L1: stockfish drying racks (fish dries outdoors over days)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:6G6dD0vIc_dOk0Y3pzeK8CzZu6U3TIjHZ9ThxNtzFt0
1791857918569603	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-rk0x	{"description":"# Context & Background\nGround rule: tiny static Api. Jarldom cooks and expedition supplies need to know preserved food; Hounds cats need a pests hook later (Version 2).\n\n# Goals\nA stable Api.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nKeep primitive types.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- mods/Larder/Api.cs per bn-1xw.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] IsPreserved true for the new foods, false otherwise\n\n# Dependencies\nLarder L1: mid-tier preserved foods for long voyages (stockfish, smoked, bn-1xw\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nEnables Jarldom side.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.5; parent goal bn-3ci.\n","kind":"task","labels":["larder","l1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3ci","size":"s","title":"Larder L1: publish Larder.Api (Version, IsPreserved(item), plus later spoilage hooks)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:3XMFOkj_XordHvzjqWICuisYFB3wVHR04dbxoEE1Q00
1791857918589407	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2o31	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.5 Jarldom side: cooks preserve food; expedition supplies; winter stores; food variety for mood.\n\n# Goals\nJarldom villagers use the standalone mod's features when it is installed, and nothing changes (no errors) when it is not.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nGround rule: no hard dependency in either direction; Jarldom resolves `<Mod>.Api` by reflection through the ApiRef helper (bn-1xw) and degrades to vanilla behaviour. Villager behaviour stays in Jarldom (spin-out rule).\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Cook work: tend smokehouse/barrel/racks like cauldron/fermenters (existing cook brewing pattern).\n- Expedition supply picking (J6 #53) prefers IsPreserved food.\n- Food variety counts Larder foods for the mood need.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A cook fills and empties a smokehouse\n- [ ] Expedition supplies include preserved food when available\n- [ ] Without the mod installed Jarldom behaves exactly as before (no errors)\n- [ ] Jarldom released (version, changelog, dist); raise Plugin.DataVersion if record/soul formats change\n\n# Dependencies\nLarder L1: publish Larder.Api (Version, IsPreserved(item), plus later s, Larder L1: smokehouse piece (fuel + raw meat/fish -> smoked over time), Larder L1: salting barrel (salt source + meat -> salted meat), Larder L1: stockfish drying racks (fish dries outdoors over days), bn-1xw\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFeeds J6 expeditions and the food need.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.5; parent goal bn-3ci.\n","kind":"task","labels":["larder","l1","next-saga","standalone","jarldom","integration"],"parent":"bn-3ci","size":"m","title":"Jarldom: cooks preserve food at Larder stations; expeditions pack preserved supplies","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:xN6hhLruqXJvgSu5-Y2Wo3HgVPLYTw2Z3l9hSlrlYU0
1791857918610324	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1a46	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone L1 of Larder (spec section 3.5). Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, dist + manifest, for this mod only.\n\n# Goals\nProve L1 works in a real game and ship it.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nUnit tests cover pure logic but taming, AI, physics and status effects only show their problems live (see claudetools-live-game memory: mailbox commands, `reload <Mod>`). Never lose Bob's gear; check `siege status` and tributes before time jumps.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Run the README playtest checklist items for this milestone in Bob's Creative world via ClaudeTools.\n- Fix what breaks (file bugs as bones if not fixed now).\n- Update README checklist, CHANGELOG, DESCRIPTION; bump version; `mise run publish`; update dist/manifest.json.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Make each preserved food\n- [ ] Works with Jarldom NOT installed\n- [ ] F6 reload mid-test leaves no duplicates/errors\n- [ ] Released as Larder 0.1.0 in dist/manifest.json\n\n# Dependencies\nLarder L1: smokehouse piece (fuel + raw meat/fish -> smoked over time), Larder L1: salting barrel (salt source + meat -> salted meat), Larder L1: stockfish drying racks (fish dries outdoors over days), Jarldom: cooks preserve food at Larder stations; expeditions pack pre\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nShips a usable slice of Larder so players get value before the whole goal is done.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.5; parent goal bn-3ci.\n","kind":"task","labels":["larder","l1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3ci","size":"s","title":"Larder L1: live test in Creative + release Larder 0.1.0","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:9OzvdKKCX2zlEYx0l8tVBIXmY2p06NOdjj3dDh8lhNE
1791857918630811	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2hpm	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.5 dairy (butter churn, cheese press, skyr). Milk comes from Byre (goats S1, cattle S2).\n\n# Goals\nDairy stations and foods.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nMilk is a Byre item; Larder must still be useful without Byre, so the dairy pieces only appear useful when milk exists (recipes require Byre's milk prefab; hide when absent).\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Larder_Churn, Larder_CheesePress pieces; foods Larder_Butter, Larder_Cheese, Larder_Skyr.\n- Detect Byre's milk prefab by name in ObjectDB.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] With Byre milk: butter, cheese, skyr craftable\n- [ ] Without Byre: pieces hidden, no errors\n\n# Dependencies\nLarder L1: live test in Creative + release Larder 0.1.0\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nDairy chain for the cook and players.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.5; parent goal bn-3ci.\n","kind":"task","labels":["larder","l2","next-saga","standalone","byre"],"parent":"bn-3ci","size":"m","title":"Larder L2: dairy - butter churn, cheese press, skyr (milk from Byre)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:yds00tcqXreBafmLDomLPGmp2Tgra7LcBVQMfttTk7I
1791857918651236	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1ifu	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.5 bread oven (rye and barley breads). Barley is vanilla Plains; rye comes from Fields F1.\n\n# Goals\nAn oven piece and breads.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nVanilla already has an oven (bread from barley flour); ours adds Norse breads; rye bread only when Fields is present.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Larder_BreadOven piece (CookingStation/oven clone); Larder_RyeBread, Larder_FlatBread.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Barley bread works alone; rye bread with Fields\n\n# Dependencies\nLarder L1: live test in Creative + release Larder 0.1.0\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFood variety.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.5; parent goal bn-3ci.\n","kind":"task","labels":["larder","l2","next-saga","standalone","fields"],"parent":"bn-3ci","size":"s","title":"Larder L2: bread oven - rye and barley breads (rye from Fields when installed)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:GAytgAGh5_nL4eJ26rwgrjE6KY8iFPJbaG_uZw-By-0
1791857918669325	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1r4s	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone L2 of Larder (spec section 3.5). Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, dist + manifest, for this mod only.\n\n# Goals\nProve L2 works in a real game and ship it.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nUnit tests cover pure logic but taming, AI, physics and status effects only show their problems live (see claudetools-live-game memory: mailbox commands, `reload <Mod>`). Never lose Bob's gear; check `siege status` and tributes before time jumps.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Run the README playtest checklist items for this milestone in Bob's Creative world via ClaudeTools.\n- Fix what breaks (file bugs as bones if not fixed now).\n- Update README checklist, CHANGELOG, DESCRIPTION; bump version; `mise run publish`; update dist/manifest.json.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Churn butter, press cheese, bake bread\n- [ ] Works with Jarldom NOT installed\n- [ ] F6 reload mid-test leaves no duplicates/errors\n- [ ] Released as Larder 0.2.0 in dist/manifest.json\n\n# Dependencies\nLarder L2: dairy - butter churn, cheese press, skyr (milk from Byre), Larder L2: bread oven - rye and barley breads (rye from Fields when ins\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nShips a usable slice of Larder so players get value before the whole goal is done.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.5; parent goal bn-3ci.\n","kind":"task","labels":["larder","l2","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3ci","size":"s","title":"Larder L2: live test in Creative + release Larder 0.2.0","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:k7txeDrNYfiuGKFeGHoNH3YH4K1-rgcznUlGWvaNSO0
1791857918688658	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2wn2	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.5 spoilage (toggle, OFF by default - decision bn-1bn): raw food spoils over days, slower in cold or roofed storage; preserved food never does.\n\n# Goals\nA tested pure model for spoilage.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nPure model first so balance can be tuned in tests without the game.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Core/Spoilage.cs: freshness per stack (store as item custom data, not per-tick writes), rate multipliers (cold biome, roof, root cellar), elapsed game time.\n- Tests for each multiplier and the never-spoils rule.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Unit tests cover rates, multipliers and preserved exemption\n\n# Dependencies\nLarder L2: live test in Creative + release Larder 0.2.0, bn-1bn\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nCore of L3.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.5; parent goal bn-3ci.\n","kind":"task","labels":["larder","l3","next-saga","standalone","toggle"],"parent":"bn-3ci","size":"m","title":"Larder L3: spoilage rules (pure) - rates by item, cold and roofed storage slow it, preserved never spoils","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:6tWet4c_6XZiVWM00vXq1LrOSnLEr4t5TFjjzKa-TZI
1791857918707068	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2h4f	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.5 spoilage toggle.\n\n# Goals\nFood in chests and inventories ages and becomes spoiled food when the server setting is on.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nApply lazily on container open/inventory load (elapsed time since last stamp) to avoid timers over every chest (perf-hitches memory).\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Server-synced setting Larder.Spoilage (default per bn-1bn).\n- Freshness shown in tooltip; Larder_SpoiledFood item (compost later?).\n- Hounds.Api.CatGuards pests hook here.\n- Pitfall check: never delete items silently; convert.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Off by default: nothing changes\n- [ ] On: raw meat in a warm chest spoils over days; preserved food never\n- [ ] Cat near a chest blocks pests loss (with Hounds)\n\n# Dependencies\nLarder L3: spoilage rules (pure) - rates by item, cold and roofed stora\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nOptional survival pressure.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.5; parent goal bn-3ci.\n","kind":"task","labels":["larder","l3","next-saga","standalone","toggle"],"parent":"bn-3ci","size":"m","title":"Larder L3: apply spoilage in containers and inventories (server toggle, off by default), spoiled food item","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:XqtbTELvlk9LS-F81nyIW-ZrojbUbORlndVQkUSovng
1791857918727121	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3w16	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.5 root cellar (a room type that slows spoilage).\n\n# Goals\nChests inside an enclosed, roofed, partly underground room spoil slower.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nRoom check via raycasts like Bathhouse's sauna check / Jarldom room rules; don't depend on Jarldom.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Core room test (roof, walls, below-ground depth or stone walls) with tests.\n- Multiplier applied by larder-spoil-game.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Chest in a cellar spoils at the cellar rate\n\n# Dependencies\nLarder L3: apply spoilage in containers and inventories (server toggle,\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nGives spoilage a building answer.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.5; parent goal bn-3ci.\n","kind":"task","labels":["larder","l3","next-saga","standalone","toggle"],"parent":"bn-3ci","size":"s","title":"Larder L3: root cellar room type that slows spoilage","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:lH9TZvjKb40jDIS-tyCQI0ecw7r_awc2R-h2FGm7KWE
1791857918745513	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2cst	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone L3 of Larder (spec section 3.5). Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, dist + manifest, for this mod only.\n\n# Goals\nProve L3 works in a real game and ship it.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nUnit tests cover pure logic but taming, AI, physics and status effects only show their problems live (see claudetools-live-game memory: mailbox commands, `reload <Mod>`). Never lose Bob's gear; check `siege status` and tributes before time jumps.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Run the README playtest checklist items for this milestone in Bob's Creative world via ClaudeTools.\n- Fix what breaks (file bugs as bones if not fixed now).\n- Update README checklist, CHANGELOG, DESCRIPTION; bump version; `mise run publish`; update dist/manifest.json.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Toggle spoilage on: raw spoils, preserved and cellar behave\n- [ ] Works with Jarldom NOT installed\n- [ ] F6 reload mid-test leaves no duplicates/errors\n- [ ] Released as Larder 0.3.0 in dist/manifest.json\n\n# Dependencies\nLarder L3: root cellar room type that slows spoilage\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nShips a usable slice of Larder so players get value before the whole goal is done.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.5; parent goal bn-3ci.\n","kind":"task","labels":["larder","l3","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-3ci","size":"s","title":"Larder L3: live test in Creative + release Larder 0.3.0","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:E1U1mnzNcVzajTwUFtzGWmgYbwrzyLvtuB1KZ4K1gWw
1791857918765841	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2p0p	{"description":"# Context & Background\nFirst task of the Fields standalone mod (spec section 3.6, goal bn-2q8). Nothing exists yet. Repo pattern: small mods like mods/Spyglass and mods/Delivery (csproj net48 via mods/Directory.Build.props, Plugin.cs, pure logic files, CHANGELOG.txt, DESCRIPTION.txt, cover.jpg), tests in tests/<Mod>.Tests (Program.cs check-style runner), mise tasks build/test/verify/publish/install, dist/manifest.json catalog for the F7 mod manager.\n\n# Goals\nAn empty-but-loadable Fields plugin that every later Fields task drops code into, with the ground rules wired in from day one.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nDoing the scaffold once up front means each feature task stays s/m and the ground rules (prefix names, server-authoritative settings, F6 reload, pure Core logic, tool command, golden prefab list) are not forgotten per feature. Fields must stay compatible with Bob's Farmhand mod (row planting/harvest).\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- mods/Fields/Fields.csproj, Plugin.cs (BepInEx plugin com.bobisme.fields, server-synced ConfigEntries, clean OnDestroy for F6 reload).\n- mods/Fields/Core/ for pure C# (no Unity) linked into tests/Fields.Tests.\n- A ClaudeTools command root `fields` (status/help first) following Jarldom's Tools/Tools.cs pattern.\n- README with a playtest checklist section, DESCRIPTION.txt, CHANGELOG.txt, cover.jpg placeholder, dist/manifest.json entry.\n- tests/Fields.Tests/prefabs.txt golden list (empty to start) + the superset test from foundation bone bn-2vn.\n- Read ~/repos/valheim-claude-tools/docs/modding-pitfalls.md before writing items.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `mise run build` and `mise run test` pass with Fields included\n- [ ] Plugin loads and F6-reloads cleanly in game with no errors\n- [ ] `fields status` tool command answers\n- [ ] Golden prefab list test exists\n- [ ] No dependency on Jarldom or any other Bob mod\n\n# Dependencies\nbn-2vn\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFoundation for the whole Fields goal; keeps it useful on its own per the standalone ground rule.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.6; parent goal bn-2q8.\n","kind":"task","labels":["fields","f1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-2q8","size":"s","title":"Fields: scaffold mods/Fields project (csproj, Plugin, Core/, tests/Fields.Tests, README checklist, manifest entry, tool command, prefab golden list)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:j6xqlgwKhWBfMavrppSr9hs30_K05tNt6OJBdGFPcW8
1791857918784849	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-25cc	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.6: new crops (rye, peas, cabbage, leeks, angelica, hops), each with a biome.\n\n# Goals\nSix plantable crops with seeds, growth, pickables and produce items.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nClone vanilla Plant/Pickable pattern (turnip/carrot) for each; keep names forever (Fields_Rye, Fields_RyeSeeds...).\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Data table in Core/Crops.cs (biome, grow time, yield) + tests.\n- Seed sources (traders, wild pickables, drops).\n- Golden prefab list.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each crop plants, grows only in its biome and harvests\n- [ ] Names in golden list\n\n# Dependencies\nFields: scaffold mods/Fields project (csproj, Plugin, Core/, tests/F\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nBase for the Fields mod and Larder breads.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.6; parent goal bn-2q8.\n","kind":"task","labels":["fields","f1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-2q8","size":"m","title":"Fields F1: new crops - rye, peas, cabbage, leeks, angelica, hops (seeds, plants, produce, biome rules)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:wepAJ9rmi_67odpeAxykEi9p6XLGfuSkf_c6XSkHiJ4
1791857918806139	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1f80	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.6: each crop has a season (with Seasons installed). Seasons is shudnal's mod; J4 also soft-integrates it.\n\n# Goals\nPlanting/growth respects the current season when Seasons is installed.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nRead Seasons' current season by reflection; never require it.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Investigate Seasons' public state (type/field names) and pin them in a Compat file with a version check.\n- Out-of-season: slower growth or no germination (decide; document).\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] With Seasons: winter planting of rye is blocked/slowed per table\n- [ ] Without Seasons: unchanged\n\n# Dependencies\nFields F1: new crops - rye, peas, cabbage, leeks, angelica, hops (seeds\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nSeasonal farming.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.6; parent goal bn-2q8.\n","kind":"task","labels":["fields","f1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-2q8","size":"s","title":"Fields F1: crop seasons via shudnal's Seasons (soft reflection); no Seasons = always in season","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:7JYP8grE1AJ1YuD5W0bklDk8nM7T-US_WYXe1ugecU0
1791857918825135	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-160x	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.6: Farmhand compatibility. Farmhand is Bob's mod in mods/Farmhand.\n\n# Goals\nFarmhand's row tools plant and harvest Fields crops.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nCheck how Farmhand recognises plants (Plant/Pickable components or names); fix on whichever side is generic.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Test planting a row of each crop with Farmhand; adjust Farmhand if it hardcodes vanilla names (release Farmhand then).\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Row planting and harvest work for all six crops\n\n# Dependencies\nFields F1: new crops - rye, peas, cabbage, leeks, angelica, hops (seeds\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nKeeps Bob's mods working together.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.6; parent goal bn-2q8.\n","kind":"task","labels":["fields","f1","next-saga","standalone","farmhand"],"parent":"bn-2q8","size":"s","title":"Fields F1: Farmhand compatibility - row planting and harvest work with the new crops","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:Zr3TBAnc4EqdnDulpGnd0iD6zgSWXUNCON80IQdqxTw
1791857918844638	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1qak	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone F1 of Fields (spec section 3.6). Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, dist + manifest, for this mod only.\n\n# Goals\nProve F1 works in a real game and ship it.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nUnit tests cover pure logic but taming, AI, physics and status effects only show their problems live (see claudetools-live-game memory: mailbox commands, `reload <Mod>`). Never lose Bob's gear; check `siege status` and tributes before time jumps.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Run the README playtest checklist items for this milestone in Bob's Creative world via ClaudeTools.\n- Fix what breaks (file bugs as bones if not fixed now).\n- Update README checklist, CHANGELOG, DESCRIPTION; bump version; `mise run publish`; update dist/manifest.json.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Plant and harvest every crop\n- [ ] Works with Jarldom NOT installed\n- [ ] F6 reload mid-test leaves no duplicates/errors\n- [ ] Released as Fields 0.1.0 in dist/manifest.json\n\n# Dependencies\nFields F1: crop seasons via shudnal's Seasons (soft reflection); no Sea, Fields F1: Farmhand compatibility - row planting and harvest work with \n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nShips a usable slice of Fields so players get value before the whole goal is done.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.6; parent goal bn-2q8.\n","kind":"task","labels":["fields","f1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-2q8","size":"s","title":"Fields F1: live test in Creative + release Fields 0.1.0","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:ZJJujcxYBlTTmFuTzik83EX_Ax0BMQdLqj8Oa2Vg4PY
1791857918863860	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-r73i	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.6: soil fertility for each tilled patch, drained by each harvest and restored by fallow, manure (from Byre) or rotation (legumes restore it).\n\n# Goals\nA per-patch fertility value that scales yield.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nStore per grid cell (e.g. 2 m) in a compact per-zone record, not per plant, to keep saves small; pure math is testable.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Core/Soil.cs: drain/restore/rotation rules + tests (legume peas restore; repeat crop drains faster).\n- World storage: per-zone ZDO or ZoneSystem global key blob; network-light.\n- Manure item from Byre (detect by name) adds fertility.\n- Hover shows soil state on cultivated ground.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Repeated rye on one patch lowers yield; peas then rye restores\n- [ ] Manure raises fertility (with Byre)\n- [ ] Unit tests cover rules\n\n# Dependencies\nFields F1: live test in Creative + release Fields 0.1.0\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nReal soil numbers for Jarldom #37 worn land.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.6; parent goal bn-2q8.\n","kind":"task","labels":["fields","f2","next-saga","standalone","byre"],"parent":"bn-2q8","size":"m","title":"Fields F2: soil fertility per tilled patch - drained by harvest, restored by fallow, manure, rotation (legumes)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:j5iqESZBdQA2_u_zqBa-6loWSfhirxtAPxJ2H_giQuM
1791857918884704	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-jly3	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.6: a plow (horse or ox team) that tills a strip at once. Horses mod (R3) and Byre cattle (S2) provide the team.\n\n# Goals\nA plow piece/vehicle that cultivates a strip behind it as it's pulled.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nVagon-like cart with a terrain cultivate op along its path (TerrainComp ops as in Shieldwall/Jarldom levelling, see jarldom-design gotchas: use v2 ops, not legacy persistent TerrainModifiers).\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Fields_Plow (cart clone); pulled by player (slow), Horses.Api horse, or Byre ox.\n- Cultivate via TerrainComp.DoOperation in a strip every N m.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Player-pulled plow tills slowly; a horse/ox tills faster\n- [ ] No legacy TerrainModifier objects left behind\n\n# Dependencies\nFields F1: live test in Creative + release Fields 0.1.0\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nBig-farm tool; Horses and Byre tie-in.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.6; parent goal bn-2q8.\n","kind":"task","labels":["fields","f2","next-saga","standalone","horses","byre"],"parent":"bn-2q8","size":"m","title":"Fields F2: plow - a horse or ox team tills a strip at once","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:pKjylwZJN0zojKmSJBU4OJpBf1qFsP8GkVfZ9qupALc
1791857918903815	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1toq	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.6 scarecrows.\n\n# Goals\nA scarecrow piece that protects crops nearby.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nVanilla crops are only eaten by... check: nothing eats crops in vanilla, so the scarecrow needs a reason - add a small chance of crop pecking by birds in Meadows (toggle) that the scarecrow prevents, or make it a fertility/yield bonus. Decide and document.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Fields_Scarecrow piece; Core rule + test.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Scarecrow effect works in radius as documented\n\n# Dependencies\nFields F1: live test in Creative + release Fields 0.1.0\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nClassic farm piece.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.6; parent goal bn-2q8.\n","kind":"task","labels":["fields","f2","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-2q8","size":"s","title":"Fields F2: scarecrows keep birds/critters off crops in a radius","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:UuI35Gydar71iU2becnpOaVWkjKLK481KNta8cuauj4
1791857918924918	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2xnu	{"description":"# Context & Background\nGround rule: tiny static Api. Jarldom farmers rotate crops; #37 worn land uses real soil numbers.\n\n# Goals\nStable Api for Jarldom.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nPrimitive types only.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- mods/Fields/Api.cs per bn-1xw.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Api returns sane values; defaults without data\n\n# Dependencies\nFields F2: soil fertility per tilled patch - drained by harvest, restor, bn-1xw\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nEnables the Jarldom side.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.6; parent goal bn-2q8.\n","kind":"task","labels":["fields","f2","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-2q8","size":"s","title":"Fields F2: publish Fields.Api (Version, Fertility(pos), IsPlowed(pos), CropOf(pickable))","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:S4zTDS_FJtunNSH4Eatts57P01KVkoTS2sS82tcaAs0
1791857918944265	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-9tpa	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.6 Jarldom side: farmers rotate crops; food variety; the fertility pressure from #37 uses real soil numbers. Jarldom farmers already hoe+sow+harvest+replant (Villager/Work.cs).\n\n# Goals\nJarldom villagers use the standalone mod's features when it is installed, and nothing changes (no errors) when it is not.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nGround rule: no hard dependency in either direction; Jarldom resolves `<Mod>.Api` by reflection through the ApiRef helper (bn-1xw) and degrades to vanilla behaviour. Villager behaviour stays in Jarldom (spin-out rule).\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Farmer sowing picks the crop by Fields.Api.Fertility (legumes on tired soil).\n- J5 #37 harvest counters defer to Fields fertility where available.\n- New crops count toward food variety.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Farmers sow peas on a tired patch\n- [ ] Worn-land overlay shows Fields fertility when installed\n- [ ] Without the mod installed Jarldom behaves exactly as before (no errors)\n- [ ] Jarldom released (version, changelog, dist); raise Plugin.DataVersion if record/soul formats change\n\n# Dependencies\nFields F2: publish Fields.Api (Version, Fertility(pos), IsPlowed(pos), , bn-1xw\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nIntegrates farming depth into the colony.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.6; parent goal bn-2q8.\n","kind":"task","labels":["fields","f2","next-saga","standalone","jarldom","integration","j5"],"parent":"bn-2q8","size":"m","title":"Jarldom: farmers rotate Fields crops by fertility; worn-land (#37) reads real soil numbers","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:Ytt9TL0O803C493-utoXENQML1OBnVtKLX8IXX9NWIU
1791857918966261	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2cfd	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone F2 of Fields (spec section 3.6). Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, dist + manifest, for this mod only.\n\n# Goals\nProve F2 works in a real game and ship it.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nUnit tests cover pure logic but taming, AI, physics and status effects only show their problems live (see claudetools-live-game memory: mailbox commands, `reload <Mod>`). Never lose Bob's gear; check `siege status` and tributes before time jumps.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Run the README playtest checklist items for this milestone in Bob's Creative world via ClaudeTools.\n- Fix what breaks (file bugs as bones if not fixed now).\n- Update README checklist, CHANGELOG, DESCRIPTION; bump version; `mise run publish`; update dist/manifest.json.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Fertility drains and restores\n- [ ] Plow a strip\n- [ ] Works with Jarldom NOT installed\n- [ ] F6 reload mid-test leaves no duplicates/errors\n- [ ] Released as Fields 0.2.0 in dist/manifest.json\n\n# Dependencies\nFields F2: plow - a horse or ox team tills a strip at once, Fields F2: scarecrows keep birds/critters off crops in a radius, Jarldom: farmers rotate Fields crops by fertility; worn-land (#37) re\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nShips a usable slice of Fields so players get value before the whole goal is done.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.6; parent goal bn-2q8.\n","kind":"task","labels":["fields","f2","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-2q8","size":"s","title":"Fields F2: live test in Creative + release Fields 0.2.0","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:f-IYj-GNZXzVGJqK-X8Vbztb3nKpxtiO4CUK2a0WqU8
1791857918986424	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3urf	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.6: apple trees (planted, years to bear).\n\n# Goals\nA plantable apple tree that matures slowly and then yields apples seasonally.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nLong maturity rewards long-lived worlds; use game days (configurable) and Seasons when present.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Fields_AppleSapling -> Fields_AppleTree (Plant -> tree with Pickable fruit regrowth).\n- Maturity in days configurable; tests for the schedule.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Sapling grows to a bearing tree after the set days\n- [ ] Apples regrow per season\n\n# Dependencies\nFields F2: live test in Creative + release Fields 0.2.0\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nOrchards.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.6; parent goal bn-2q8.\n","kind":"task","labels":["fields","f3","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-2q8","size":"m","title":"Fields F3: apple trees - planted saplings take years (colony/game days) to bear; apples and cider-able fruit","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:i1HHKDjpvM0usFpqYGyKNk8rRTqZO8l1AvsXZ8_Ve-k
1791857919007418	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-37nc	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.6: Idunn's apples are a rare late-game graft that gives a long, strong regen buff.\n\n# Goals\nA graft item (late-game ingredients) applied to a mature apple tree turning it into an Idunn tree with rare golden apples.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nLate-game gate keeps it special; buff balance tested against vanilla regen.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Fields_IdunnGraft (Mistlands/Ashlands-tier ingredients), Fields_IdunnApple food/consumable with SE regen buff.\n- Golden list.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Grafted tree yields rare golden apples\n- [ ] Buff duration/strength as documented\n\n# Dependencies\nFields F3: apple trees - planted saplings take years (colony/game days)\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nLate-game farming goal.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.6; parent goal bn-2q8.\n","kind":"task","labels":["fields","f3","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-2q8","size":"m","title":"Fields F3: Idunn's apples - rare late-game graft giving a long, strong regen buff","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:nSpDZmZKH70IFSc2B55f20gsRh9wD8eszKPV6nVjbqo
