1791857919047028	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-15hu	{"description":"# Context & Background\nFirst task of the Tafl standalone mod (spec section 3.9, goal bn-350). Nothing exists yet. Repo pattern: small mods like mods/Spyglass and mods/Delivery (csproj net48 via mods/Directory.Build.props, Plugin.cs, pure logic files, CHANGELOG.txt, DESCRIPTION.txt, cover.jpg), tests in tests/<Mod>.Tests (Program.cs check-style runner), mise tasks build/test/verify/publish/install, dist/manifest.json catalog for the F7 mod manager.\n\n# Goals\nAn empty-but-loadable Tafl plugin that every later Tafl task drops code into, with the ground rules wired in from day one.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nDoing the scaffold once up front means each feature task stays s/m and the ground rules (prefix names, server-authoritative settings, F6 reload, pure Core logic, tool command, golden prefab list) are not forgotten per feature. Tafl's rules engine and AI are pure C# and should be test-heavy.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- mods/Tafl/Tafl.csproj, Plugin.cs (BepInEx plugin com.bobisme.tafl, server-synced ConfigEntries, clean OnDestroy for F6 reload).\n- mods/Tafl/Core/ for pure C# (no Unity) linked into tests/Tafl.Tests.\n- A ClaudeTools command root `tafl` (status/help first) following Jarldom's Tools/Tools.cs pattern.\n- README with a playtest checklist section, DESCRIPTION.txt, CHANGELOG.txt, cover.jpg placeholder, dist/manifest.json entry.\n- tests/Tafl.Tests/prefabs.txt golden list (empty to start) + the superset test from foundation bone bn-2vn.\n- Read ~/repos/valheim-claude-tools/docs/modding-pitfalls.md before writing items.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `mise run build` and `mise run test` pass with Tafl included\n- [ ] Plugin loads and F6-reloads cleanly in game with no errors\n- [ ] `tafl status` tool command answers\n- [ ] Golden prefab list test exists\n- [ ] No dependency on Jarldom or any other Bob mod\n\n# Dependencies\nbn-2vn\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFoundation for the whole Tafl goal; keeps it useful on its own per the standalone ground rule.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.9; parent goal bn-350.\n","kind":"task","labels":["tafl","t1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-350","size":"s","title":"Tafl: scaffold mods/Tafl project (csproj, Plugin, Core/, tests/Tafl.Tests, README checklist, manifest entry, tool command, prefab golden list)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:K8hv5iDLyx-QdDZ9ZbWMiBpftCu8t9cHnXuSAdN9Lks
1791857919068397	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-ciz5	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.9: playable hnefatafl (11x11, standard rules). Jarldom's Villager/Leisure.cs already has an idle 'tafl' activity without a real game.\n\n# Goals\nA correct, fast rules engine: moves, captures (custodial, against throne/corners), king capture (4 sides / edge rules), shieldwall captures, edge forts if adopted, repetition, win/lose/draw.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nPick one documented ruleset (Copenhagen hnefatafl 11x11 is the de facto standard) and cite it in the README; pure engine reused by UI, AI and Jarldom simulation.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Core/Tafl/Board.cs, Rules.cs, Move generation; bitboard or array.\n- tests: capture cases, king escape at corners, throne hostility, repetition, illegal moves.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Rules documented in README\n- [ ] Test suite covers every capture and win rule\n- [ ] Legal move generation verified on known positions\n\n# Dependencies\nTafl: scaffold mods/Tafl project (csproj, Plugin, Core/, tests/Taf\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFoundation for PvP, AI and villagers' games.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.9; parent goal bn-350.\n","kind":"task","labels":["tafl","t1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-350","size":"m","title":"Tafl T1: hnefatafl rules engine (11x11, standard Copenhagen-style rules) - pure C# with exhaustive tests","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:8nDga8xJZgdIwxuzv6dNPVYhfGcbWAWQIhZ_XcYcNyg
1791857919089083	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-dd0f	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.9: a tafl board table piece, player vs player.\n\n# Goals\nA table piece where two players sit and play; state on the board's ZDO, moves via RPC to the owner.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nBoard state is small (121 cells + turn) so a ZDO byte[] is fine (still object, not moving). Owner validates moves with the rules engine.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Tafl_Board piece (table model + piece meshes from vanilla primitives/simple models).\n- Interaction: E to sit as attacker/defender; mouse pick piece/square; highlight legal moves.\n- Spectators see moves.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Two players finish a full game in multiplayer\n- [ ] Illegal moves rejected\n- [ ] Board state survives reload\n\n# Dependencies\nTafl T1: hnefatafl rules engine (11x11, standard Copenhagen-style rul\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nPlayable game in world.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.9; parent goal bn-350.\n","kind":"task","labels":["tafl","t1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-350","size":"m","title":"Tafl T1: tafl board table piece - 3D pieces, click to move, two seated players (PvP, network-synced)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:xK9nHXdZFDKskUz96CjgpKBVuPSNPfPu-7PUqKnDdLw
1791857919109591	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-390t	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone T1 of Tafl (spec section 3.9). Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, dist + manifest, for this mod only.\n\n# Goals\nProve T1 works in a real game and ship it.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nUnit tests cover pure logic but taming, AI, physics and status effects only show their problems live (see claudetools-live-game memory: mailbox commands, `reload <Mod>`). Never lose Bob's gear; check `siege status` and tributes before time jumps.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Run the README playtest checklist items for this milestone in Bob's Creative world via ClaudeTools.\n- Fix what breaks (file bugs as bones if not fixed now).\n- Update README checklist, CHANGELOG, DESCRIPTION; bump version; `mise run publish`; update dist/manifest.json.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Play a full PvP game\n- [ ] Works with Jarldom NOT installed\n- [ ] F6 reload mid-test leaves no duplicates/errors\n- [ ] Released as Tafl 0.1.0 in dist/manifest.json\n\n# Dependencies\nTafl T1: tafl board table piece - 3D pieces, click to move, two seate\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nShips a usable slice of Tafl so players get value before the whole goal is done.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.9; parent goal bn-350.\n","kind":"task","labels":["tafl","t1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-350","size":"s","title":"Tafl T1: live test in Creative + release Tafl 0.1.0","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:xRuG96jQiggyfGTynKb35-Wezhj3tYEZ4XiyBe_lZ-A
1791857919130552	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2qb2	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.9: vs an AI (search depth by difficulty).\n\n# Goals\nA competent AI at 3 difficulties that never stalls the frame.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nAlpha-beta with iterative deepening and a ms budget, run in a coroutine or worker thread on pure data (no Unity calls), keeps frame time safe.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Core/Tafl/Ai.cs: eval (king distance to corners, material, mobility); depth 1/2/4 by difficulty.\n- Tests: finds mate-in-1 escapes/captures; time cap respected.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] AI plays legal moves at each difficulty\n- [ ] Mate-in-1 found in tests\n- [ ] No frame hitch > 5 ms\n\n# Dependencies\nTafl T1: live test in Creative + release Tafl 0.1.0\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nSolo play and simulated villager games.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.9; parent goal bn-350.\n","kind":"task","labels":["tafl","t2","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-350","size":"m","title":"Tafl T2: AI opponent - alpha-beta search with depth by difficulty, evaluation function, time cap","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:uG0SlY2zX6VBVAnpBdNZ3ZoQHIJ1MK7Nbydl9cH8v2Y
1791857919151982	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-lsc6	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone T2 of Tafl (spec section 3.9). Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, dist + manifest, for this mod only.\n\n# Goals\nProve T2 works in a real game and ship it.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nUnit tests cover pure logic but taming, AI, physics and status effects only show their problems live (see claudetools-live-game memory: mailbox commands, `reload <Mod>`). Never lose Bob's gear; check `siege status` and tributes before time jumps.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Run the README playtest checklist items for this milestone in Bob's Creative world via ClaudeTools.\n- Fix what breaks (file bugs as bones if not fixed now).\n- Update README checklist, CHANGELOG, DESCRIPTION; bump version; `mise run publish`; update dist/manifest.json.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Beat (or lose to) the AI at each difficulty\n- [ ] Works with Jarldom NOT installed\n- [ ] F6 reload mid-test leaves no duplicates/errors\n- [ ] Released as Tafl 0.2.0 in dist/manifest.json\n\n# Dependencies\nTafl T2: AI opponent - alpha-beta search with depth by difficulty, ev\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nShips a usable slice of Tafl so players get value before the whole goal is done.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.9; parent goal bn-350.\n","kind":"task","labels":["tafl","t2","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-350","size":"s","title":"Tafl T2: live test in Creative + release Tafl 0.2.0","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:yVe2FnwLhty6mFmSNIKzlKwwiZ5fOu6KZup2eQ2Yryg
1791857919172826	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-24bg	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.9: dice (a cup, betting in coins).\n\n# Goals\nA dice cup item/table where players stake coins and roll.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nServer-authoritative roll (owner RNG) prevents client cheating; coins moved via vanilla inventory.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Tafl_DiceCup; simple game (highest roll wins pot); pitfall: item transfer must be atomic.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Two players bet and the winner receives the pot\n- [ ] No coin duplication on disconnect\n\n# Dependencies\nTafl T2: live test in Creative + release Tafl 0.2.0\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nTavern gambling.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.9; parent goal bn-350.\n","kind":"task","labels":["tafl","t3","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-350","size":"s","title":"Tafl T3: dice cup - roll dice and bet coins between players","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:3x8awtecARD-kwBK0nBDM1EU_QWMV6ugld1zWzQ91_s
1791857919193300	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-26ja	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.9: knattleikr (a ball and two bats on a marked field, simple rules, physics ball).\n\n# Goals\nA small physics sport: hit a ball with a bat across a marked field, score at ends.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nPhysics ball ownership is the tricky part in multiplayer; reuse Golf's ball approach (mods/Golf) if it fits.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Tafl_KnattBall, Tafl_KnattBat items; field marker piece defining ends; score display.\n- Check mods/Golf for ball sync code.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Two players can play a scored match\n- [ ] Ball sync acceptable in multiplayer\n\n# Dependencies\nTafl T2: live test in Creative + release Tafl 0.2.0\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nOutdoor sport.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.9; parent goal bn-350.\n","kind":"task","labels":["tafl","t3","next-saga","standalone","golf"],"parent":"bn-350","size":"m","title":"Tafl T3: knattleikr - ball, two bats, marked field, simple rules, physics ball","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:t74yIkcsh4USuTJJ6TVvy5jXbRXVaIK4q8k8qhQCKAo
1791857919214697	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3oxg	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone T3 of Tafl (spec section 3.9). Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, dist + manifest, for this mod only.\n\n# Goals\nProve T3 works in a real game and ship it.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nUnit tests cover pure logic but taming, AI, physics and status effects only show their problems live (see claudetools-live-game memory: mailbox commands, `reload <Mod>`). Never lose Bob's gear; check `siege status` and tributes before time jumps.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Run the README playtest checklist items for this milestone in Bob's Creative world via ClaudeTools.\n- Fix what breaks (file bugs as bones if not fixed now).\n- Update README checklist, CHANGELOG, DESCRIPTION; bump version; `mise run publish`; update dist/manifest.json.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Dice betting and a knattleikr match\n- [ ] Works with Jarldom NOT installed\n- [ ] F6 reload mid-test leaves no duplicates/errors\n- [ ] Released as Tafl 0.3.0 in dist/manifest.json\n\n# Dependencies\nTafl T3: dice cup - roll dice and bet coins between players, Tafl T3: knattleikr - ball, two bats, marked field, simple rules, phy\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nShips a usable slice of Tafl so players get value before the whole goal is done.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.9; parent goal bn-350.\n","kind":"task","labels":["tafl","t3","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-350","size":"s","title":"Tafl T3: live test in Creative + release Tafl 0.3.0","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:O6MoWpbXXLKtOrtjJ8NaN-DBwb5AWqy_nNZdP2_YJvs
1791857919236033	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-uyt3	{"description":"# Context & Background\nGround rule: tiny static Api; Jarldom villagers play tafl in the hall and can be challenged.\n\n# Goals\nApi to run simulated games and drive a board visibly.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nKeep primitive types.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- mods/Tafl/Api.cs per bn-1xw.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Simulated game returns winner and move list\n\n# Dependencies\nTafl T3: live test in Creative + release Tafl 0.3.0, bn-1xw\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nEnables Jarldom side.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.9; parent goal bn-350.\n","kind":"task","labels":["tafl","t4","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-350","size":"s","title":"Tafl T4: publish Tafl.Api (Version, SimulateGame(seed, skillA, skillB), board positions, StartGameVs(villager))","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:qlOqdMubgQCKnPImIfbB1COl8WaHOuoKy3LRmd386xc
1791857919255453	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3tyy	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.9 Jarldom side: villagers play tafl in the hall in the evenings (simulated games, shown with pieces moving); a tafl champion byname (uses J2 bynames); challenge a villager to a real game; a dice gambling moodlet (wins and losses). Leisure 'tafl' exists in Villager/Leisure.cs.\n\n# Goals\nJarldom villagers use the standalone mod's features when it is installed, and nothing changes (no errors) when it is not.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nGround rule: no hard dependency in either direction; Jarldom resolves `<Mod>.Api` by reflection through the ApiRef helper (bn-1xw) and degrades to vanilla behaviour. Villager behaviour stays in Jarldom (spin-out rule).\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Leisure tafl uses a nearby Tafl_Board when present: Tafl.Api simulated game animated move by move.\n- Track wins; champion byname via J2 byname system.\n- Challenge from the villager panel -> real game vs AI with villager's skill as difficulty.\n- Dice: win/lose moodlets.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Two villagers visibly play at the board in the evening\n- [ ] Champion byname appears after N wins\n- [ ] Player can challenge a villager\n- [ ] Without the mod installed Jarldom behaves exactly as before (no errors)\n- [ ] Jarldom released (version, changelog, dist); raise Plugin.DataVersion if record/soul formats change\n\n# Dependencies\nTafl T4: publish Tafl.Api (Version, SimulateGame(seed, skillA, skillB, bn-1xw\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nEvening culture in the colony.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.9; parent goal bn-350.\n","kind":"task","labels":["tafl","t4","next-saga","standalone","jarldom","integration","j2"],"parent":"bn-350","size":"m","title":"Jarldom: villagers play real tafl in the hall evenings (pieces move), tafl champion byname, challenge a villager, dice moodlet","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:qiuUVMnU4qLU31_a4RDj3aDM2_YAthnjpGgvAHaI62o
1791857919275134	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-lio7	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone T4 of Tafl (spec section 3.9). Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, dist + manifest, for this mod only.\n\n# Goals\nProve T4 works in a real game and ship it.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nUnit tests cover pure logic but taming, AI, physics and status effects only show their problems live (see claudetools-live-game memory: mailbox commands, `reload <Mod>`). Never lose Bob's gear; check `siege status` and tributes before time jumps.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Run the README playtest checklist items for this milestone in Bob's Creative world via ClaudeTools.\n- Fix what breaks (file bugs as bones if not fixed now).\n- Update README checklist, CHANGELOG, DESCRIPTION; bump version; `mise run publish`; update dist/manifest.json.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Villagers play at the board\n- [ ] Works with Jarldom NOT installed\n- [ ] F6 reload mid-test leaves no duplicates/errors\n- [ ] Released as Tafl 0.4.0 in dist/manifest.json\n\n# Dependencies\nJarldom: villagers play real tafl in the hall evenings (pieces move),\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nShips a usable slice of Tafl so players get value before the whole goal is done.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.9; parent goal bn-350.\n","kind":"task","labels":["tafl","t4","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-350","size":"s","title":"Tafl T4: live test in Creative + release Tafl 0.4.0","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:-Dz0jnrIb6e0lgJzxAxohlKuDZ8tjh6JgupFOZP28Ks
1791857919296532	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2rrg	{"description":"# Context & Background\nFirst task of the Runecarver standalone mod (spec section 3.10, goal bn-21n). Nothing exists yet. Repo pattern: small mods like mods/Spyglass and mods/Delivery (csproj net48 via mods/Directory.Build.props, Plugin.cs, pure logic files, CHANGELOG.txt, DESCRIPTION.txt, cover.jpg), tests in tests/<Mod>.Tests (Program.cs check-style runner), mise tasks build/test/verify/publish/install, dist/manifest.json catalog for the F7 mod manager.\n\n# Goals\nAn empty-but-loadable Runecarver plugin that every later Runecarver task drops code into, with the ground rules wired in from day one.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nDoing the scaffold once up front means each feature task stays s/m and the ground rules (prefix names, server-authoritative settings, F6 reload, pure Core logic, tool command, golden prefab list) are not forgotten per feature. Runecarver's transliteration is pure logic; rendering is the hard part.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- mods/Runecarver/Runecarver.csproj, Plugin.cs (BepInEx plugin com.bobisme.runecarver, server-synced ConfigEntries, clean OnDestroy for F6 reload).\n- mods/Runecarver/Core/ for pure C# (no Unity) linked into tests/Runecarver.Tests.\n- A ClaudeTools command root `runecarver` (status/help first) following Jarldom's Tools/Tools.cs pattern.\n- README with a playtest checklist section, DESCRIPTION.txt, CHANGELOG.txt, cover.jpg placeholder, dist/manifest.json entry.\n- tests/Runecarver.Tests/prefabs.txt golden list (empty to start) + the superset test from foundation bone bn-2vn.\n- Read ~/repos/valheim-claude-tools/docs/modding-pitfalls.md before writing items.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `mise run build` and `mise run test` pass with Runecarver included\n- [ ] Plugin loads and F6-reloads cleanly in game with no errors\n- [ ] `runecarver status` tool command answers\n- [ ] Golden prefab list test exists\n- [ ] No dependency on Jarldom or any other Bob mod\n\n# Dependencies\nbn-2vn\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFoundation for the whole Runecarver goal; keeps it useful on its own per the standalone ground rule.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.10; parent goal bn-21n.\n","kind":"task","labels":["runecarver","c1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-21n","size":"s","title":"Runecarver: scaffold mods/Runecarver project (csproj, Plugin, Core/, tests/Runecarver.Tests, README checklist, manifest entry, tool command, prefab golden list)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:wHQyZn6903lXFB_giwWKaKjQC5hIjLlnzHPo6cUEBBY
1791857919317690	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1equ	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.10: transliterated to Younger Futhark (long-branch) with a documented English -> Old Norse sound mapping; no translation.\n\n# Goals\nA deterministic transliterator: English text -> phoneme-ish sounds -> 16 long-branch runes, with word separators.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nYounger Futhark has 16 runes covering many sounds (e.g. u for u/o/w/v, i for i/e/j, k for k/g, t for t/d, p/b as bjarkan); a rule table + digraphs (th, sh, ch, ng) documented in the README so results are explainable. No translation keeps scope small and honest.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Core/Futhark.cs: normalise, digraph rules, mapping table, double-letter collapse (runic convention), separators.\n- Docs: README section with the mapping table and examples.\n- Tests: dozens of words/names (Bob, Quad, Sigrid, Thor...).\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Mapping documented\n- [ ] Tests cover every rune and digraph\n- [ ] Unicode runic output (U+16A0 block) for hover/debug\n\n# Dependencies\nRunecarver: scaffold mods/Runecarver project (csproj, Plugin, Core/, tes\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nCore of every runic render, incl. Jarldom memorials.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.10; parent goal bn-21n.\n","kind":"task","labels":["runecarver","c1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-21n","size":"m","title":"Runecarver C1: English -> Old Norse sound mapping document + Younger Futhark long-branch transliteration (pure, fully tested)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:mrhJy7DUDyj_pBv6wl-VQ7V-5n56TaUXWLd3Y44QSU4
1791857919339053	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-b8tv	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.10: carve runestones with your own text; hover shows the English. Jarldom 0.1.18 carves runes offline via Blender (mods/Jarldom/Models/carve/carve.py); player text needs a RUNTIME approach.\n\n# Goals\nA runestone piece with a text prompt; the runes appear on its face.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nRuntime options: (1) a generated texture (draw rune glyph strokes into a RenderTexture/Texture2D used as a decal/detail map), (2) generated mesh strokes. Texture is cheaper and robust; pick it unless it looks bad. Text stored on the piece ZDO (small string).\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Runecarver_Stone piece (vanilla runestone mesh or a Blender-made stone).\n- Glyph stroke data for 16 runes (vector polylines) in Core.\n- Render: rasterise strokes into a texture applied to a carved-face material.\n- Text input via vanilla TextInput (like signs).\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Text entered appears as runes on the stone in multiplayer\n- [ ] Hover shows the English\n- [ ] Reload keeps the carving\n\n# Dependencies\nRunecarver C1: English -> Old Norse sound mapping document + Younger Futhar\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nPlayer-made memorials in the world.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.10; parent goal bn-21n.\n","kind":"task","labels":["runecarver","c1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-21n","size":"m","title":"Runecarver C1: one carvable runestone piece - enter text, runes rendered on the stone, hover shows English","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:FvOE1cTEozDTGYJPJ734j5rmveJbRiXf8Bn_5aOLH90
1791857919361269	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3nw6	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone C1 of Runecarver (spec section 3.10). Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, dist + manifest, for this mod only.\n\n# Goals\nProve C1 works in a real game and ship it.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nUnit tests cover pure logic but taming, AI, physics and status effects only show their problems live (see claudetools-live-game memory: mailbox commands, `reload <Mod>`). Never lose Bob's gear; check `siege status` and tributes before time jumps.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Run the README playtest checklist items for this milestone in Bob's Creative world via ClaudeTools.\n- Fix what breaks (file bugs as bones if not fixed now).\n- Update README checklist, CHANGELOG, DESCRIPTION; bump version; `mise run publish`; update dist/manifest.json.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Carve a stone with your name\n- [ ] Works with Jarldom NOT installed\n- [ ] F6 reload mid-test leaves no duplicates/errors\n- [ ] Released as Runecarver 0.1.0 in dist/manifest.json\n\n# Dependencies\nRunecarver C1: one carvable runestone piece - enter text, runes rendered on\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nShips a usable slice of Runecarver so players get value before the whole goal is done.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.10; parent goal bn-21n.\n","kind":"task","labels":["runecarver","c1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-21n","size":"s","title":"Runecarver C1: live test in Creative + release Runecarver 0.1.0","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:ifnfXuwoN0pXgq2rOEmRX_FjLrfnTt3lqgKx4Nn0M20
1791857919384060	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-q8tj	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.10: carved in a band along a serpent outline.\n\n# Goals\nRunes laid along a curved band with a serpent head and tail, the classic runestone look.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nLayout as pure math: band polyline/spline, sample positions and rotations per rune, fit text length (scale/spacing) - testable.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Core/Band.cs: spline templates per stone shape; glyph placement.\n- Renderer draws band outline + runes into the texture.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Long and short texts fit the band\n- [ ] Head/tail drawn\n- [ ] Layout tests\n\n# Dependencies\nRunecarver C1: live test in Creative + release Runecarver 0.1.0\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nThe iconic runestone look.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.10; parent goal bn-21n.\n","kind":"task","labels":["runecarver","c2","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-21n","size":"m","title":"Runecarver C2: serpent band layout - runes follow a serpent outline (Urnes-style band) with head and tail","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:SdY6F7ZIe1gTwkiSuut3Yr5-w-tMIJIZSRgTqXwuIqE
1791857919404988	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-tda6	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.10: choose the stone shape and paint colours.\n\n# Goals\nA few stone shapes and a paint choice.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nHistoric runestones were painted (red ochre etc.); Bob dislikes pink effects - keep colours earthy.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- 3-4 stone shapes (piece variants), paint colour stored on ZDO.\n- Paint applied to the band/rune texture.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each shape works with the band layout\n- [ ] Colour choice persists\n\n# Dependencies\nRunecarver C2: serpent band layout - runes follow a serpent outline (Urnes-\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nPersonalisation.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.10; parent goal bn-21n.\n","kind":"task","labels":["runecarver","c2","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-21n","size":"s","title":"Runecarver C2: stone shapes and paint colours (red ochre, black, white...)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:FVnIZWIVUCOmkcehMqNjgCumsajKcIVdiRjv1xNwFGI
1791857919426213	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1w7w	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.10: also carve shields, door lintels and memorial stones.\n\n# Goals\nRunic text on shields (item custom data), lintel pieces and memorial stone pieces.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nShields are items: store text in ItemData.m_customData; render via the same texture approach on the shield face.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Lintel and memorial pieces; shield carving at a station.\n- Hover shows English everywhere.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Carved shield keeps text in inventory/drops\n- [ ] Lintel and memorial pieces carve\n\n# Dependencies\nRunecarver C2: serpent band layout - runes follow a serpent outline (Urnes-\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nBroad use.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.10; parent goal bn-21n.\n","kind":"task","labels":["runecarver","c2","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-21n","size":"m","title":"Runecarver C2: carve shields, door lintels and memorial stones too","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:XxHWoi43tkVgziF6H8Sl-idctCUurxp5z5pAQz8bSZg
1791857919447127	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2igx	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone C2 of Runecarver (spec section 3.10). Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, dist + manifest, for this mod only.\n\n# Goals\nProve C2 works in a real game and ship it.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nUnit tests cover pure logic but taming, AI, physics and status effects only show their problems live (see claudetools-live-game memory: mailbox commands, `reload <Mod>`). Never lose Bob's gear; check `siege status` and tributes before time jumps.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Run the README playtest checklist items for this milestone in Bob's Creative world via ClaudeTools.\n- Fix what breaks (file bugs as bones if not fixed now).\n- Update README checklist, CHANGELOG, DESCRIPTION; bump version; `mise run publish`; update dist/manifest.json.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Serpent band stones in each shape and paint\n- [ ] Works with Jarldom NOT installed\n- [ ] F6 reload mid-test leaves no duplicates/errors\n- [ ] Released as Runecarver 0.2.0 in dist/manifest.json\n\n# Dependencies\nRunecarver C2: stone shapes and paint colours (red ochre, black, white...), Runecarver C2: carve shields, door lintels and memorial stones too\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nShips a usable slice of Runecarver so players get value before the whole goal is done.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.10; parent goal bn-21n.\n","kind":"task","labels":["runecarver","c2","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-21n","size":"s","title":"Runecarver C2: live test in Creative + release Runecarver 0.2.0","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:Q0xxJchZTJkdNcHQWkFwP8f5lcnbKRsQif79ecZdlBU
1791857919469641	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-38n2	{"description":"# Context & Background\nGround rule: tiny static Api; Jarldom's memorial wall (#25), milestones (#48), gravestones and chronicle stones render in runes.\n\n# Goals\nApi to transliterate and to render runes onto a given renderer/piece.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nPrimitive types + GameObject only.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- mods/Runecarver/Api.cs per bn-1xw.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Api renders runes on an arbitrary target\n\n# Dependencies\nRunecarver C2: live test in Creative + release Runecarver 0.2.0, bn-1xw\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nEnables Jarldom side.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.10; parent goal bn-21n.\n","kind":"task","labels":["runecarver","c3","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-21n","size":"s","title":"Runecarver C3: publish Runecarver.Api (Version, Transliterate(text), Carve(piece/gameobject, text, style))","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:PAwlb0diSXmahkTxrDXZOLa-cuKYfNHMzbeqOkauL54
1791857919489738	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3lma	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.10 Jarldom side; J3 #25 memorial wall and J6 #48 milestones (other forks' bones) render in runes with an English hover when Runecarver is installed.\n\n# Goals\nJarldom villagers use the standalone mod's features when it is installed, and nothing changes (no errors) when it is not.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nGround rule: no hard dependency in either direction; Jarldom resolves `<Mod>.Api` by reflection through the ApiRef helper (bn-1xw) and degrades to vanilla behaviour. Villager behaviour stays in Jarldom (spin-out rule).\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Each Jarldom text piece calls Runecarver.Api.Carve when present, falls back to plain text.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Memorial wall shows runes with English hover\n- [ ] Gravestones carve the name\n- [ ] Without the mod installed Jarldom behaves exactly as before (no errors)\n- [ ] Jarldom released (version, changelog, dist); raise Plugin.DataVersion if record/soul formats change\n\n# Dependencies\nRunecarver C3: publish Runecarver.Api (Version, Transliterate(text), Carve(, bn-1xw\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nRunic look for the colony's memory.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.10; parent goal bn-21n.\n","kind":"task","labels":["runecarver","c3","next-saga","standalone","jarldom","integration","j3","j6"],"parent":"bn-21n","size":"m","title":"Jarldom: memorial wall, milestones, gravestones and chronicle stones render in runes (English hover) with Runecarver","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:5BOGpPCiHFuxkc_6lbWZuZsNAJL3xrMRDDNPQT59Nqo
1791857919511663	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1e0d	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone C3 of Runecarver (spec section 3.10). Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, dist + manifest, for this mod only.\n\n# Goals\nProve C3 works in a real game and ship it.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nUnit tests cover pure logic but taming, AI, physics and status effects only show their problems live (see claudetools-live-game memory: mailbox commands, `reload <Mod>`). Never lose Bob's gear; check `siege status` and tributes before time jumps.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Run the README playtest checklist items for this milestone in Bob's Creative world via ClaudeTools.\n- Fix what breaks (file bugs as bones if not fixed now).\n- Update README checklist, CHANGELOG, DESCRIPTION; bump version; `mise run publish`; update dist/manifest.json.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Jarldom memorial in runes\n- [ ] Works with Jarldom NOT installed\n- [ ] F6 reload mid-test leaves no duplicates/errors\n- [ ] Released as Runecarver 0.3.0 in dist/manifest.json\n\n# Dependencies\nJarldom: memorial wall, milestones, gravestones and chronicle stones \n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nShips a usable slice of Runecarver so players get value before the whole goal is done.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.10; parent goal bn-21n.\n","kind":"task","labels":["runecarver","c3","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-21n","size":"s","title":"Runecarver C3: live test in Creative + release Runecarver 0.3.0","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:bgmCZyPMMjetoMe47E55BpJ9vcfapmIw52-lnPhJJGY
1791857919532611	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-19o7	{"description":"# Context & Background\nFirst task of the Wounds standalone mod (spec section 3.11, goal bn-4nf). Nothing exists yet. Repo pattern: small mods like mods/Spyglass and mods/Delivery (csproj net48 via mods/Directory.Build.props, Plugin.cs, pure logic files, CHANGELOG.txt, DESCRIPTION.txt, cover.jpg), tests in tests/<Mod>.Tests (Program.cs check-style runner), mise tasks build/test/verify/publish/install, dist/manifest.json catalog for the F7 mod manager.\n\n# Goals\nAn empty-but-loadable Wounds plugin that every later Wounds task drops code into, with the ground rules wired in from day one.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nDoing the scaffold once up front means each feature task stays s/m and the ground rules (prefix names, server-authoritative settings, F6 reload, pure Core logic, tool command, golden prefab list) are not forgotten per feature. Wounds: each wound type gets its own server toggle.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- mods/Wounds/Wounds.csproj, Plugin.cs (BepInEx plugin com.bobisme.wounds, server-synced ConfigEntries, clean OnDestroy for F6 reload).\n- mods/Wounds/Core/ for pure C# (no Unity) linked into tests/Wounds.Tests.\n- A ClaudeTools command root `wounds` (status/help first) following Jarldom's Tools/Tools.cs pattern.\n- README with a playtest checklist section, DESCRIPTION.txt, CHANGELOG.txt, cover.jpg placeholder, dist/manifest.json entry.\n- tests/Wounds.Tests/prefabs.txt golden list (empty to start) + the superset test from foundation bone bn-2vn.\n- Read ~/repos/valheim-claude-tools/docs/modding-pitfalls.md before writing items.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `mise run build` and `mise run test` pass with Wounds included\n- [ ] Plugin loads and F6-reloads cleanly in game with no errors\n- [ ] `wounds status` tool command answers\n- [ ] Golden prefab list test exists\n- [ ] No dependency on Jarldom or any other Bob mod\n\n# Dependencies\nbn-2vn\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFoundation for the whole Wounds goal; keeps it useful on its own per the standalone ground rule.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.11; parent goal bn-4nf.\n","kind":"task","labels":["wounds","w1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-4nf","size":"s","title":"Wounds: scaffold mods/Wounds project (csproj, Plugin, Core/, tests/Wounds.Tests, README checklist, manifest entry, tool command, prefab golden list)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:HAgYDxEJeV-aOdYVGe10xA5txvQiY0vCytM4fzm_V28
1791857919554345	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1c56	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.11: toggle per wound type: bleeding, broken bones, infection.\n\n# Goals\nA single tested model for all wound types so W2/W3 only add rules.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nOne state machine keeps interactions (infection from untreated wounds) consistent and testable.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Core/Wounds.cs: Wound{type, severity, treated, age}; Apply(hit), Tick(dt, env), Treat(item).\n- Tests per transition.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Tests cover cause, tick and treatment for bleeding (W2/W3 extend)\n\n# Dependencies\nWounds: scaffold mods/Wounds project (csproj, Plugin, Core/, tests/W\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nShared base for every wound.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.11; parent goal bn-4nf.\n","kind":"task","labels":["wounds","w1","next-saga","standalone","toggle"],"parent":"bn-4nf","size":"m","title":"Wounds W1: wound state machine (pure) - wound types, causes, severity, treatment, healing, toggles","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:7KsfqfA2TyLURSalzFwbeXYb57kSpUsTF5-VCAAP68c
1791857919574267	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3ejd	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.11: bleeding (from slashes; stops with a bandage).\n\n# Goals\nSlash damage over a threshold can cause bleeding (SE_Bleeding) that drains HP until bandaged or it clots slowly.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nTie to HitData.m_damage.m_slash so it's predictable; server toggle Wounds.Bleeding.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Patch Character.Damage on the player; SE icon and tooltip.\n- Wounds_Bandage item (linen/leather scraps) consumable cures bleeding.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Big slash hit can start bleeding\n- [ ] Bandage stops it\n- [ ] Toggle off = never happens\n\n# Dependencies\nWounds W1: wound state machine (pure) - wound types, causes, severity, \n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFirst wound.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.11; parent goal bn-4nf.\n","kind":"task","labels":["wounds","w1","next-saga","standalone","toggle"],"parent":"bn-4nf","size":"m","title":"Wounds W1: bleeding from slashing hits (toggle) - HP drain status effect, stops with a bandage","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:siRgW0zhNBIGkTLbVishNVWlH3ct2PNbPrUP15rAJiI
1791857919596325	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-384n	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone W1 of Wounds (spec section 3.11). Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, dist + manifest, for this mod only.\n\n# Goals\nProve W1 works in a real game and ship it.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nUnit tests cover pure logic but taming, AI, physics and status effects only show their problems live (see claudetools-live-game memory: mailbox commands, `reload <Mod>`). Never lose Bob's gear; check `siege status` and tributes before time jumps.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Run the README playtest checklist items for this milestone in Bob's Creative world via ClaudeTools.\n- Fix what breaks (file bugs as bones if not fixed now).\n- Update README checklist, CHANGELOG, DESCRIPTION; bump version; `mise run publish`; update dist/manifest.json.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Bleed from a slash and bandage it\n- [ ] Works with Jarldom NOT installed\n- [ ] F6 reload mid-test leaves no duplicates/errors\n- [ ] Released as Wounds 0.1.0 in dist/manifest.json\n\n# Dependencies\nWounds W1: bleeding from slashing hits (toggle) - HP drain status effec\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nShips a usable slice of Wounds so players get value before the whole goal is done.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.11; parent goal bn-4nf.\n","kind":"task","labels":["wounds","w1","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-4nf","size":"s","title":"Wounds W1: live test in Creative + release Wounds 0.1.0","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:W31IlNHAwC7ASn6Z-woYXu0GKvjX7LUqh6eDz3XIP98
1791857919615979	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-7p97	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.11: broken bones (from big falls or troll hits; slower movement until splinted, then heals over time).\n\n# Goals\nFall damage over a threshold or blunt hits from big foes break a bone: movement slowed; a splint item lets it heal over time.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nThresholds tunable; toggle Wounds.Bones.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Patch fall damage and blunt hits (Troll and similar).\n- Wounds_Splint item; healing timer.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] High fall breaks a bone (slow)\n- [ ] Splint then heal over the set time\n- [ ] Toggle off works\n\n# Dependencies\nWounds W1: live test in Creative + release Wounds 0.1.0\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nWeight to big hits.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.11; parent goal bn-4nf.\n","kind":"task","labels":["wounds","w2","next-saga","standalone","toggle"],"parent":"bn-4nf","size":"m","title":"Wounds W2: broken bones from big falls or troll hits (toggle) - slower movement until splinted, then heal over time","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:Lq-zKkGAsD_qRsmcddopmTly6QOkjthGptxdx0Kab6E
1791857919635413	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3f3t	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone W2 of Wounds (spec section 3.11). Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, dist + manifest, for this mod only.\n\n# Goals\nProve W2 works in a real game and ship it.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nUnit tests cover pure logic but taming, AI, physics and status effects only show their problems live (see claudetools-live-game memory: mailbox commands, `reload <Mod>`). Never lose Bob's gear; check `siege status` and tributes before time jumps.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Run the README playtest checklist items for this milestone in Bob's Creative world via ClaudeTools.\n- Fix what breaks (file bugs as bones if not fixed now).\n- Update README checklist, CHANGELOG, DESCRIPTION; bump version; `mise run publish`; update dist/manifest.json.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Break a bone and splint it\n- [ ] Works with Jarldom NOT installed\n- [ ] F6 reload mid-test leaves no duplicates/errors\n- [ ] Released as Wounds 0.2.0 in dist/manifest.json\n\n# Dependencies\nWounds W2: broken bones from big falls or troll hits (toggle) - slower \n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nShips a usable slice of Wounds so players get value before the whole goal is done.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.11; parent goal bn-4nf.\n","kind":"task","labels":["wounds","w2","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-4nf","size":"s","title":"Wounds W2: live test in Creative + release Wounds 0.2.0","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:y-qtVUsVNANHEJP6r5ujfhIjvG2rdIUE4DXjRQVLR1M
1791857919657200	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2aq7	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.11: infection (untreated wounds in the swamp; a fever debuff; cured with herbs).\n\n# Goals\nOpen wounds while in the Swamp risk infection: fever lowers stamina/regen until treated with a poultice.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nBiome-based risk is readable for players.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Rule in Core/Wounds.cs; SE_Fever; toggle Wounds.Infection.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Untreated wound in Swamp can infect\n- [ ] Poultice cures fever\n\n# Dependencies\nWounds W2: live test in Creative + release Wounds 0.2.0\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nSwamp danger.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.11; parent goal bn-4nf.\n","kind":"task","labels":["wounds","w3","next-saga","standalone","toggle"],"parent":"bn-4nf","size":"m","title":"Wounds W3: infection - untreated wounds in the Swamp become infected (fever debuff), cured with herbs (toggle)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:N4Ip9o0ul4_wq_mujGIHVyXqnsUZsY6Un8FXsiXKSI8
1791857919676229	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-fqi9	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.11: an herb garden (yarrow, angelica, plantain) and a mortar to make poultices and bandages. Angelica is also a Fields crop - share one prefab if Fields is installed? No: keep Wounds_Angelica separate unless both mods agree (document).\n\n# Goals\nPlantable herbs and a mortar station.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nPlant/Pickable clones; mortar as a crafting station.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Wounds_Yarrow/Angelica/Plantain seeds + plants; Wounds_Mortar station; Wounds_Poultice recipe.\n- Wild herb pickables in Meadows/Black Forest.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Grow herbs and grind a poultice\n\n# Dependencies\nWounds W2: live test in Creative + release Wounds 0.2.0\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nTreatment economy.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.11; parent goal bn-4nf.\n","kind":"task","labels":["wounds","w3","next-saga","standalone","fields"],"parent":"bn-4nf","size":"m","title":"Wounds W3: herb garden (yarrow, angelica, plantain) + mortar for poultices and bandages","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:XabaPvhPPKj52O0qSoTiLMZGvn-nJcdow_U3b52xdfA
1791857919696127	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2vgm	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone W3 of Wounds (spec section 3.11). Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, dist + manifest, for this mod only.\n\n# Goals\nProve W3 works in a real game and ship it.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nUnit tests cover pure logic but taming, AI, physics and status effects only show their problems live (see claudetools-live-game memory: mailbox commands, `reload <Mod>`). Never lose Bob's gear; check `siege status` and tributes before time jumps.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Run the README playtest checklist items for this milestone in Bob's Creative world via ClaudeTools.\n- Fix what breaks (file bugs as bones if not fixed now).\n- Update README checklist, CHANGELOG, DESCRIPTION; bump version; `mise run publish`; update dist/manifest.json.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Infection in the Swamp cured by a poultice\n- [ ] Works with Jarldom NOT installed\n- [ ] F6 reload mid-test leaves no duplicates/errors\n- [ ] Released as Wounds 0.3.0 in dist/manifest.json\n\n# Dependencies\nWounds W3: infection - untreated wounds in the Swamp become infected (f, Wounds W3: herb garden (yarrow, angelica, plantain) + mortar for poulti\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nShips a usable slice of Wounds so players get value before the whole goal is done.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.11; parent goal bn-4nf.\n","kind":"task","labels":["wounds","w3","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-4nf","size":"s","title":"Wounds W3: live test in Creative + release Wounds 0.3.0","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:IN4VzuXLXMnXlF-NBdGn8lwIlkdeWJHy5aPiELsBv38
1791857919716600	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-7zs4	{"description":"# Context & Background\nGround rule: tiny static Api. Jarldom villagers are Player-prefab clones, so wounds can apply to them.\n\n# Goals\nApi for Jarldom healers.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nPrimitive types.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- mods/Wounds/Api.cs per bn-1xw.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Api lists and treats wounds on a villager body\n\n# Dependencies\nWounds W3: live test in Creative + release Wounds 0.3.0, bn-1xw\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nEnables Jarldom side.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.11; parent goal bn-4nf.\n","kind":"task","labels":["wounds","w4","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-4nf","size":"s","title":"Wounds W4: publish Wounds.Api (Version, WoundsOf(Character), Treat(Character, item), Apply to non-players)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:T9rGMkIdLCIarLneu4j60GOvigchug5eQZ7I0Pj-aVc
1791857919738173	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2hqe	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec 3.11 Jarldom side: the healer and the healer's house have real work; injured villagers need treatment; expeditions want a medic. Healer HealTask exists (Villager/Tasks.cs).\n\n# Goals\nJarldom villagers use the standalone mod's features when it is installed, and nothing changes (no errors) when it is not.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nGround rule: no hard dependency in either direction; Jarldom resolves `<Mod>.Api` by reflection through the ApiRef helper (bn-1xw) and degrades to vanilla behaviour. Villager behaviour stays in Jarldom (spin-out rule).\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- HealTask treats villager wounds via Wounds.Api using poultices/bandages from stores.\n- Needs-you hint when the healer lacks supplies.\n- Expedition role 'medic' (J6 #53) treats crew.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Wounded villager is treated by the healer\n- [ ] Untreated villager shows the wound in their panel\n- [ ] Without the mod installed Jarldom behaves exactly as before (no errors)\n- [ ] Jarldom released (version, changelog, dist); raise Plugin.DataVersion if record/soul formats change\n\n# Dependencies\nWounds W4: publish Wounds.Api (Version, WoundsOf(Character), Treat(Char, bn-1xw\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nPurpose for the healer profession.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.11; parent goal bn-4nf.\n","kind":"task","labels":["wounds","w4","next-saga","standalone","jarldom","integration","j6"],"parent":"bn-4nf","size":"m","title":"Jarldom: injured villagers need treatment at the healer's house; expeditions want a medic","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:f8JCr2-uTlxzV0oiVh7sBzZ1CRZPFtF8F1siT9YqTP8
1791857919758863	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-b8xy	{"description":"# Context & Background\nCloses milestone W4 of Wounds (spec section 3.11). Release-every-change rule: bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, dist + manifest, for this mod only.\n\n# Goals\nProve W4 works in a real game and ship it.\n\n# Reasoning/Justification\nUnit tests cover pure logic but taming, AI, physics and status effects only show their problems live (see claudetools-live-game memory: mailbox commands, `reload <Mod>`). Never lose Bob's gear; check `siege status` and tributes before time jumps.\n\n# Implementation Approach\n- Run the README playtest checklist items for this milestone in Bob's Creative world via ClaudeTools.\n- Fix what breaks (file bugs as bones if not fixed now).\n- Update README checklist, CHANGELOG, DESCRIPTION; bump version; `mise run publish`; update dist/manifest.json.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Healer treats a villager\n- [ ] Works with Jarldom NOT installed\n- [ ] F6 reload mid-test leaves no duplicates/errors\n- [ ] Released as Wounds 0.4.0 in dist/manifest.json\n\n# Dependencies\nJarldom: injured villagers need treatment at the healer's house; expe\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nShips a usable slice of Wounds so players get value before the whole goal is done.\n\nSpec: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md section 3.11; parent goal bn-4nf.\n","kind":"task","labels":["wounds","w4","next-saga","standalone"],"parent":"bn-4nf","size":"s","title":"Wounds W4: live test in Creative + release Wounds 0.4.0","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:-aXeGnvzQzGLKQXchVpbG5lX4DSmWwBwhmN172f28Kg
